/* Lecture 5 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":5,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-1/lecture05/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"What's New, a Transformer Recap and Why Scale Matters","blurb":"From the latest video models and OpenClaw back to the Transformer, then a first look at scaling laws and emergent abilities, and today's roadmap.","file":"lecture05_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part1.jpg","duration":779.9,"first":1,"last":13,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 5","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"What happened after last lecture","t":68.09},{"n":3,"title":"It become crazy after Spring Festival","t":150.06},{"n":4,"title":"Video Generation","t":206.32},{"n":5,"title":"OpenClaw","t":262.17},{"n":6,"title":"How OpenClaw is popular!","t":324.81},{"n":7,"title":"To recap and an overview","t":380.61},{"n":8,"title":"Inductive bias of composition","t":405.51},{"n":9,"title":"A video you must watch","t":466.89},{"n":10,"title":"Multi-head self-attention","t":526.62},{"n":11,"title":"Benefits to be large： Scaling Law Performance depends strongly on scale! We keep getting better performance as we scale","t":594.58},{"n":12,"title":"Benefits to be large： Emergent abilities Some ability of LM is not present in smaller models but is present in larger mo","t":654.87},{"n":13,"title":"Outline","t":721.04}],"sents":[[0.8,3.06,1,"Good morning, everyone, and welcome back.","大家早上好，欢迎回来。"],[3.41,15.67,1,"Last time, in Lecture 4, we took the Transformer apart: self-attention, multi-head attention, positional information, the feed-forward blocks, and some variants beyond the original design.","上一次，在第四讲里，我们把 Transformer 拆开来看：自注意力、多头注意力、位置信息、前馈模块，以及一些超越原始设计的变体。"],[16.02,17.46,1,"You now know the engine.","现在你们已经了解这台发动机了。"],[17.81,20.81,1,"Today we put that engine into the car.","今天，我们要把这台发动机装进汽车里。"],[21.16,24.16,1,"Lecture 5 is about large language models.","第五讲的主题是大语言模型。"],[24.51,35.12,1,"In the first half, we ask what an LLM actually is, how large large really is, why scale matters so much, and what we can learn from the story of ChatGPT.","前半部分，我们会问：LLM 到底是什么，“大”究竟有多大，为什么规模如此重要，以及我们能从 ChatGPT 的故事中学到什么。"],[35.47,41.69,1,"We'll also talk about the different ways you can use an LLM, from prompting and agents to training your own.","我们还会讨论使用 LLM 的不同方式，从提示词和智能体，到训练你自己的模型。"],[42.04,53.1,1,"In the second half, we open the black box and walk through how an LLM is built from scratch: tokenization, pretraining, supervised fine-tuning, and RLHF.","后半部分，我们会打开黑盒子，一步步看 LLM 是如何从零构建的：分词、预训练、监督微调和 RLHF。"],[53.45,54.79,1,"Why does this matter?","这为什么重要？"],[55.14,65.02,1,"Almost everything we do in the rest of the course, from reasoning and RL to agents, medical models and multimodal models, sits on top of what we cover today.","本课程后面几乎所有内容，从推理和强化学习，到智能体、医疗模型和多模态模型，都建立在今天所讲的内容之上。"],[65.37,66.69,1,"So let's get going.","那我们开始吧。"],[67.94,73.96,2,"Before the technical part, a quick reality check on how fast this field moves.","在进入技术内容之前，先快速感受一下这个领域发展得有多快。"],[74.31,83.12,2,"This is a snapshot from a few weeks earlier this year, around the Spring Festival, and look at how much happened in such a short window.","这是今年早些时候、春节前后几周的一个快照，看看在这么短的时间里发生了多少事情。"],[83.47,87.77,2,"On the model side, almost every major Chinese lab shipped something.","在模型方面，几乎每家主要的中国实验室都发布了新东西。"],[88.12,101.93,2,"Qwen 3.5-Plus from Alibaba, MiniMax M2.5, and Kimi K2.5 from Moonshot, plus GLM-5 from Zhipu.","阿里的 Qwen 3.5-Plus、MiniMax M2.5、月之暗面的 Kimi K2.5，还有智谱的 GLM-5。"],[102.28,105.44,2,"And Seedance 2.0 from ByteDance, for video.","还有字节跳动的视频模型 Seedance 2.0。"],[105.79,113.02,2,"On the product side, assistants like Tencent Yuanbao and Ant's AFu were pushed hard to ordinary users.","在产品方面，腾讯元宝、蚂蚁阿福这样的助手被大力推向普通用户。"],[113.37,123.08,2,"And the picture on the right shows humanoid robots dancing at the Spring Festival Gala, which tells you that embodied AI has gone mainstream too.","右边这张图是春晚上跳舞的人形机器人，说明具身智能也已经走进了大众视野。"],[123.43,133.82,2,"On the same day I first made this slide, OpenAI released GPT-5.4 Thinking and GPT-5.4 Pro.","就在我第一次做这页幻灯片的那天，OpenAI 发布了 GPT-5.4 Thinking 和 GPT-5.4 Pro。"],[134.17,139.86,2,"The one thing to take away: the half-life of state of the art is now measured in weeks.","最需要记住的一点是：“最先进”的半衰期现在是以周来计算的。"],[140.21,143.77,2,"That's exactly why we focus on principles in this course.","这正是我们这门课注重原理的原因。"],[144.12,148.66,2,"The specific model names will change, but the ideas behind them won't.","具体的模型名字会变，但背后的思想不会变。"],[149.91,152.96,3,"And it's not just researchers who noticed.","注意到这一点的不只是研究者。"],[153.31,159.84,3,"These are two market snapshots from early March, one for MiniMax and one for Zhipu, which trades as Knowledge Atlas.","这是三月初的两张行情截图，一张是 MiniMax，一张是智谱，它的上市名称是 Knowledge Atlas。"],[160.19,162.87,3,"Both had listed in Hong Kong not long before.","两家公司都是不久前才在香港上市的。"],[163.22,172.13,3,"Look at the one-month change: MiniMax is up about seventy-eight percent, and Zhipu is up about one hundred sixty-seven percent in a single month.","看看一个月的涨幅：MiniMax 上涨了约 78%，智谱更是在一个月内上涨了约 167%。"],[172.48,178.12,3,"Each has a market value of roughly two hundred forty to two hundred sixty billion Hong Kong dollars.","两家的市值都在大约两千四百亿到两千六百亿港元之间。"],[178.47,181.17,3,"You don't need to care about stocks to read the message here.","你不需要关心股票，也能读懂这里传递的信息。"],[181.52,189.52,3,"Investors were betting that LLM companies, including Chinese ones, are building something with real economic value.","投资者押注的是：大模型公司，包括中国的公司，正在创造真正有经济价值的东西。"],[189.87,192.72,3,"I'm not giving you investment advice, of course.","当然，我不是在给大家投资建议。"],[193.07,199.61,3,"The point is simply that the technology we're studying today has moved from the lab into the center of the economy.","重点只是：我们今天学习的技术，已经从实验室走到了经济的中心。"],[199.96,204.92,3,"And that's part of why understanding how these models work is such a valuable skill.","这也是为什么理解这些模型的工作原理是一项如此有价值的技能。"],[206.17,211.98,4,"One of the things that caused the excitement was Seedance 2.0 from ByteDance.","引发这股热潮的原因之一，是字节跳动的 Seedance 2.0。"],[212.33,220.8,4,"These are frames from generated videos: a close-up of chess pieces, and a cinematic shot of a young man in a cockpit.","这些是生成视频中的画面：一个是国际象棋棋子的特写，另一个是驾驶舱里一位年轻人的电影级镜头。"],[221.15,223.36,4,"What I want you to notice is the quality.","我想让大家注意的是画质。"],[223.71,229.7,4,"The lighting, the depth of field, and the facial detail all look like they came out of a real film shoot.","光线、景深和面部细节，看起来都像是真实电影拍摄出来的。"],[230.05,236.76,4,"A couple of years ago, generated video was blurry, and objects melted into each other after a few seconds.","几年前，生成的视频还很模糊，几秒钟之后物体就会相互融化在一起。"],[237.11,242.07,4,"Now we're talking about clips that people genuinely can't tell apart from real footage.","而现在，人们已经真的分辨不出这些片段和真实拍摄的区别了。"],[242.42,247.12,4,"We'll come back to multimodal and video generation properly in Lecture 10.","我们会在第十讲系统地讨论多模态和视频生成。"],[247.47,257.51,4,"For today, just keep in mind that the same recipe of scaling data, models and compute that we'll discuss for text also drives these video models.","今天只需要记住：我们将要为文本讨论的那套配方，也就是扩展数据、模型和算力，同样驱动着这些视频模型。"],[257.86,260.77,4,"Check out the links if you want to see the actual clips.","如果想看实际的视频片段，可以去看下面的链接。"],[262.02,264.82,5,"The other big story was OpenClaw.","另一个大新闻是 OpenClaw。"],[265.17,271.55,5,"Its tagline is: the AI that actually does things, and that's the key difference from a chatbot.","它的口号是：“真正能做事的 AI”，这正是它和聊天机器人的关键区别。"],[271.9,273.78,5,"Look at the six boxes on the right.","看右边这六个方框。"],[274.13,278.13,5,"It runs on your own machine, with whichever model you choose.","它运行在你自己的电脑上，可以使用你选择的任何模型。"],[278.48,284.18,5,"You talk to it through the chat apps you already use, like WhatsApp or Telegram.","你可以通过已经在用的聊天软件和它对话，比如 WhatsApp 或 Telegram。"],[284.53,289.12,5,"It has persistent memory, so it learns your preferences over time.","它有持久记忆，所以会随着时间逐渐了解你的偏好。"],[289.47,296.76,5,"It can control a browser, it can read and write files and run shell commands, and you can extend it with skills and plugins.","它可以控制浏览器，可以读写文件、运行 shell 命令，你还可以用技能和插件来扩展它。"],[297.11,303.64,5,"So instead of just answering questions, it clears your inbox, books things, and fills in forms.","所以它不只是回答问题，而是帮你清理收件箱、预订东西、填写表单。"],[303.99,310.81,5,"That's what we call an agent: an LLM that doesn't just talk, but acts in an environment.","这就是我们所说的智能体：一个不只会说、还能在环境中行动的 LLM。"],[311.16,317.86,5,"Hold on to this example, because later today we'll talk about agents as one of the main ways of using LLMs.","记住这个例子，因为今天稍后我们会把智能体作为使用 LLM 的主要方式之一来讨论。"],[318.21,323.41,5,"And Lecture 7 is entirely about agents and the harness around them.","而第七讲将完全围绕智能体以及它们周围的“驾驭框架”展开。"],[324.66,328.94,6,"How popular did it get? Here are two fun pieces of evidence.","它到底有多火？这里有两个有趣的证据。"],[329.29,339.92,6,"On the left is a post from a Chinese social media app: someone in Shenzhen offering to come to your home and install OpenClaw, for four hundred ninety-nine yuan per visit.","左边是一条中国社交媒体上的帖子：深圳有人提供上门安装 OpenClaw 的服务，每次 499 元。"],[340.27,347.03,6,"When people start paying a technician to install your open-source project, you know it has broken out of the developer bubble.","当人们开始花钱请技术员来安装你的开源项目时，你就知道它已经冲出了开发者的圈子。"],[347.38,353.92,6,"On the right is a chart that circulated online, showing Mac Mini sales shooting up in December and January.","右边是一张在网上流传的图表，显示 Mac Mini 的销量在十二月和一月猛增。"],[354.27,360.93,6,"The story going around was that people were buying small always-on machines just to host their personal agent.","流传的说法是，人们购买这种小巧、可以一直开着的机器，就是为了运行自己的个人智能体。"],[361.28,368.47,6,"I'd treat the exact numbers with some caution, since it's an informal chart, but the trend is real enough to be interesting.","由于这是一张非正式的图表，具体数字要谨慎看待，但这个趋势足够真实，也很有意思。"],[368.82,372.65,6,"The lesson is that capability alone isn't enough.","这里的启示是：光有能力是不够的。"],[373.0,379.21,6,"A product becomes a phenomenon when it lets ordinary people do something useful with almost no friction.","当一个产品能让普通人几乎毫不费力地做成有用的事情时，它才会成为现象级产品。"],[380.46,382.04,7,"Okay, enough news.","好，新闻就说到这里。"],[382.39,387.37,7,"Let's step back and recap where we are, and then build up the big picture for today.","我们退一步，回顾一下目前的进度，然后搭建起今天的整体框架。"],[387.72,390.38,7,"The question for the next few slides is simple.","接下来几页要回答的问题很简单。"],[390.73,398.47,7,"Why did the Transformer, the architecture you studied last lecture, turn out to be the thing that made large language models possible?","为什么上一讲学的 Transformer 架构，最终成为了让大语言模型成为可能的关键？"],[398.82,404.11,7,"The answer has to do with inductive bias and with scale, so let's look at both.","答案和归纳偏置以及规模有关，我们来分别看看。"],[405.36,413.53,8,"Remember that every neural architecture builds in some assumptions about how to combine, or compose, the pieces of the input.","记住，每一种神经网络架构都内置了一些假设，规定了如何组合输入的各个部分。"],[413.88,416.48,8,"We call those assumptions inductive bias.","我们把这些假设称为归纳偏置。"],[416.83,420.08,8,"A CNN assumes that composition is local.","CNN 假设组合是局部的。"],[420.43,426.93,8,"It slides a small window over the input, like the filter on the left, and only combines things that are close to each other.","它在输入上滑动一个小窗口，就像左边的卷积核那样，只组合彼此相邻的东西。"],[427.28,431.22,8,"An RNN assumes composition is sequential.","RNN 假设组合是顺序进行的。"],[431.57,440.57,8,"It reads tokens one at a time, left to right or right to left, and squeezes everything so far into one hidden state, like the animation on the right.","它一次读一个词元，从左到右或从右到左，把目前读到的所有内容压缩进一个隐藏状态，就像右边的动画那样。"],[440.92,442.72,8,"These biases are not bad.","这些偏置并不是坏事。"],[443.07,447.64,8,"They help a lot when you have little data, because they tell the model what to look for.","在数据很少的时候，它们帮助很大，因为它们告诉模型该关注什么。"],[447.99,449.98,8,"But they're also restrictions.","但它们同时也是限制。"],[450.33,459.8,8,"A CNN struggles to connect two words that are far apart, and an RNN has to carry information across many steps, where it tends to fade.","CNN 很难把相距很远的两个词联系起来，而 RNN 需要把信息传递很多步，信息在这个过程中往往会逐渐衰减。"],[460.15,465.49,8,"Keep that trade-off in mind, because it's exactly the point of the next slide.","记住这个权衡，因为这正是下一页要讲的重点。"],[466.74,470.06,9,"This is a video I really want you to watch after class.","这是一个我非常希望大家课后去看的视频。"],[470.41,472.69,9,"The chart summarizes its main argument.","这张图概括了它的主要观点。"],[473.04,477.7,9,"On the x-axis is compute, and on the y-axis is performance.","横轴是算力，纵轴是性能。"],[478.05,482.41,9,"The blue curve is a method with more structure imposed by humans.","蓝色曲线代表人为施加了更多结构的方法。"],[482.76,487.99,9,"It starts off quickly, because the built-in assumptions help, but then it flattens out.","它起步很快，因为内置的假设起了作用，但之后就趋于平缓。"],[488.34,490.54,9,"The green curve has less structure.","绿色曲线代表结构更少的方法。"],[490.89,498.12,9,"It's worse at the beginning, but as you pour in more compute, it keeps going up and eventually overtakes the structured method.","它一开始更差，但随着投入更多算力，它会持续上升，最终超过结构化的方法。"],[498.47,500.7,9,"That's the story of the Transformer.","这就是 Transformer 的故事。"],[501.05,507.6,9,"Self-attention throws away the local and recurrent biases and lets every token look at every other token.","自注意力抛弃了局部偏置和循环偏置，让每个词元都能看到其他所有词元。"],[507.95,510.69,9,"With small data, that's not an advantage.","在数据量小的时候，这并不是优势。"],[511.04,518.2,9,"With huge data and compute, it's exactly what you want, because the model learns the structure itself instead of being told.","但在海量数据和算力下，这正是你想要的，因为模型会自己学习结构，而不是被告知结构。"],[518.55,525.22,9,"The one sentence to remember: the more structure we hard-code, the less scalable the method usually is.","要记住的一句话是：我们硬编码的结构越多，方法通常就越难扩展。"],[526.47,531.79,10,"Let me bring back the multi-head self-attention picture from last lecture, just to refresh your memory.","我把上一讲多头自注意力的图再拿出来，帮大家回忆一下。"],[532.14,542.98,10,"At the bottom, each word, Nobel, committee, awards, Strickland, who, advanced, optics, gets turned into a query, a key and a value.","在底部，每个词，Nobel、committee、awards、Strickland、who、advanced、optics，都会被转换成一个查询、一个键和一个值。"],[543.33,549.83,10,"The purple columns are attention weights: each word decides how much to look at every other word in the sentence.","紫色的列是注意力权重：每个词决定要在多大程度上关注句子中的其他每个词。"],[550.18,558.77,10,"For example, when the model processes the word who, it should attend strongly to Strickland, because that is the person the word who refers to.","例如，当模型处理 who 这个词时，它应该重点关注 Strickland，因为 who 指代的正是这个人。"],[559.12,565.77,10,"Multiple heads, M one to M H, let the model track several such relations at once.","多个注意力头，从 M1 到 MH，让模型可以同时追踪好几种这样的关系。"],[566.12,569.77,10,"Then a feed-forward layer processes each position.","然后由一个前馈层处理每一个位置。"],[570.12,573.21,10,"Stack this many times, and you get a Transformer.","把这样的结构堆叠很多次，就得到了 Transformer。"],[573.56,581.5,10,"The key property for today: every token can directly reach every other token, and all positions are computed in parallel.","今天要强调的关键性质是：每个词元都可以直接连到其他所有词元，并且所有位置都是并行计算的。"],[581.85,587.64,10,"That parallelism is what lets us train on trillions of tokens with thousands of GPUs.","正是这种并行性，让我们能够用数千块 GPU 在数万亿个词元上进行训练。"],[587.99,593.18,10,"Which brings us to the question of what happens when we actually make these models big.","这就引出了一个问题：当我们真的把这些模型做大时，会发生什么？"],[594.43,596.93,11,"And here's the answer: scaling laws.","答案就是：缩放定律。"],[597.28,601.44,11,"This is the well-known work by Kaplan and colleagues at OpenAI.","这是 OpenAI 的 Kaplan 及其同事的著名工作。"],[601.79,603.19,11,"Look at the three plots.","看这三张图。"],[603.54,611.91,11,"The y-axis is test loss, and the x-axes are compute, dataset size, and number of parameters, all on log scales.","纵轴是测试损失，横轴分别是算力、数据集大小和参数量，全部采用对数刻度。"],[612.26,615.12,11,"In each case, you get almost a straight line.","在每种情况下，你都会得到一条几乎笔直的直线。"],[615.47,623.58,11,"A straight line on a log-log plot means a power law: every time you multiply the resource by ten, the loss drops by a predictable fraction.","双对数坐标图上的直线意味着幂律：每当资源增加十倍，损失就会按一个可预测的比例下降。"],[623.93,631.93,11,"Each formula in the boxes just says the loss equals the resource divided by a constant, raised to a small negative power.","框里的每个公式说的都是：损失等于资源除以一个常数，再取一个很小的负数次幂。"],[632.28,633.82,11,"Why is this such a big deal?","为什么这件事如此重要？"],[634.17,639.35,11,"Because it turns building better models from an art into something closer to engineering.","因为它把构建更好的模型从一门艺术，变成了更接近工程的事情。"],[639.7,646.19,11,"If I know the curve, I can predict how good a model will be before I spend millions of dollars training it.","如果我知道这条曲线，就可以在花费数百万美元训练模型之前，预测它会有多好。"],[646.54,653.47,11,"That predictability is what gave companies the confidence to bet on bigger and bigger models.","正是这种可预测性，给了公司押注越来越大模型的信心。"],[654.72,658.7,12,"Scaling laws tell us the loss goes down smoothly.","缩放定律告诉我们，损失是平滑下降的。"],[659.05,664.93,12,"But something more surprising shows up when you look at specific tasks: emergent abilities.","但当你观察具体任务时，会出现更令人惊讶的现象：涌现能力。"],[665.28,673.0,12,"An ability is called emergent if it's basically absent in smaller models, and then appears in larger ones.","如果一种能力在较小的模型中基本不存在，而在较大的模型中出现，我们就称它为涌现能力。"],[673.35,681.19,12,"These eight plots cover tasks like modular arithmetic, word unscrambling, Persian question answering, and TruthfulQA.","这八张图涵盖的任务包括模运算、单词还原、波斯语问答和 TruthfulQA。"],[681.54,686.24,12,"The x-axis is training compute, and the y-axis is accuracy.","横轴是训练算力，纵轴是准确率。"],[686.59,694.62,12,"For a long time, performance sits flat at the random-guessing level, and then, past a certain scale, it suddenly shoots up.","在很长一段时间里，性能一直停留在随机猜测的水平，然后超过某个规模之后，它突然急剧上升。"],[694.97,696.26,12,"That's counter-intuitive.","这是反直觉的。"],[696.61,700.82,12,"The loss improved gradually, but the ability looks like it switched on.","损失是逐渐改善的，但能力看起来却像是突然被打开了开关。"],[701.17,710.29,12,"There's an ongoing debate about whether this is truly a phase transition, or partly an artifact of how we measure accuracy, and we'll revisit that.","关于这究竟是真正的相变，还是部分源于我们衡量准确率的方式，目前仍有争论，我们之后会再讨论。"],[710.64,714.42,12,"But either way, it's one of the main reasons people kept scaling.","但无论如何，这都是人们不断扩大规模的主要原因之一。"],[714.77,719.64,12,"You don't know which new abilities are waiting just beyond the next order of magnitude.","你不知道在下一个数量级之后，还有哪些新能力在等着你。"],[720.89,724.4,13,"Here's our roadmap for today. It has two big parts.","这是我们今天的路线图，它分为两大部分。"],[724.75,728.65,13,"Part one is about understanding LLMs from the outside.","第一部分是从外部理解 LLM。"],[729.0,733.19,13,"What are they? How large is large? Why does size matter so much?","它们是什么？“大”有多大？为什么规模如此重要？"],[733.54,739.0,13,"Then a case study of ChatGPT, the model that changed public perception overnight.","然后是 ChatGPT 的案例研究，这个模型一夜之间改变了公众的认知。"],[739.35,745.58,13,"And then how you can actually use LLMs, from prompting to agents to training your own.","接着是如何真正使用 LLM，从提示词到智能体，再到训练你自己的模型。"],[745.93,749.96,13,"Part two goes inside: how do you train an LLM from scratch?","第二部分深入内部：如何从零开始训练一个 LLM？"],[750.31,760.65,13,"We'll follow the pipeline step by step: first an overview, then tokenization, then pretraining, then supervised fine-tuning, and finally RLHF.","我们会一步步沿着流程走：先是概览，然后是分词、预训练、监督微调，最后是 RLHF。"],[761.0,764.21,13,"After that, we'll compare these stages with each other.","之后，我们会把这些阶段相互比较。"],[764.56,771.68,13,"One small note on ordering: the renaissance of small LLMs is listed in part one, but I'll actually cover it near the end.","关于顺序有一个小说明：小模型的复兴列在第一部分，但我实际上会放到接近最后再讲。"],[772.03,775.65,13,"It makes more sense once you know how models are trained.","等你了解了模型是如何训练的，再讲它会更容易理解。"],[776.0,778.07,13,"Let's start with the most basic question.","我们从最基本的问题开始。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"What Is an LLM? Compression, AGI and How Large Is Large","blurb":"One model for nearly everything: the deep-learning hypothesis, intelligence as compression, and how parameters, compute and trillions of tokens define 'large'.","file":"lecture05_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part2.jpg","duration":900.1,"first":14,"last":29,"slides":[{"n":14,"title":"What are LLMs","t":0.8},{"n":15,"title":"Think about that: What is the difference between Large Language models (LLMs) and language models? Just larger?","t":17.14},{"n":16,"title":"What is an LLM （one model for nearly everything）","t":70.78},{"n":17,"title":"DL hypothesis","t":131.41},{"n":18,"title":"Jason Wei’s Rule of thumb","t":192.11},{"n":19,"title":"AGI","t":249.66},{"n":20,"title":"A possible way to AGI","t":302.51},{"n":21,"title":"Why LLMs: Learning/intelligence as compression","t":367.61},{"n":22,"title":"Next word prediction forces the neural network to learn a lot about the world:","t":430.71},{"n":23,"title":"How large is large?","t":494.81},{"n":24,"title":"How Large are “Large” LMs?","t":507.24},{"n":25,"title":"Large Language Models - yottaFlops of Compute","t":571.32},{"n":26,"title":"How large is “large”？","t":642.21},{"n":27,"title":"Data scaling - Trillions of Tokens","t":700.72},{"n":28,"title":"Qwen3 Technical Report. https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.09388","t":769.37},{"n":29,"title":"Some funny facts （may be wrong）","t":837.97}],"sents":[[0.8,5.01,14,"Let's begin with section one: what exactly is a large language model?","我们从第一节开始：大语言模型到底是什么？"],[5.36,9.21,14,"It sounds like a trivial question, since it's right there in the name.","这听起来像个很简单的问题，毕竟名字里就写着。"],[9.56,15.74,14,"But as you'll see in a second, the answer is a bit more interesting than a language model, just bigger.","但你马上会看到，答案比“一个更大的语言模型”要有趣一些。"],[16.99,20.42,15,"So let me ask you to think about this for a moment.","所以请大家先花点时间思考一下这个问题。"],[20.77,29.12,15,"You already learned about language models in Lecture 3: models that assign probabilities to sequences of words, or predict the next word.","你们在第三讲已经学过语言模型：为词序列分配概率，或者预测下一个词的模型。"],[29.47,34.74,15,"What's the difference between those and a large language model? Is it just that it's larger?","它们和大语言模型有什么区别？仅仅是更大吗？"],[35.09,37.77,15,"Pause for a few seconds and think about it.","停下来想几秒钟。"],[38.12,39.0,15,"Here's my answer.","这是我的答案。"],[39.35,44.96,15,"Quantitatively, yes, it's larger: more parameters, more data, more compute.","从数量上看，是的，它更大：更多参数、更多数据、更多算力。"],[45.31,47.24,15,"But the interesting part is qualitative.","但有趣的部分在于质的变化。"],[47.59,54.42,15,"At some scale, the model stops being just a next-word predictor, and starts behaving like a general-purpose problem solver.","在某个规模上，模型不再只是一个预测下一个词的工具，而开始表现得像一个通用的问题求解者。"],[54.77,61.31,15,"It can follow instructions, learn from a few examples in the prompt, and reason step by step.","它能遵循指令，能从提示中的几个例子里学习，还能一步步推理。"],[61.66,64.13,15,"Nobody explicitly trained those skills.","没有人专门训练过这些技能。"],[64.48,69.38,15,"That qualitative jump is what makes large a meaningful word, and we'll keep coming back to it.","正是这种质的飞跃，让“大”这个词有了意义，我们会反复回到这一点。"],[70.63,77.12,16,"One way to describe that qualitative change is the phrase on this slide: one model for nearly everything.","描述这种质变的一种方式就是这页上的说法：一个模型解决几乎所有问题。"],[77.47,81.19,16,"In the old days of NLP, we built one model per task.","在过去的 NLP 中，我们为每个任务单独构建一个模型。"],[81.54,87.97,16,"A classifier for sentiment, a separate system for question answering, another for summarization.","情感分析用一个分类器，问答用一个单独的系统，摘要再用另一个。"],[88.32,98.17,16,"Look at the top row: an LLM handles text classification, question answering, document summarization and text generation, with the same set of weights.","看上面一行：一个 LLM 用同一套权重，就能处理文本分类、问答、文档摘要和文本生成。"],[98.52,107.26,16,"And in the bottom row, it can be adapted to very different fields, like retail, finance and entertainment, using relatively small domain datasets.","下面一行显示，它可以用相对较小的领域数据集，适配到零售、金融、娱乐等非常不同的领域。"],[107.61,113.5,16,"This is why Stanford researchers coined the term foundation model, in the paper cited at the bottom.","这就是为什么斯坦福的研究者在底部引用的论文中提出了“基础模型”这个术语。"],[113.85,122.46,16,"The idea is that you build one big general model once, and then everything else is built on top of it, like a building on its foundation.","它的思想是：先构建一个大型通用模型，然后其他一切都建在它之上，就像大楼建在地基上一样。"],[122.81,130.01,16,"That changes the economics of AI: the expensive part is done once, and adaptation becomes cheap.","这改变了 AI 的经济模式：昂贵的部分只做一次，而适配变得很便宜。"],[131.26,136.49,17,"Let me give you a little bit of history of how people thought about what neural networks can do.","我先讲一点历史，看看人们过去是如何看待神经网络能做什么的。"],[136.84,142.93,17,"Around two thousand fourteen, Ilya Sutskever framed what he called the deep learning hypothesis.","大约在 2014 年，Ilya Sutskever 提出了他所谓的深度学习假说。"],[143.28,150.24,17,"Anything a human can do in about zero point one seconds, a big ten-layer neural network can do too.","任何人类能在大约 0.1 秒内完成的事情，一个大型的十层神经网络也能做到。"],[150.59,159.17,17,"Think about what you can do in a tenth of a second: recognize a face, recognize a spoken word, see that a picture contains a cat.","想想你在十分之一秒内能做什么：认出一张脸，听出一个词，看出一张图里有只猫。"],[159.52,165.09,17,"Those are perception tasks, and that's exactly where deep learning first succeeded.","这些都是感知任务，而这正是深度学习最先取得成功的地方。"],[165.44,168.52,17,"Why ten layers, and why zero point one seconds?","为什么是十层？为什么是 0.1 秒？"],[168.87,177.72,17,"The intuition is that neurons in the brain are slow, so in a tenth of a second, a signal can only pass through a handful of processing stages.","直觉是，大脑中的神经元很慢，所以在十分之一秒内，信号只能经过少数几个处理阶段。"],[178.07,184.89,17,"At that time, we simply could not train much larger models, so this was the ambition that matched the hardware.","那时候我们根本无法训练大得多的模型，所以这是一个与当时硬件相匹配的目标。"],[185.24,190.71,17,"Keep that zero point one seconds in mind, because the next slide moves the bar.","记住这个 0.1 秒，因为下一页会把这个标准往上提。"],[191.96,197.35,18,"Fast-forward to the LLM era, and Jason Wei proposed an updated rule of thumb.","快进到大模型时代，Jason Wei 提出了一个更新版的经验法则。"],[197.7,204.27,18,"Language models can do, with decent accuracy, most things an average human can do in one minute.","语言模型能以不错的准确率，完成普通人在一分钟内能做的大多数事情。"],[204.62,210.77,18,"So we went from zero point one seconds to one minute, a factor of about six hundred.","所以我们从 0.1 秒走到了一分钟，大约提高了六百倍。"],[211.12,212.76,18,"What can you do in a minute?","你在一分钟内能做什么？"],[213.11,221.09,18,"Answer a factual question, write a short email, translate a paragraph, fix a simple bug, explain a concept.","回答一个事实性问题，写一封简短的邮件，翻译一段话，修一个简单的 bug，解释一个概念。"],[221.44,225.25,18,"Those are exactly the things ChatGPT-style models are good at.","这些正是 ChatGPT 这类模型所擅长的。"],[225.6,231.66,18,"What about tasks that take a human an hour, or a week? That's the frontier right now.","那么需要人花一小时或者一周的任务呢？这正是当前的前沿。"],[232.01,239.0,18,"Reasoning models that think longer, and agents that take many actions, are essentially trying to stretch that time horizon further.","会思考更久的推理模型，和会执行很多步行动的智能体，本质上都是在试图把这个时间跨度进一步拉长。"],[239.35,241.48,18,"It's a handy mental model.","这是一个很好用的思维模型。"],[241.83,248.26,18,"When you wonder whether an LLM can do a task, ask yourself how long it would take a typical person.","当你想知道 LLM 能否完成某个任务时，问问自己一个普通人需要花多长时间。"],[249.51,255.93,19,"Which leads to the big question everyone asks: AGI, artificial general intelligence.","这引出了每个人都会问的大问题：AGI，通用人工智能。"],[256.28,263.5,19,"The definition here is a machine that can understand or learn any intellectual task that a human being can.","这里的定义是：一台能够理解或学习人类能做的任何智力任务的机器。"],[263.85,265.29,19,"Notice the word any.","注意“任何”这个词。"],[265.64,271.46,19,"Not chess, not translation, but everything, including tasks it has never seen before.","不是下棋，也不是翻译，而是一切，包括它从未见过的任务。"],[271.81,275.67,19,"So let me ask you: do you believe LLMs can get there?","所以我问大家：你相信 LLM 能做到吗？"],[276.02,282.29,19,"Think about where you stand: yes, no, or that LLMs are necessary but not enough.","想想你的立场：能，不能，还是 LLM 是必要的但还不够？"],[282.64,286.52,19,"There's no settled answer, and smart people disagree strongly.","这个问题没有定论，聪明人之间的分歧也很大。"],[286.87,292.13,19,"Some argue next-token prediction is a dead end without grounding in the physical world.","有人认为，如果不与物理世界建立联系，预测下一个词元就是一条死胡同。"],[292.48,297.49,19,"Others argue we just need more scale, better reasoning and better tools.","也有人认为，我们只需要更大的规模、更好的推理和更好的工具。"],[297.84,301.11,19,"The next slide shows one view that I find reasonable.","下一页展示了一个我认为比较合理的观点。"],[302.36,307.1,20,"One possible path to AGI is LLM plus agent.","通往 AGI 的一条可能路径是：LLM 加智能体。"],[307.45,309.74,20,"The idea is to split the job in two.","思路是把工作一分为二。"],[310.09,319.49,20,"The LLM is the brain, and the agent framework gives that brain hands: tools like calculators, solvers, databases, search engines.","LLM 是大脑，而智能体框架给这个大脑装上双手：计算器、求解器、数据库、搜索引擎等工具。"],[319.84,321.48,20,"Humans work the same way.","人类也是这样工作的。"],[321.83,327.34,20,"We're not good at multiplying eight-digit numbers in our heads, so we use a calculator.","我们不擅长心算八位数乘法，所以我们用计算器。"],[327.69,330.45,20,"Nobody says that makes us less intelligent.","没有人会说这让我们变得不聪明了。"],[330.8,332.32,20,"Both sides can be improved.","两边都可以改进。"],[332.67,339.8,20,"For the brain, we can let it think longer, which is what o1-style reasoning models do with long chains of thought.","对于大脑，我们可以让它思考得更久，这正是 o1 这类推理模型用长思维链所做的。"],[340.15,345.76,20,"For the tools, we can give it external knowledge, information, and even explicit rules.","对于工具，我们可以给它外部知识、信息，甚至是明确的规则。"],[346.11,351.1,20,"That's a bit like the old expert systems, but now driven by a flexible language model.","这有点像过去的专家系统，只不过现在是由一个灵活的语言模型来驱动。"],[351.45,356.15,20,"The paper at the bottom studies the reasoning boundary of chain-of-thought.","底部的这篇论文研究的是思维链的推理边界。"],[356.5,362.29,20,"That's a nice way of saying that thinking alone has limits, and tools are one way to push past them.","换句话说，单靠思考是有极限的，而工具是突破这些极限的一种方式。"],[362.64,366.21,20,"We'll come back to both halves in Lectures 6 and 7.","我们会在第六讲和第七讲中分别回到这两部分。"],[367.46,369.92,21,"Now let's ask why this works at all.","现在我们来问：这一切为什么会奏效？"],[370.27,374.7,21,"A very useful way to think about LLMs is as compression.","理解 LLM 的一个非常有用的方式，是把它看作压缩。"],[375.05,378.82,21,"Look at the top row, a picture popularized by Andrej Karpathy.","看上面一行，这是 Andrej Karpathy 推广的一张图。"],[379.17,382.91,21,"You take a chunk of the internet, about ten terabytes of text.","你拿来互联网的一大块内容，大约 10 TB 的文本。"],[383.26,392.28,21,"You run it through roughly six thousand GPUs for twelve days, costing around two million dollars and about ten to the twenty-four floating-point operations.","用大约六千块 GPU 跑十二天，花费约两百万美元，总计约十的二十四次方次浮点运算。"],[392.63,397.68,21,"What comes out is a single file of parameters, about one hundred forty gigabytes.","最后得到的是一个参数文件，大约 140 GB。"],[398.03,401.19,21,"That's a lossy compression of the internet into the weights.","这就是把互联网有损地压缩进了模型权重里。"],[401.54,403.87,21,"The bottom picture makes it concrete.","下面这张图让它更加具体。"],[404.22,413.53,21,"For a model like Llama 2 70B, the whole thing is just two files: the parameters, and roughly five hundred lines of C code to run them.","对于 Llama 2 70B 这样的模型，整个东西只有两个文件：参数文件，和大约五百行用来运行它的 C 代码。"],[413.88,415.6,21,"You could put it on a laptop.","你可以把它放在一台笔记本电脑上。"],[415.95,417.53,21,"Why call it intelligence?","为什么称之为智能？"],[417.88,422.33,21,"Because to compress data well, you have to understand its regularities.","因为要把数据压缩得好，你就必须理解其中的规律。"],[422.68,429.31,21,"The better you predict, the better you compress, and good prediction requires real knowledge about the world.","预测得越好，压缩得就越好，而好的预测需要对世界有真正的了解。"],[430.56,435.73,22,"Let me make that idea concrete. This is a Wikipedia page about Ruth Handler.","我来把这个想法具体化。这是关于 Ruth Handler 的维基百科页面。"],[436.08,442.28,22,"Imagine the network is reading this page and has to predict the next word at every position.","想象一下，网络正在读这个页面，并且必须在每个位置预测下一个词。"],[442.63,447.27,22,"After the words, she is best known for inventing the, it needs to know: Barbie doll.","在“她最为人所知的是发明了”之后，它需要知道答案是：芭比娃娃。"],[447.62,454.89,22,"After the words, born on November fourth, nineteen sixteen, in, it needs: Denver, Colorado.","在“出生于 1916 年 11 月 4 日，地点是”之后，它需要知道：科罗拉多州丹佛。"],[455.24,459.99,22,"After the words, co-founder of toy manufacturer, it needs: Mattel.","在“玩具制造商的联合创始人”之后，它需要知道：美泰。"],[460.34,464.18,22,"There's no way to predict those words well by just learning grammar.","仅仅学会语法，是不可能把这些词预测好的。"],[464.53,471.96,22,"The only way to lower the loss is to actually store facts: who she was, where she was born, what company she founded.","降低损失的唯一方法，就是真正记住事实：她是谁、出生在哪里、创办了什么公司。"],[472.31,482.5,22,"Across billions of documents, that pressure forces the network to absorb an enormous amount of knowledge about history, science, people and places.","在数十亿篇文档中，这种压力迫使网络吸收大量关于历史、科学、人物和地点的知识。"],[482.85,488.82,22,"That's the deep reason a simple objective like next-word prediction produces such capable models.","这就是为什么像预测下一个词这样简单的目标，能够产生如此强大的模型的深层原因。"],[489.17,493.41,22,"Keep this in mind when we get to pretraining in the second half.","等我们在后半部分讲到预训练时，请记住这一点。"],[494.66,497.09,23,"So we've talked about what LLMs are.","我们已经讨论了 LLM 是什么。"],[497.44,500.66,23,"The next natural question is: how large is large?","接下来自然要问：“大”到底有多大？"],[501.01,505.84,23,"Let's put some numbers on the table: parameters, compute and training data.","我们来摆出一些数字：参数量、算力和训练数据。"],[507.09,509.05,24,"Here's a first look at the numbers.","先来初步看看这些数字。"],[509.4,516.06,24,"On the left, the number of parameters, and on the right, the size of the training corpus in tokens.","左边是参数数量，右边是以词元计的训练语料规模。"],[516.41,522.22,24,"Notice both x-axes are on a log scale, so every gridline is a factor of ten.","注意两张图的横轴都是对数刻度，所以每条网格线代表十倍。"],[522.57,526.67,24,"ELMo models are around ten to one hundred million parameters.","ELMo 模型大约有一千万到一亿个参数。"],[527.02,530.14,24,"BERT is around one hundred to three hundred million.","BERT 大约在一亿到三亿之间。"],[530.49,533.91,24,"GPT-2 goes up to about one point five billion.","GPT-2 最大约为十五亿。"],[534.26,540.41,24,"Then GPT-3 jumps to one hundred seventy-five billion, more than a hundred times bigger than GPT-2.","然后 GPT-3 跃升到一千七百五十亿，比 GPT-2 大一百多倍。"],[540.76,547.83,24,"The corpus grows the same way: GPT-3's bar is way off to the right compared with BERT and GPT-2.","语料规模也以同样的方式增长：和 BERT、GPT-2 相比，GPT-3 的柱子远远伸到了右边。"],[548.18,558.29,24,"At the bottom are some other large early models: PaLM at five hundred forty billion, OPT at one hundred seventy-five billion, BLOOM at one hundred seventy-six billion.","底部列出了其他一些早期大模型：PaLM 有五千四百亿参数，OPT 有一千七百五十亿，BLOOM 有一千七百六十亿。"],[558.64,565.53,24,"The lesson is that within just two or three years, the field went up by three orders of magnitude in model size.","这里的启示是：仅仅两三年内，这个领域的模型规模就提升了三个数量级。"],[565.88,569.92,24,"That's not incremental progress; that's a different regime.","这不是渐进式的进步，而是进入了一个全新的阶段。"],[571.17,573.65,25,"Another way to see the scale is compute.","看规模的另一个角度是算力。"],[574.0,585.24,25,"This chart shows the estimated training compute of notable AI systems, from the nineteen fifties until about two thousand twenty-two, again on a log scale.","这张图展示了从 1950 年代到大约 2022 年，一些著名 AI 系统的估计训练算力，同样是对数刻度。"],[585.59,589.89,25,"On the far left you have Theseus, a tiny maze-solving system.","最左边是 Theseus，一个很小的走迷宫系统。"],[590.24,596.54,25,"Then ADALINE, Neocognitron, NetTalk, and the neural probabilistic language model.","然后是 ADALINE、Neocognitron、NetTalk，以及神经概率语言模型。"],[596.89,609.35,25,"And then the curve really takes off after twenty ten: BERT-Large, GPT-2, GPT-3, LaMDA, and PaLM near ten to the twenty-four FLOPs at the top right.","2010 年之后，曲线真正起飞：BERT-Large、GPT-2、GPT-3、LaMDA，以及右上角接近十的二十四次方 FLOPs 的 PaLM。"],[609.7,614.65,25,"FLOPs here means the total number of floating-point operations used for training.","这里的 FLOPs 指的是训练所用的浮点运算总次数。"],[615.0,618.44,25,"That's why the title says yotta-scale compute.","这就是为什么标题说是 yotta 级别的算力。"],[618.79,622.21,25,"You'll notice I've crossed out the line about GPT-4.","你会注意到，我把关于 GPT-4 的那一行划掉了。"],[622.56,630.58,25,"There were many rumors about its size, but OpenAI never confirmed them, so treat any specific number as speculation.","关于它的规模有很多传言，但 OpenAI 从未证实，所以任何具体数字都只能当作猜测。"],[630.93,640.81,25,"What is certain is the trend: training compute for frontier models has grown many orders of magnitude, and that's what made LLMs possible.","可以确定的是趋势：前沿模型的训练算力已经增长了许多个数量级，正是这一点让 LLM 成为可能。"],[642.06,647.63,26,"Another important point: large is relative, and the meaning keeps changing.","另一个要点是：“大”是相对的，它的含义一直在变化。"],[647.98,655.33,26,"In the BERT era, a base model was about one hundred million parameters, and a large one was about three hundred million.","在 BERT 时代，base 模型大约一亿参数，large 模型大约三亿。"],[655.68,663.42,26,"In the T5 era, the small model was sixty million, base around two hundred million, and large seven hundred seventy million.","在 T5 时代，small 模型六千万参数，base 约两亿，large 七亿七千万。"],[663.77,667.52,26,"And the really big ones were three billion and eleven billion.","而真正大的模型有三十亿和一百一十亿参数。"],[667.87,677.94,26,"Today, a seven to thirteen billion parameter model is what many people would call a base or medium-size LLM, and that's not even close to the frontier.","今天，七十亿到一百三十亿参数的模型，很多人只会把它叫作基础或中等规模的 LLM，而且离前沿还差得很远。"],[678.29,680.1,26,"I love the picture on the right.","我很喜欢右边这张图。"],[680.45,686.76,26,"It's like ordering coffee: you point at the smallest cup, and the barista says, sorry, sir, that's a large.","就像点咖啡：你指着最小的杯子，店员却说：“对不起先生，那个是大杯。”"],[687.11,691.81,26,"Today's small model would have been the largest model in the world a few years ago.","今天的“小”模型，放在几年前会是世界上最大的模型。"],[692.16,696.83,26,"So when you read a paper that says large, always check the year.","所以当你读到一篇论文说“大”的时候，一定要看看它是哪一年的。"],[697.18,699.32,26,"The label is a moving target.","这个标签是不断变化的。"],[700.57,702.82,27,"Parameters are only half the story.","参数只是故事的一半。"],[703.17,707.82,27,"The other half is data, measured in tokens seen during training.","另一半是数据，用训练中见过的词元数量来衡量。"],[708.17,710.99,27,"Look at the circles from left to right.","从左到右看这些圆。"],[711.34,716.47,27,"A thirteen-year-old human has heard or read fewer than one hundred million words.","一个十三岁的孩子听过或读过的词不到一亿个。"],[716.82,723.61,27,"BERT in twenty eighteen was trained on about three billion tokens, and RoBERTa on thirty billion.","2018 年的 BERT 在大约三十亿词元上训练，RoBERTa 则是三百亿。"],[723.96,730.17,27,"GPT-3 on two hundred billion, and Chinchilla in twenty twenty-two on one point four trillion.","GPT-3 是两千亿，2022 年的 Chinchilla 是一万四千亿。"],[730.52,736.08,27,"And models like Llama 2, PaLM 2 and Mistral on roughly three to ten trillion.","而 Llama 2、PaLM 2 和 Mistral 这类模型大约是三万亿到十万亿。"],[736.43,741.89,27,"As the title says, we've already moved well past hundreds of billions, into the trillions.","正如标题所说，我们早已越过了千亿级，进入了万亿级。"],[742.24,743.38,27,"Two observations.","有两点观察。"],[743.73,750.72,27,"First, these models see thousands of times more text than a human child, yet children learn language far more efficiently.","第一，这些模型看到的文本比一个孩子多几千倍，但孩子学习语言的效率却高得多。"],[751.07,757.48,27,"That gap is a fascinating research question, and the BabyLM challenge linked at the bottom is exactly about it.","这个差距是一个非常有趣的研究问题，底部链接的 BabyLM 挑战赛研究的正是这个。"],[757.83,764.34,27,"Second, the GPT-4 number is crossed out again, because it's an unconfirmed rumor.","第二，GPT-4 的数字又被划掉了，因为它只是未经证实的传言。"],[764.69,767.97,27,"For a confirmed recent number, let's look at Qwen.","要看一个已经证实的最新数字，我们来看看 Qwen。"],[769.22,774.2,28,"Here's a data point you can actually verify: the Qwen3 technical report.","这是一个你可以亲自核实的数据：Qwen3 技术报告。"],[774.55,785.21,28,"The highlighted sentence says all Qwen3 models are trained on a dataset covering one hundred nineteen languages and dialects, with a total of thirty-six trillion tokens.","高亮的句子说，所有 Qwen3 模型都在一个涵盖 119 种语言和方言、总计 36 万亿词元的数据集上训练。"],[785.56,794.37,28,"That's about twice as many as Qwen2.5, and more than ten times the Llama 2 era.","这大约是 Qwen2.5 的两倍，是 Llama 2 时代的十倍以上。"],[794.72,799.52,28,"Read the second paragraph too, because it shows where those tokens come from.","也请读一下第二段，因为它说明了这些词元从何而来。"],[799.87,808.32,28,"They used their vision-language model to extract text from huge numbers of PDF documents, then cleaned it with another model.","他们用自己的视觉语言模型从海量 PDF 文档中提取文本，再用另一个模型进行清洗。"],[808.67,815.72,28,"They used their math and coding models to synthesize trillions of tokens of textbooks, question-answer pairs and code.","他们用自己的数学和代码模型合成了数万亿词元的教材、问答对和代码。"],[816.07,826.58,28,"And they built a system to annotate over thirty trillion tokens with labels like educational value and domain, so they could choose the data mixture carefully.","他们还构建了一个系统，用教育价值和领域等标签标注了超过 30 万亿词元，以便仔细选择数据配比。"],[826.93,831.55,28,"The takeaway: at this scale, collecting data is no longer just crawling the web.","要点是：在这种规模下，收集数据已经不仅仅是爬取网页了。"],[831.9,836.57,28,"It's an engineering pipeline where models help build the data for the next models.","它是一条工程流水线，由模型来帮助构建下一代模型的数据。"],[837.82,840.49,29,"Let's lighten things up with some funny facts.","我们来点轻松的，看一些有趣的“事实”。"],[840.84,847.6,29,"The title says may be wrong, and I mean it, so please treat this slide as gossip, not as material for your exam.","标题写着“可能是错的”，我是认真的，所以请把这一页当作八卦，而不是考试内容。"],[847.95,854.26,29,"The rumors going around are that GPT-5 and Claude are around four trillion parameters.","流传的说法是，GPT-5 和 Claude 大约有四万亿参数。"],[854.61,857.73,29,"Other frontier models may be close to ten trillion.","其他一些前沿模型可能接近十万亿。"],[858.08,866.53,29,"And some next-generation systems may use a looped Transformer, which reuses the same layers several times instead of stacking new ones.","还有一些下一代系统可能使用了循环 Transformer，它会把同样的层重复使用多次，而不是堆叠新的层。"],[866.88,869.4,29,"None of this is officially confirmed.","这些都没有得到官方证实。"],[869.75,871.28,29,"The last line is different.","最后一行则不同。"],[871.63,880.92,29,"Alibaba has said publicly that Qwen3-Max has over one trillion parameters, and was pretrained on thirty-six trillion tokens.","阿里巴巴公开表示，Qwen3-Max 拥有超过一万亿参数，并在 36 万亿词元上进行了预训练。"],[881.27,886.68,29,"So the trillion-parameter club is real, and at least some of its members are open about it.","所以万亿参数俱乐部是真实存在的，而且至少有一些成员是公开透明的。"],[887.03,888.45,29,"Why show rumors at all?","那为什么还要展示传言呢？"],[888.8,898.2,29,"Because frontier labs no longer publish their sizes, and part of being a researcher today is learning to separate what's confirmed from what's speculation.","因为前沿实验室已经不再公布模型规模，而当今做研究者的一部分功课，就是学会区分什么是证实的、什么是猜测。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"Why Larger Models: Emergent Abilities and Generalization","blurb":"What changes from LM to LLM: few-shot and zero-shot prompting emerge with scale, knowledge generalizes, and reinforcement learning only pays off on big models.","file":"lecture05_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part3.jpg","duration":614.7,"first":30,"last":40,"slides":[{"n":30,"title":"Why LLMs?","t":0.8},{"n":31,"title":"LM vs. LLM","t":18.27},{"n":32,"title":"Why Larger language models","t":73.63},{"n":33,"title":"Why LLMs?","t":137.0},{"n":34,"title":"Example of Emergent abilities: Few-shot prompting","t":192.78},{"n":35,"title":"Example of Emergent abilities: Zero-shot prompting","t":242.87},{"n":36,"title":"Why LLMs?","t":302.46},{"n":37,"title":"We can expect a lot more “general capability” across all areas of knowledge","t":359.49},{"n":38,"title":"LLMs might benefit from generalization","t":427.73},{"n":39,"title":"Emergent ability: RL only works when models scale","t":488.36},{"n":40,"title":"Some basics for large language models","t":553.66}],"sents":[[0.8,6.46,30,"We've seen that LLMs are huge in parameters, compute and data.","我们已经看到，LLM 在参数、算力和数据上都非常庞大。"],[6.81,9.83,30,"That raises the obvious question: why bother?","这就引出了一个显而易见的问题：何必呢？"],[10.18,16.87,30,"What do we actually gain from making models this large? Let's look at the main reasons.","把模型做得这么大，我们到底能得到什么？我们来看看主要原因。"],[18.12,23.69,31,"This slide answers the question I asked you a few minutes ago: LM versus LLM.","这一页回答了我几分钟前问大家的问题：LM 和 LLM 的区别。"],[24.04,29.79,31,"Large language models are a subset of language models, the small circle inside the big one.","大语言模型是语言模型的一个子集，就是大圆里面的那个小圆。"],[30.14,36.44,31,"Quantitatively, people usually draw the line somewhere around ten to one hundred billion parameters.","从数量上看，人们通常把界线划在大约一百亿到一千亿参数之间。"],[36.79,40.62,31,"Although, as we just saw, that line keeps moving.","不过正如我们刚才看到的，这条线一直在移动。"],[40.97,48.9,31,"The more interesting part is the right-hand side: qualitatively, LLMs show emergent properties, and zero-shot learning is the classic example.","更有趣的是右侧：从质的角度看，LLM 表现出涌现特性，零样本学习就是经典的例子。"],[49.25,53.8,31,"You can describe a task the model has never been trained on, and it just does it.","你可以描述一个模型从未训练过的任务，它就能直接完成。"],[54.15,59.44,31,"A small language model can complete your sentence; a large one can follow your instructions.","小语言模型能帮你补全句子，而大模型能遵循你的指令。"],[59.79,69.63,31,"So when someone asks you whether an LLM is just a bigger language model, the honest answer is: technically yes, but the size changes what it can do.","所以当有人问你 LLM 是否只是一个更大的语言模型时，诚实的回答是：技术上是的，但规模改变了它能做的事情。"],[69.98,72.23,31,"Let's look at those changes one by one.","我们来逐一看看这些变化。"],[73.48,76.62,32,"Here are the main reasons to go large, in one slide.","这一页概括了把模型做大的主要原因。"],[76.97,78.73,32,"First, more world knowledge.","第一，更多的世界知识。"],[79.08,86.43,32,"The LAMA work showed that you can query a pretrained model like a knowledge base, asking it to fill in: Dante was born in, blank.","LAMA 的工作表明，你可以像查询知识库一样查询预训练模型，比如让它填空：但丁出生于哪里。"],[86.78,89.88,32,"And bigger models store more of those facts.","而更大的模型存储了更多这样的事实。"],[90.23,96.97,32,"Second, more capacity to learn problem-solving skills like coding, revising articles and reasoning.","第二，更强的能力去学习解决问题的技能，比如编程、修改文章和推理。"],[97.32,100.99,32,"Third, better generalization to tasks it hasn't seen.","第三，对没见过的任务有更好的泛化能力。"],[101.34,104.14,32,"And fourth, emergent abilities.","第四，涌现能力。"],[104.49,112.91,32,"Look at the four plots on the right: chain-of-thought prompting, instruction tuning, a scratchpad for eight-digit addition, and calibration.","看右边的四张图：思维链提示、指令微调、用于八位数加法的草稿纸，以及校准。"],[113.26,119.39,32,"They all do little or even hurt at small scale, shown by the flat or lower lines on the left.","在小规模时它们作用不大甚至有害，表现为左侧平坦或更低的线。"],[119.74,123.53,32,"And then they suddenly help a lot once the model is big enough.","而一旦模型足够大，它们就会突然带来很大帮助。"],[123.88,129.21,32,"That's a subtle but important point: it's not only the raw abilities that emerge.","这是一个微妙但重要的观点：涌现的不只是原始能力。"],[129.56,135.6,32,"Even our techniques, like chain-of-thought, only start working above a certain size.","就连我们的技术，比如思维链，也只有在超过一定规模后才开始起作用。"],[136.85,142.98,33,"Let's zoom in on emergence a bit more, because it's one of the most talked-about properties of LLMs.","我们再深入看一下涌现，因为它是 LLM 最受关注的特性之一。"],[143.33,151.7,33,"The definition again: an ability is emergent if it's not present in smaller models, but is present in larger ones.","再说一遍定义：如果一种能力在小模型中不存在、而在大模型中存在，它就是涌现能力。"],[152.05,161.15,33,"The capabilities that most famously emerged are zero-shot prompting, few-shot prompting, chain-of-thought, and many others.","最著名的涌现能力包括零样本提示、少样本提示、思维链，以及其他很多能力。"],[161.5,166.08,33,"On the left is the simplest example: a few-shot sentiment prompt.","左边是最简单的例子：一个少样本的情感分析提示。"],[166.43,169.78,33,"On the right you see the same eight task plots from earlier.","右边是之前那八个任务的图。"],[170.13,173.52,33,"The precise definition in blue is worth reading carefully.","蓝色的精确定义值得仔细读一读。"],[173.87,180.39,33,"A few-shot task is emergent if small models get random accuracy, and large models get above-random accuracy.","如果小模型只能达到随机水平的准确率，而大模型能超过随机水平，那么这个少样本任务就是涌现的。"],[180.74,186.41,33,"In other words, the curve doesn't rise gradually from zero; it stays flat and then takes off.","换句话说，曲线不是从零开始逐渐上升，而是先保持平坦，然后突然起飞。"],[186.76,191.38,33,"The next two slides show what few-shot and zero-shot prompting actually look like.","接下来两页会展示少样本和零样本提示实际是什么样子。"],[192.63,196.71,34,"Here is few-shot prompting, also called in-context learning.","这是少样本提示，也叫上下文学习。"],[197.06,203.3,34,"The input gives the model one example: Review: This movie sucks. Sentiment: negative.","输入给了模型一个例子：评论：这部电影太烂了。情感：负面。"],[203.65,208.63,34,"Then a new review, I love this movie, with the sentiment left blank.","然后是一条新评论，“我爱这部电影”，情感一栏留空。"],[208.98,211.3,34,"The model fills in: positive.","模型填上了：正面。"],[211.65,215.95,34,"What's remarkable is that no weights changed. We didn't fine-tune anything.","值得注意的是，没有任何权重发生变化，我们什么都没有微调。"],[216.3,220.46,34,"The model figured out the task purely from the examples in its context window.","模型完全是从上下文窗口里的例子中弄明白了任务。"],[220.81,226.51,34,"It's the same way you'd understand a new exam format by looking at one solved example.","就像你看了一道做好的例题，就能明白一种新的考试题型一样。"],[226.86,234.89,34,"GPT-3 was the paper that really showed this works at scale, and small models simply can't do it reliably.","GPT-3 那篇论文真正证明了这在大规模下是可行的，而小模型根本无法可靠地做到。"],[235.24,238.52,34,"They'll often just continue the text in a random direction.","它们往往只会把文本朝某个随机的方向续写下去。"],[238.87,241.47,34,"That's why it's counted as an emergent ability.","这就是为什么它被算作一种涌现能力。"],[242.72,248.53,35,"Zero-shot prompting goes one step further: no examples at all, just a description of the task.","零样本提示更进一步：完全没有例子，只有对任务的描述。"],[248.88,257.07,35,"The definition at the top is the key: the ability of a model to complete a task it was not explicitly trained to do.","顶部的定义是关键：模型完成一项它没有被专门训练过的任务的能力。"],[257.42,260.14,35,"Compare the old way and the new way.","比较一下旧方法和新方法。"],[260.49,268.11,35,"In the old way, on the left, if you wanted a language-identification system, you'd collect thousands to millions of labeled examples.","在左边的旧方法中，如果你想要一个语种识别系统，你得收集几千到几百万条标注样本。"],[268.46,274.01,35,"Hello is English, Hola is Spanish, and you'd train a classifier just for that.","Hello 是英语，Hola 是西班牙语，然后专门为此训练一个分类器。"],[274.36,282.39,35,"In the new way, on the right, you train a very large model on a very large unlabeled corpus that happens to contain English and Spanish.","在右边的新方法中，你在一个恰好包含英语和西班牙语的超大无标注语料上训练一个超大模型。"],[282.74,287.23,35,"Afterwards, you can simply ask: which language is this sentence in?","之后，你只需要问：这句话是什么语言？"],[287.58,293.84,35,"And it answers correctly, even though nobody ever gave it a single labeled example for that task.","它就能正确回答，尽管从来没有人为这个任务给过它哪怕一个标注样本。"],[294.19,301.06,35,"That's a huge shift in how we build NLP systems: from collecting labels for each task, to just asking.","这是构建 NLP 系统方式的巨大转变：从为每个任务收集标注，到直接提问。"],[302.31,308.57,36,"Another big benefit of scale is generalization: one model that can solve many NLP tasks.","规模的另一大好处是泛化：一个模型就能解决许多 NLP 任务。"],[308.92,314.36,36,"This is the T5 picture you may remember. Every task is written as text in, text out.","这是你们可能还记得的 T5 图。每个任务都被写成文本输入、文本输出的形式。"],[314.71,319.69,36,"Translate English to German: That is good, gives: Das ist gut.","“把英语翻译成德语：That is good”，输出“Das ist gut”。"],[320.04,327.66,36,"A cola sentence prefix asks whether a sentence is grammatical, and the answer is: not acceptable.","带 cola sentence 前缀的输入询问一个句子是否合乎语法，答案是“not acceptable”。"],[328.01,335.43,36,"An stsb prefix asks for a similarity score, and the model literally outputs the string three point eight.","stsb 前缀要求给出相似度分数，模型直接输出字符串“3.8”。"],[335.78,338.42,36,"And summarize produces a summary.","而 summarize 则会生成一段摘要。"],[338.77,340.97,36,"The bottom line is the important one.","底部这一行才是重点。"],[341.32,351.7,36,"Models like FLAN take this further: if you train on enough different tasks described with instructions, the model can generalize to new tasks it never saw during training.","像 FLAN 这样的模型更进一步：如果你在足够多用指令描述的不同任务上训练，模型就能泛化到训练中从未见过的新任务。"],[352.05,358.09,36,"We'll see FLAN again in the SFT section, because this idea is the heart of instruction tuning.","我们会在 SFT 部分再次看到 FLAN，因为这个思想正是指令微调的核心。"],[359.34,365.02,37,"And when models get large enough, they start to generalize to genuinely difficult tasks.","当模型足够大时，它们开始能泛化到真正困难的任务上。"],[365.37,373.15,37,"This chart compares GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 on a range of real human exams.","这张图比较了 GPT-3.5 和 GPT-4 在一系列真实人类考试上的表现。"],[373.5,384.59,37,"The blue bars are GPT-3.5, and the green bars show how much higher GPT-4 goes, as an estimated percentile among human test takers.","蓝色柱子是 GPT-3.5，绿色柱子显示 GPT-4 高出多少，以人类考生中的估计百分位来表示。"],[384.94,389.92,37,"The exams are sorted by GPT-3.5's performance.","这些考试是按 GPT-3.5 的成绩排序的。"],[390.27,399.3,37,"Look at the left side, where GPT-3.5 basically failed: AP Calculus, AMC 12, the bar exam.","看左侧，GPT-3.5 基本上都失败了：AP 微积分、AMC 12、律师资格考试。"],[399.65,402.66,37,"GPT-4 makes enormous jumps there.","GPT-4 在这些地方有巨大的飞跃。"],[403.01,410.24,37,"On the Uniform Bar Exam, it goes from around the bottom ten percent of test takers to around the top ten percent.","在统一律师资格考试上，它从考生中大约倒数百分之十，跃升到大约前百分之十。"],[410.59,415.66,37,"What this tells us is that scale doesn't only polish the easy tasks.","这告诉我们，规模并不只是在简单任务上锦上添花。"],[416.01,419.19,37,"The biggest gains often show up on the hardest ones.","最大的提升往往出现在最难的任务上。"],[419.54,426.33,37,"The message at the bottom says it well: we can expect a lot more general capability across all areas of knowledge.","底部的话说得好：我们可以期待在所有知识领域都有更多的通用能力。"],[427.58,434.59,38,"Why would a bigger model generalize better? Here's one possible explanation: combinational generalization.","为什么更大的模型泛化得更好？一个可能的解释是：组合泛化。"],[434.94,436.24,38,"Look at the simple picture.","看这张简单的图。"],[436.59,440.4,38,"During training, the model sees a white cat and a black dog.","训练时，模型看到了一只白猫和一只黑狗。"],[440.75,445.21,38,"At test time, it's asked about a black cat, which it has never seen.","测试时，它被问到一只从未见过的黑猫。"],[445.56,450.55,38,"But it has seen black, and it has seen cat, so it can combine the pieces.","但它见过“黑”，也见过“猫”，所以它可以把这些部分组合起来。"],[450.9,453.14,38,"That's combinational generalization.","这就是组合泛化。"],[453.49,455.09,38,"Now think about LLMs.","现在来想想 LLM。"],[455.44,460.83,38,"During pretraining, they've seen almost every concept, style and fact on the internet.","在预训练过程中，它们几乎见过互联网上的每一个概念、风格和事实。"],[461.18,466.59,38,"So many new test questions are really new combinations of things they've already seen.","所以很多“新”的测试问题，其实是它们已经见过的东西的新组合。"],[466.94,471.7,38,"A larger model has more capacity to store those pieces and to combine them.","更大的模型有更多的容量来存储这些部分，并把它们组合起来。"],[472.05,481.67,38,"The gray line at the bottom is an open thought: for more complex, higher-order combinations, the model may need to think longer, step by step.","底部的灰色文字是一个开放性的想法：对于更复杂、更高阶的组合，模型可能需要一步一步地思考更久。"],[482.02,486.96,38,"That's one way to see why reasoning models with long chains of thought help.","这是理解长思维链推理模型为何有效的一个角度。"],[488.21,496.31,39,"Here's another emergent effect that matters a lot for the second half of today: reinforcement learning only pays off at scale.","这是另一个对今天后半部分非常重要的涌现效应：强化学习只有在大规模时才有回报。"],[496.66,503.76,39,"This plot is from Anthropic's work on training a helpful and harmless assistant with RLHF.","这张图来自 Anthropic 用 RLHF 训练一个有用且无害的助手的工作。"],[504.11,512.0,39,"The x-axis is the number of parameters, and the y-axis is average zero-shot accuracy across tasks.","横轴是参数数量，纵轴是各任务上的平均零样本准确率。"],[512.35,518.13,39,"The blue line is a plain language model, and the orange line is the same model after RLHF.","蓝线是普通的语言模型，橙线是同一个模型经过 RLHF 之后的结果。"],[518.48,525.79,39,"In the green box, for smaller models, the orange line is below the blue line: RLHF actually hurts performance.","在绿色框里，对于较小的模型，橙线在蓝线下方：RLHF 实际上损害了性能。"],[526.14,533.42,39,"In the orange box, once the models reach roughly ten billion parameters or more, RLHF starts to help.","在橙色框里，一旦模型达到大约一百亿参数或更多，RLHF 就开始起作用。"],[533.77,540.41,39,"The intuition is that RL can only reinforce behaviors that the model is already capable of producing.","直觉是：强化学习只能强化模型本来就有能力产生的行为。"],[540.76,545.2,39,"A small model doesn't have enough underlying ability for RL to work with.","小模型没有足够的基础能力供强化学习去利用。"],[545.55,552.26,39,"Keep this in mind: it's one reason why the full ChatGPT recipe only works on top of a strong pretrained model.","请记住这一点：这是完整的 ChatGPT 配方只有建立在强大的预训练模型之上才能奏效的原因之一。"],[553.51,559.63,40,"Let me summarize the basic ingredients that make large language models possible. Everything has to be scalable.","我来总结一下让大语言模型成为可能的基本要素。一切都必须是可扩展的。"],[559.98,562.28,40,"First, a scalable architecture.","第一，可扩展的架构。"],[562.63,571.93,40,"The Transformer parallelizes across positions, unlike an RNN, and it has fewer built-in biases than a CNN, as we discussed earlier.","与 RNN 不同，Transformer 可以在各个位置上并行，而且正如前面讨论的，它比 CNN 内置的偏置更少。"],[572.28,574.53,40,"Second, a scalable objective.","第二，可扩展的目标。"],[574.88,583.88,40,"Conditional, auto-regressive language modeling, just predicting the next token, works for any text and directly gives you a generator.","条件式的自回归语言建模，也就是只预测下一个词元，适用于任何文本，并且直接给你一个生成器。"],[584.23,588.54,40,"The plot from the GPT-4 report shows how predictable it is.","GPT-4 报告中的这张图显示了它有多么可预测。"],[588.89,596.2,40,"They fit a curve on much smaller training runs, and the final GPT-4 loss, the green dot, lands right on the predicted line.","他们在小得多的训练上拟合了一条曲线，而 GPT-4 的最终损失，也就是那个绿点，正好落在预测的曲线上。"],[596.55,598.39,40,"Third, scalable data.","第三，可扩展的数据。"],[598.74,603.15,40,"Plain text is everywhere, while supervised labeled data is expensive.","纯文本无处不在，而有监督的标注数据很昂贵。"],[603.5,609.32,40,"But the last line is a warning: this fossil fuel of AI, human-written data, is running out.","但最后一行是一个警告：AI 的“化石燃料”，也就是人类撰写的数据，正在耗尽。"],[609.67,612.89,40,"We'll return to that at the very end of the lecture.","我们会在这一讲的最后再回到这个问题。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"A Case Study: From GPT-3 to ChatGPT, GPT-4 and o1","blurb":"How GPT-3 became ChatGPT, what we know about its size and training recipe, why it was hard to replicate, and where GPT-4, Sora and o1 took things.","file":"lecture05_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part4.jpg","duration":1161.8,"first":41,"last":59,"slides":[{"n":41,"title":"A case from ChatGPT","t":0.8},{"n":42,"title":"From 2020 GPT-3 to 2022 ChatGPT","t":19.9},{"n":43,"title":"Three important abilities that the initial GPT-3 exhibits","t":88.77},{"n":44,"title":"Emergence of ChatGPT","t":153.52},{"n":45,"title":"What’s ChatGPT","t":218.52},{"n":46,"title":"The Size of ChatGPT","t":278.92},{"n":47,"title":"The Size of ChatGPT","t":333.95},{"n":48,"title":"The Size of GPT4","t":396.57},{"n":49,"title":"ChatGPT Timeline","t":467.01},{"n":50,"title":"Techniques of ChatGPT","t":529.35},{"n":51,"title":"Techniques of ChatGPT","t":589.32},{"n":52,"title":"Train ChatGPT","t":652.45},{"n":53,"title":"GPT-4","t":716.52},{"n":54,"title":"Difficulties to Replicate ChatGPT","t":789.79},{"n":55,"title":"Difficulties to Replicate ChatGPT","t":858.18},{"n":56,"title":"GPT-4V","t":908.24},{"n":57,"title":"Sora","t":967.97},{"n":58,"title":"OpenAI o1","t":1032.18},{"n":59,"title":"Modern LLM Large-scale RL Looped Transformer OPD for small models","t":1093.86}],"sents":[[0.8,2.86,41,"We now understand the ingredients.","现在我们了解了这些要素。"],[3.21,9.1,41,"Let's see how they came together in practice, with the most famous case of all: ChatGPT.","我们来看看它们在实践中是如何结合在一起的，用最著名的案例：ChatGPT。"],[9.45,18.5,41,"How did OpenAI get from GPT-3 in twenty twenty to ChatGPT at the end of twenty twenty-two, and why was it so hard for others to replicate?","OpenAI 是如何从 2020 年的 GPT-3 走到 2022 年底的 ChatGPT 的？为什么别人很难复现？"],[19.75,27.29,42,"This family tree, from Yao Fu's well-known blog post, is a great map of how GPT-3 turned into ChatGPT.","这张来自符尧那篇著名博客的家谱图，很好地展示了 GPT-3 如何演变成 ChatGPT。"],[27.64,35.43,42,"Start at the top with the initial GPT-3, called davinci, trained with large-scale language model pretraining.","从顶部开始，是最初的 GPT-3，叫作 davinci，它通过大规模语言模型预训练得到。"],[35.78,38.42,42,"From there, it splits into two branches.","从这里开始，它分成了两个分支。"],[38.77,42.17,42,"On the left, training on code gives the Codex models.","左边，在代码上训练得到了 Codex 系列模型。"],[42.52,47.59,42,"On the right, instruction tuning gives the first InstructGPT models.","右边，指令微调得到了最初的 InstructGPT 模型。"],[47.94,55.16,42,"Then the branches merge: code-davinci-002 combines language modeling, code training and instruction tuning.","然后两个分支合并：code-davinci-002 结合了语言建模、代码训练和指令微调。"],[55.51,60.17,42,"This is considered the base of the GPT-3.5 series.","它被认为是 GPT-3.5 系列的基础。"],[60.52,66.24,42,"Supervised instruction tuning on top of that gives text-davinci-002.","在此基础上进行有监督的指令微调，得到了 text-davinci-002。"],[66.59,73.48,42,"Finally, RLHF gives two siblings: text-davinci-003 and ChatGPT.","最后，RLHF 产生了两个兄弟模型：text-davinci-003 和 ChatGPT。"],[73.83,74.74,42,"Two lessons.","有两点启示。"],[75.09,81.65,42,"First, ChatGPT wasn't a single leap; it was a sequence of steps over about two and a half years.","第一，ChatGPT 不是一次飞跃，而是在大约两年半时间里的一系列步骤。"],[82.0,87.37,42,"Second, many people believe training on code is part of what improved reasoning in these models.","第二，很多人认为，在代码上训练是这些模型推理能力提升的原因之一。"],[88.62,94.47,43,"Let's look at what the original GPT-3 could already do, before any of the fine-tuning steps.","我们来看看在任何微调步骤之前，最初的 GPT-3 已经能做什么。"],[94.82,96.62,43,"It had three important abilities.","它有三种重要的能力。"],[96.97,102.22,43,"Language generation: give it a prompt, and it continues it fluently.","语言生成：给它一个提示，它就能流畅地续写下去。"],[102.57,107.88,43,"In-context learning: show it a few examples, and it does the task on a new case.","上下文学习：给它看几个例子，它就能在新的样例上完成任务。"],[108.23,111.57,43,"And world knowledge, both factual and commonsense.","还有世界知识，包括事实性知识和常识。"],[111.92,113.23,43,"Where did those come from?","这些能力是从哪里来的？"],[113.58,120.31,43,"All from large-scale pretraining: a one hundred seventy-five billion parameter model on three hundred billion tokens.","全部来自大规模预训练：一个一千七百五十亿参数的模型，在三千亿词元上训练。"],[120.66,126.72,43,"Language generation comes directly from the training objective: we trained it to generate text.","语言生成能力直接来自训练目标：我们就是训练它去生成文本的。"],[127.07,132.34,43,"World knowledge comes from the training corpus; there's nowhere else it could come from.","世界知识来自训练语料，它不可能来自别的地方。"],[132.69,135.34,43,"In-context learning is the mysterious one.","上下文学习是其中最神秘的。"],[135.69,144.01,43,"Nobody designed it, and it's still not fully understood why pretraining produces it, or why it behaves so differently from fine-tuning.","没有人设计过它，我们至今仍未完全理解为什么预训练会产生它，以及为什么它的表现和微调如此不同。"],[144.36,149.18,43,"I've put some readings here, and I especially recommend the first one, from The Gradient.","我在这里列了一些阅读材料，特别推荐第一篇，来自 The Gradient。"],[149.53,152.12,43,"It's a great topic for a final project.","这是一个很好的期末项目选题。"],[153.37,158.95,44,"And then ChatGPT launched, and the world reacted in a way nobody expected.","然后 ChatGPT 发布了，全世界的反应出乎所有人的意料。"],[159.3,165.75,44,"It reached one million users in five days, and one hundred million users in about two months.","它在五天内达到一百万用户，在大约两个月内达到一亿用户。"],[166.1,177.29,44,"Look at the green box: GPT-3 took twenty-four months to reach a million users, Netflix forty-one months, Facebook ten months, Instagram two and a half months.","看绿色的框：GPT-3 花了 24 个月才达到一百万用户，Netflix 用了 41 个月，Facebook 10 个月，Instagram 两个半月。"],[177.64,179.58,44,"ChatGPT: five days.","而 ChatGPT：只用了五天。"],[179.93,182.33,44,"The industry reaction was dramatic.","业界的反应非常剧烈。"],[182.68,185.52,44,"Google declared an internal red alert.","谷歌内部拉响了红色警报。"],[185.87,192.21,44,"It rushed out Bard, which made a mistake in its first demo, and its stock dropped by about eight percent.","它匆忙推出了 Bard，结果在首次演示中就出了错，股价下跌了约百分之八。"],[192.56,198.43,44,"Microsoft invested ten billion dollars in OpenAI, and built ChatGPT into Bing and Office.","微软向 OpenAI 投资了一百亿美元，并把 ChatGPT 集成进了 Bing 和 Office。"],[198.78,208.52,44,"And here in China, it triggered what people called the battle of a hundred models, as almost every big company and many startups raced to build their own.","在中国，它引发了所谓的“百模大战”，几乎每家大公司和许多创业公司都争相打造自己的模型。"],[208.87,215.21,44,"The interesting question is why ChatGPT exploded, when GPT-3 had been available for two years.","有趣的问题是：GPT-3 已经推出两年了，为什么偏偏是 ChatGPT 引爆了？"],[215.56,217.12,44,"Let's look at that next.","我们接下来就看看这个问题。"],[218.37,224.8,45,"Let's see what OpenAI itself highlighted as ChatGPT's main features in its launch blog.","我们来看看 OpenAI 在发布博客中强调的 ChatGPT 的主要特性。"],[225.15,227.13,45,"It can answer follow-up questions.","它能回答追问。"],[227.48,229.27,45,"It can admit its mistakes.","它能承认自己的错误。"],[229.62,232.35,45,"It can challenge incorrect premises.","它能质疑错误的前提。"],[232.7,236.83,45,"And it can reject inappropriate requests.","它还能拒绝不恰当的请求。"],[237.18,241.56,45,"Notice that none of these is about knowing more facts or being better at math.","注意，这些特性没有一个是关于知道更多事实或者更擅长数学的。"],[241.91,244.43,45,"GPT-3 already had a lot of knowledge.","GPT-3 本来就已经有很多知识了。"],[244.78,250.21,45,"These four features are all about interaction: behaving like a helpful, honest conversation partner.","这四个特性都是关于交互的：表现得像一个乐于助人、诚实的对话伙伴。"],[250.56,259.83,45,"If you ask why Einstein won the Nobel Prize for relativity, a good assistant should correct you, because he actually won it for the photoelectric effect.","如果你问“爱因斯坦为什么因相对论获得诺贝尔奖”，一个好的助手应该纠正你，因为他实际上是因光电效应获奖的。"],[260.18,262.65,45,"That's the real breakthrough of ChatGPT.","这才是 ChatGPT 真正的突破。"],[263.0,269.49,45,"It's less a breakthrough in raw capability, and more a breakthrough in alignment and user experience.","与其说是原始能力上的突破，不如说是对齐和用户体验上的突破。"],[269.84,277.52,45,"And that's exactly what SFT and RLHF, which we'll study in the second half, are designed to deliver.","而这正是我们将在后半部分学习的 SFT 和 RLHF 所要实现的目标。"],[278.77,285.3,46,"How big is ChatGPT? OpenAI never said officially, so people had to work it out indirectly.","ChatGPT 有多大？OpenAI 从未正式公布，所以人们只能间接推算。"],[285.65,289.01,46,"The table at the top is from the GPT-3 paper.","上方的表格来自 GPT-3 论文。"],[289.36,296.92,46,"It lists eight model sizes, from one hundred twenty-five million up to one hundred seventy-five billion parameters.","它列出了八种模型规模，从一亿两千五百万到一千七百五十亿参数。"],[297.27,304.69,46,"It also gives the number of layers, the hidden size, the number of attention heads, the batch size and the learning rate.","表中还给出了层数、隐藏层维度、注意力头数、批大小和学习率。"],[305.04,311.69,46,"Look at the trend in the last two columns: as models get bigger, the batch size goes up and the learning rate goes down.","看最后两列的趋势：模型越大，批大小越大，学习率越低。"],[312.04,314.65,46,"That's a typical pattern when training large models.","这是训练大模型时的典型规律。"],[315.0,325.56,46,"Below, OpenAI's API offered four base models, Ada, Babbage, Curie and Davinci, from fastest and cheapest to most powerful and most expensive.","下方是 OpenAI 的 API 提供的四个基础模型：Ada、Babbage、Curie 和 Davinci，从最快最便宜到最强最贵。"],[325.91,328.56,46,"But it didn't say which size each one was.","但它没有说明每个模型的规模是多少。"],[328.91,332.55,46,"The next slide shows a clever way people matched them up.","下一页展示了人们把它们对应起来的一个巧妙方法。"],[333.8,339.32,47,"This is a nice piece of detective work by Leo Gao from EleutherAI.","这是 EleutherAI 的 Leo Gao 做的一项漂亮的“侦探工作”。"],[339.67,340.98,47,"The idea is simple.","思路很简单。"],[341.33,352.73,47,"The GPT-3 paper reports scores for each model size on standard benchmarks: LAMBADA perplexity and accuracy, Winogrande, HellaSwag and PIQA.","GPT-3 论文报告了每种规模的模型在标准基准上的分数：LAMBADA 困惑度和准确率、Winogrande、HellaSwag 和 PIQA。"],[353.08,360.03,47,"So he ran the same benchmarks on the API models, with the same evaluation harness, and compared.","于是他用同样的评测框架，在 API 模型上跑了同样的基准，然后进行比较。"],[360.38,365.82,47,"Look at the table. Ada's numbers sit right next to the three hundred fifty million parameter model.","看这张表。Ada 的数字和三亿五千万参数的模型非常接近。"],[366.17,368.9,47,"Babbage matches one point three billion.","Babbage 对应十三亿。"],[369.25,375.05,47,"Curie matches six point seven billion; look at the identical LAMBADA perplexity of four point zero zero.","Curie 对应六十七亿，看那个完全相同的 LAMBADA 困惑度 4.00。"],[375.4,379.03,47,"And Davinci lines up with the one hundred seventy-five billion model.","而 Davinci 与一千七百五十亿参数的模型对得上。"],[379.38,384.22,47,"As the slide says, this isn't ironclad proof, but it's very suggestive.","正如幻灯片所说，这不是铁证，但很有说服力。"],[384.57,390.23,47,"I like this example because it shows you how to reason scientifically about a closed system.","我喜欢这个例子，因为它展示了如何科学地推理一个封闭系统。"],[390.58,395.17,47,"When you can't see inside, you compare its behavior to things you do know.","当你看不到内部时，就把它的行为和你已知的东西进行比较。"],[396.42,403.35,48,"For GPT-4, we again have no official numbers, so this slide summarizes widely circulated estimates.","对于 GPT-4，我们同样没有官方数字，所以这一页汇总的是广为流传的估计。"],[403.7,406.32,48,"Please read the last line first: not confirmed.","请先读最后一行：未经证实。"],[406.67,413.79,48,"The rumor is that GPT-4 has about one point eight trillion parameters and one hundred twenty layers.","传言说 GPT-4 大约有一万八千亿参数和 120 层。"],[414.14,419.19,48,"The more important idea here is the architecture: Mixture of Experts, or MoE.","这里更重要的是架构思想：混合专家模型，也就是 MoE。"],[419.54,428.71,48,"Instead of one big feed-forward network in each layer, you have many experts, here sixteen, and a router picks only two of them for each token.","每一层不再是一个大的前馈网络，而是有很多个专家，这里是十六个，由路由器为每个词元只挑选其中两个。"],[429.06,434.06,48,"That gives you a crucial distinction between total parameters and active parameters.","这带来了一个关键区别：总参数量和激活参数量。"],[434.41,440.96,48,"The model might store one point eight trillion parameters, but each token only uses about two hundred eighty billion.","模型可能存储了一万八千亿参数，但每个词元只用到大约两千八百亿。"],[441.31,447.2,48,"So the compute per token is much lower than for a dense model of the same total size.","所以每个词元的计算量，远低于同样总规模的稠密模型。"],[447.55,451.65,48,"By the way, comparing parameters to brain neurons is a loose analogy.","顺便说一句，把参数和大脑神经元相比只是一个粗略的类比。"],[452.0,460.69,48,"The brain has around eighty-six billion neurons, but on the order of a hundred trillion synapses, and synapses are the closer analogue to parameters.","大脑约有八百六十亿个神经元，但突触的数量在百万亿量级，而突触才更接近参数的对应物。"],[461.04,465.61,48,"MoE is now standard in many open models too, like DeepSeek and Qwen.","现在 MoE 在许多开源模型中也已成为标配，比如 DeepSeek 和 Qwen。"],[466.86,468.68,49,"Let's put it all on one timeline.","我们把这些放到一条时间线上。"],[469.03,479.7,49,"On the right are the milestones: GPT-1 in June twenty eighteen, GPT-2 in February twenty nineteen, and the GPT-3 paper in May twenty twenty.","右边是各个里程碑：2018 年 6 月的 GPT-1，2019 年 2 月的 GPT-2，以及 2020 年 5 月的 GPT-3 论文。"],[480.05,488.37,49,"The GPT-3 API opened to the public in November twenty twenty-one, and InstructGPT came in January twenty twenty-two.","GPT-3 API 在 2021 年 11 月向公众开放，InstructGPT 在 2022 年 1 月发布。"],[488.72,498.75,49,"Then text-davinci-003 on November twenty-eighth, twenty twenty-two, and ChatGPT just two days later, on November thirtieth.","然后是 2022 年 11 月 28 日的 text-davinci-003，而仅仅两天后，11 月 30 日，ChatGPT 发布。"],[499.1,502.74,49,"The picture on the left summarizes the recipe as layers.","左边的图把这套配方概括成了几层。"],[503.09,505.02,49,"GPT-3 is the base.","GPT-3 是基础。"],[505.37,510.47,49,"Add RLHF with human labelers, and you get InstructGPT.","加上由人类标注员参与的 RLHF，就得到了 InstructGPT。"],[510.82,515.61,49,"Add a further safety layer and train for dialogue, and you get ChatGPT.","再加一层安全措施，并针对对话进行训练，就得到了 ChatGPT。"],[515.96,521.4,49,"So ChatGPT is really GPT-3, plus years of careful work on top.","所以 ChatGPT 实际上就是 GPT-3，再加上在其之上多年的精心打磨。"],[521.75,527.95,49,"Remember these three layers, because the second half of the lecture walks through each of them.","记住这三层，因为这一讲的后半部分会逐一讲解它们。"],[529.2,534.15,50,"Let's state the ChatGPT recipe explicitly, in three phases.","我们来明确地写出 ChatGPT 的配方，分为三个阶段。"],[534.5,542.12,50,"Phase 1 is pretraining, where the model learns general world knowledge and abilities from huge amounts of text.","第一阶段是预训练，模型从海量文本中学习通用的世界知识和能力。"],[542.47,546.94,50,"Phase 2 is supervised fine-tuning, which tailors the model to tasks.","第二阶段是监督微调，让模型适应各种任务。"],[547.29,548.9,50,"I like the word unlock here.","我很喜欢这里“解锁”这个词。"],[549.25,555.47,50,"SFT mostly unlocks abilities the model already gained in pretraining, rather than teaching brand-new ones.","SFT 主要是解锁模型在预训练中已经获得的能力，而不是教它全新的能力。"],[555.82,560.77,50,"Phase 3 is RLHF, which tailors the model to humans and their preferences.","第三阶段是 RLHF，让模型适应人类及其偏好。"],[561.12,568.33,50,"Even you can contribute: every time you click thumbs-up or thumbs-down in ChatGPT, that's potential human feedback.","就连你也可以贡献：每次你在 ChatGPT 里点赞或点踩，都可能成为人类反馈。"],[568.68,573.81,50,"As the note at the bottom says, most of this was already explored in InstructGPT.","正如底部的说明所说，这些大部分已经在 InstructGPT 中探索过了。"],[574.16,579.19,50,"ChatGPT's main difference was training on chat data, plus a lot of product engineering.","ChatGPT 的主要区别在于用对话数据进行训练，再加上大量的产品工程。"],[579.54,587.92,50,"The citation for Toolformer is a hint of what came next: models that learn to call tools by themselves.","Toolformer 的引用暗示了接下来的方向：模型自己学会调用工具。"],[589.17,592.32,51,"Here's the classic three-step diagram from OpenAI.","这是 OpenAI 经典的三步示意图。"],[592.67,597.22,51,"You'll see it again in the RLHF section, so let's make sure it's clear.","在 RLHF 部分你还会再看到它，所以我们先把它弄清楚。"],[597.57,602.08,51,"Step 1: collect demonstration data and train a supervised policy.","第一步：收集示范数据，训练一个监督策略。"],[602.43,609.27,51,"A prompt like, explain the moon landing to a six-year-old, is sampled, and a human labeler writes a good answer.","先采样一个提示，比如“向一个六岁孩子解释登月”，然后由人类标注员写出一个好的回答。"],[609.62,614.98,51,"Then we fine-tune GPT-3 on these examples. That's SFT.","然后我们用这些样例对 GPT-3 进行微调。这就是 SFT。"],[615.33,619.5,51,"Step 2: collect comparison data and train a reward model.","第二步：收集比较数据，训练一个奖励模型。"],[619.85,625.15,51,"For the same prompt, the model generates several answers, A, B, C, D.","对于同一个提示，模型生成几个回答：A、B、C、D。"],[625.5,631.75,51,"A labeler ranks them, for example: D better than C, better than A, which equals B.","标注员对它们进行排序，例如：D 优于 C，C 优于 A，A 与 B 相当。"],[632.1,635.83,51,"A reward model learns to predict those rankings.","奖励模型学习去预测这些排序。"],[636.18,642.71,51,"Step 3: optimize the policy against the reward model with reinforcement learning, specifically PPO.","第三步：用强化学习，具体来说是 PPO，针对奖励模型优化策略。"],[643.06,651.05,51,"A new prompt comes in, the model writes an answer, the reward model scores it, and that score is used to update the model.","来了一个新的提示，模型写出回答，奖励模型给它打分，这个分数再被用来更新模型。"],[652.3,656.38,52,"Andrej Karpathy also has a more practical view of the same pipeline.","Andrej Karpathy 对同一流程还有一个更偏实践的视角。"],[656.73,661.35,52,"I love it because it includes how often each step happens.","我很喜欢它，因为它还标出了每一步多久进行一次。"],[661.7,664.81,52,"Stage 1 is pretraining, done roughly once a year.","第一阶段是预训练，大约一年做一次。"],[665.16,670.97,52,"Download about ten terabytes of text, and get a cluster of about six thousand GPUs.","下载大约 10 TB 的文本，准备一个大约六千块 GPU 的集群。"],[671.32,676.42,52,"Pay around two million dollars, wait about twelve days, and you get a base model.","花费大约两百万美元，等待大约十二天，你就得到了一个基础模型。"],[676.77,680.09,52,"Stage 2 is fine-tuning, done roughly every week.","第二阶段是微调，大约每周做一次。"],[680.44,689.49,52,"Write labeling instructions, hire people or use a labeling company, and collect around one hundred thousand high-quality ideal responses or comparisons.","编写标注说明，雇人或使用标注公司，收集大约十万条高质量的理想回答或比较数据。"],[689.84,694.29,52,"Fine-tune the base model, which takes about a day, and you get an assistant model.","对基础模型进行微调，大约需要一天，你就得到了一个助手模型。"],[694.64,703.55,52,"Then run lots of evaluations, deploy, monitor, collect the cases where the model misbehaves, and go back to step one.","然后进行大量评估、部署、监控，收集模型表现不佳的案例，再回到第一步。"],[703.9,709.18,52,"The big takeaway: pretraining is expensive and rare, while fine-tuning is cheap and iterative.","最重要的结论是：预训练昂贵且很少进行，而微调便宜且不断迭代。"],[709.53,715.12,52,"That's why most product improvements you see actually come from the second stage.","这就是为什么你看到的大多数产品改进，其实都来自第二阶段。"],[716.37,719.35,53,"Then came GPT-4. What was new?","然后 GPT-4 来了。它有什么新东西？"],[719.7,727.05,53,"Better multilingual ability: it could answer thousands of multiple-choice questions across twenty-six languages with high accuracy.","更好的多语言能力：它能以很高的准确率回答 26 种语言的数千道选择题。"],[727.4,735.73,53,"A much longer memory: ChatGPT handled about four thousand tokens, while GPT-4 offered up to about thirty-two thousand.","更长的记忆：ChatGPT 能处理大约四千个词元，而 GPT-4 最多可达约三万二千个。"],[736.08,739.63,53,"That's enough for a short story of around thirty-two pages.","这足够容纳一篇大约 32 页的短篇小说。"],[739.98,744.43,53,"And multimodal input: it could take images as well as text.","还有多模态输入：它既能接收文本，也能接收图像。"],[744.78,748.3,53,"The technical report is notable for what it doesn't say.","这份技术报告值得注意的，恰恰是它没有说的东西。"],[748.65,759.14,53,"Read the quote: because of competition and safety, it contains no details about architecture, model size, hardware, compute, data or training method.","读一下这段引文：出于竞争和安全考虑，报告中没有关于架构、模型规模、硬件、算力、数据或训练方法的任何细节。"],[759.49,762.96,53,"That was a turning point for openness in the field.","这是这个领域开放性的一个转折点。"],[763.31,771.79,53,"On capability, there's the bar exam result we saw earlier: around the top ten percent, versus the bottom ten percent for ChatGPT.","在能力方面，就是我们之前看到的律师考试成绩：大约前百分之十，而 ChatGPT 是倒数百分之十。"],[772.14,775.72,53,"And on safety, over fifty experts tested it.","在安全方面，有五十多位专家对它进行了测试。"],[776.07,783.56,53,"After training was finished in August twenty twenty-two, they spent about seven months on safety and alignment before releasing it.","在 2022 年 8 月训练完成之后，他们花了大约七个月时间做安全和对齐，然后才发布。"],[783.91,788.39,53,"That tells you how seriously alignment is taken at the frontier.","这说明前沿机构对对齐有多么重视。"],[789.64,796.33,54,"So why was ChatGPT so hard to replicate, at least at first? Here are the main obstacles.","那么为什么 ChatGPT 很难复现，至少在一开始？这里是主要的障碍。"],[796.68,800.63,54,"Compute: money is all you need, as the joke goes.","算力：就像那个玩笑说的，你只需要钱。"],[800.98,809.56,54,"Data and annotation: you need very careful cleaning, filtering and selection, because training is too expensive to waste on bad data.","数据和标注：你需要非常仔细的清洗、过滤和筛选，因为训练太昂贵了，不能浪费在糟糕的数据上。"],[809.91,814.06,54,"Plain corpora and transferable SFT data can be shared.","纯文本语料和可迁移的 SFT 数据是可以共享的。"],[814.41,823.38,54,"But human feedback data is model-dependent: preferences collected on one model's outputs don't transfer cleanly to another model.","但人类反馈数据是依赖于模型的：在一个模型输出上收集的偏好，无法干净地迁移到另一个模型。"],[823.73,831.39,54,"Algorithms: the general methods are open, but the engineering, the training tricks and efficient deployment, is hard.","算法：通用的方法是公开的，但工程实现，包括训练技巧和高效部署，是很难的。"],[831.74,836.54,54,"And as the slide says, releasing a model is easy; keeping it polished is not.","正如幻灯片所说，发布一个模型很容易，持续打磨它却不容易。"],[836.89,844.28,54,"And talent: OpenAI's team was described as first-tier young researchers, with an average age around thirty-two.","还有人才：OpenAI 的团队被描述为一流的年轻研究者，平均年龄大约 32 岁。"],[844.63,849.28,54,"Note the comment at the bottom: this analysis is a bit dated.","注意底部的说明：这个分析有点过时了。"],[849.63,856.78,54,"Today, Chinese labs are essentially on the same line as OpenAI, as we saw at the start of the lecture.","今天，中国的实验室基本上已经和 OpenAI 站在同一条起跑线上了，正如我们在这一讲开头看到的那样。"],[858.03,863.14,55,"I want to leave you with one question from that list, because I think it's underrated.","我想把那份清单中的一个问题留给大家，因为我觉得它被低估了。"],[863.49,867.99,55,"How do you efficiently organize young, high-density talent?","如何高效地组织年轻、高密度的人才？"],[868.34,871.36,55,"Building an LLM isn't just a technical problem.","构建 LLM 不仅仅是一个技术问题。"],[871.71,882.26,55,"It needs tight collaboration between people who understand data, infrastructure, algorithms and evaluation, moving fast and making decisions together.","它需要懂数据、基础设施、算法和评测的人紧密合作，快速推进，共同决策。"],[882.61,891.24,55,"Several of the most successful labs, here and abroad, are known for small, young, very dense teams, rather than huge organizations.","国内外好几个最成功的实验室，都以小而年轻、人才密度极高的团队著称，而不是庞大的组织。"],[891.59,893.21,55,"That's encouraging for you.","这对你们来说是个鼓舞。"],[893.56,898.48,55,"Many of the people who built these systems were not much older than you are now.","构建这些系统的很多人，并不比现在的你们大多少。"],[898.83,906.84,55,"So take this as a hint about the kind of people, and the kind of teams, that will matter in the next few years.","所以请把这当作一个提示：未来几年，什么样的人、什么样的团队会变得重要。"],[908.09,916.32,56,"After ChatGPT and GPT-4, the frontier kept expanding. First, into vision: GPT-4V.","在 ChatGPT 和 GPT-4 之后，前沿继续扩展。首先是视觉：GPT-4V。"],[916.67,919.94,56,"As with GPT-4, the model details are unknown.","和 GPT-4 一样，模型细节是未知的。"],[920.29,928.1,56,"But the capability was striking: strong zero-shot visual understanding and reasoning on real user tasks in the wild.","但它的能力令人惊叹：在真实场景的用户任务上，具有很强的零样本视觉理解和推理能力。"],[928.45,930.2,56,"Look at the two examples.","看这两个例子。"],[930.55,940.62,56,"On the left, asked what's unusual about the image, it explains that a man is ironing clothes on an ironing board attached to the roof of a moving taxi.","左边，被问到这张图有什么不寻常之处时，它解释说：一个男人正在一块固定在行驶中出租车车顶的熨衣板上熨衣服。"],[940.97,943.26,56,"On the right, it explains a meme.","右边，它解释了一个表情包。"],[943.61,952.07,56,"The text promises a beautiful picture of the Earth from space, but the image is chicken nuggets arranged to look like a world map.","文字说的是一张从太空看地球的美丽照片，但图片却是一些摆成世界地图形状的鸡块。"],[952.42,955.05,56,"And the humor comes from that mismatch.","幽默就来自这种反差。"],[955.4,959.0,56,"Getting a joke requires both perception and commonsense.","理解一个笑话既需要感知，也需要常识。"],[959.35,966.57,56,"The question in pink, how can we build multimodal GPT-4-like models, is exactly what we'll answer in Lecture 10.","粉色的问题，如何构建类似 GPT-4 的多模态模型，正是我们将在第十讲回答的。"],[967.82,975.43,57,"Then video: Sora, which OpenAI described as video generation models as world simulators.","然后是视频：Sora，OpenAI 称之为“作为世界模拟器的视频生成模型”。"],[975.78,981.87,57,"It can generate high-quality videos from text, edit videos with text, and extend videos.","它可以根据文本生成高质量视频，用文本编辑视频，还能延长视频。"],[982.22,989.41,57,"It can also produce high-resolution images, and handle different durations, resolutions and aspect ratios.","它还能生成高分辨率图像，并处理不同的时长、分辨率和宽高比。"],[989.76,996.25,57,"The diagram at the bottom shows the trick, and it connects directly to what we'll discuss today about tokens.","底部的图展示了其中的诀窍，它和我们今天要讨论的词元直接相关。"],[996.6,1001.88,57,"A visual encoder compresses the video into a compact latent representation.","视觉编码器把视频压缩成一个紧凑的潜在表示。"],[1002.23,1011.14,57,"That representation is then cut into small spacetime patches, little cubes covering a region of the image over a short time.","然后这个表示被切分成小的时空块，也就是覆盖图像某个区域、持续一小段时间的小立方体。"],[1011.49,1017.51,57,"Those patches are flattened into a sequence, just like words in a sentence, and fed to a Transformer.","这些块被展平成一个序列，就像句子中的单词一样，然后输入 Transformer。"],[1017.86,1027.07,57,"So the same idea that powers language models, turning the input into a sequence of tokens and scaling a Transformer on it, works for video too.","所以驱动语言模型的同一个思想，也就是把输入变成词元序列并在上面扩展 Transformer，对视频也同样有效。"],[1027.42,1030.78,57,"That's why the title talks about world simulators.","这就是为什么标题说的是世界模拟器。"],[1032.03,1039.48,58,"The next big step, in late twenty twenty-four, was OpenAI o1, the first widely used reasoning model.","下一个重大进展是 2024 年底的 OpenAI o1，第一个被广泛使用的推理模型。"],[1039.83,1041.0,58,"Look at the screenshot.","看这张截图。"],[1041.35,1047.46,58,"The user asks a complex question about why climate-friendly behaviors are slow to spread.","用户问了一个复杂的问题：为什么对气候友好的行为推广得很慢。"],[1047.81,1054.61,58,"Before answering, the model shows: thought for eight seconds, with a summary of its thinking.","在回答之前，模型显示“思考了 8 秒”，并附上了思考过程的摘要。"],[1054.96,1059.8,58,"Understanding the barriers, examining them, then thinking about interventions.","理解障碍，审视障碍，然后思考干预措施。"],[1060.15,1068.66,58,"That's the key change: the model spends extra computation at test time, generating a long internal chain of thought before giving the final answer.","这是关键的变化：模型在测试时花费额外的计算，在给出最终答案之前，先生成一条很长的内部思维链。"],[1069.01,1074.54,58,"And it was trained with reinforcement learning to make that thinking useful.","而且它是用强化学习训练的，让这种思考变得有用。"],[1074.89,1081.81,58,"This opened up a new kind of scaling: not just bigger models and more data, but more thinking at inference time.","这开启了一种新的扩展方式：不只是更大的模型和更多的数据，而是在推理时进行更多思考。"],[1082.16,1087.24,58,"DeepSeek-R1 later showed an open recipe for the same idea.","后来 DeepSeek-R1 给出了同一思路的开源配方。"],[1087.59,1092.46,58,"This is a main topic of Lecture 6, on RL for LLM post-training.","这是第六讲的主要内容，也就是用于大模型后训练的强化学习。"],[1093.71,1098.61,59,"So what does a modern LLM look like today? Here are three trends I'd point to.","那么今天的现代 LLM 是什么样的？我想指出三个趋势。"],[1098.96,1101.29,59,"First, large-scale RL.","第一，大规模强化学习。"],[1101.64,1108.18,59,"After o1 and DeepSeek-R1, reinforcement learning is no longer a small final polish.","在 o1 和 DeepSeek-R1 之后，强化学习不再只是最后的一点小打磨。"],[1108.53,1115.02,59,"It's a major training stage that uses huge amounts of compute, especially for reasoning and agentic tasks.","它是一个使用大量算力的主要训练阶段，尤其是针对推理和智能体任务。"],[1115.37,1117.73,59,"Second, the looped Transformer.","第二，循环 Transformer。"],[1118.08,1122.78,59,"Instead of stacking more and more distinct layers, you reuse the same block several times.","不是堆叠越来越多不同的层，而是把同一个模块重复使用多次。"],[1123.13,1128.22,59,"So the model can do more computation per token, without more parameters.","这样模型可以在不增加参数的情况下，对每个词元做更多计算。"],[1128.57,1132.99,59,"It's a way of adding depth, a bit like thinking longer inside the network.","这是一种增加深度的方式，有点像在网络内部思考得更久。"],[1133.34,1138.15,59,"Third, OPD, on-policy distillation, for small models.","第三，用于小模型的 OPD，也就是同策略蒸馏。"],[1138.5,1146.37,59,"A small student model generates its own answers, and a strong teacher gives feedback on exactly those answers, token by token.","一个小的学生模型生成自己的回答，由一个强大的教师模型针对这些回答，逐个词元地给出反馈。"],[1146.72,1156.24,59,"It combines the dense supervision of distillation with the on-policy nature of RL, and it's an efficient way to make small models strong.","它结合了蒸馏的稠密监督和强化学习的同策略特性，是让小模型变强的一种高效方法。"],[1156.59,1159.96,59,"You'll hear much more about all three in the next lectures.","在接下来的几讲中，你们会听到更多关于这三点的内容。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"Using LLMs, Level 1: Prompt Engineering and Agents","blurb":"The cheapest way to use an LLM: prompt engineering, tool-using agents and frameworks such as LangChain, Dify, Manus and OpenClaw, plus the homework.","file":"lecture05_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part5.jpg","duration":598.4,"first":60,"last":71,"slides":[{"n":60,"title":"How to use LLMs? prompt Engineering, model fine-tuning and training from scratch","t":0.8},{"n":61,"title":"How to use LLMs? Level 1: Prompt Engineering and agents","t":36.19},{"n":62,"title":"Prompt Engineering","t":57.59},{"n":63,"title":"Agent","t":118.73},{"n":64,"title":"Agent: Tool use","t":178.32},{"n":65,"title":"LangChain","t":252.69},{"n":66,"title":"DIFY （https://dify.ai/）","t":317.13},{"n":67,"title":"Manus","t":370.51},{"n":68,"title":"OpenClaw 大龙虾","t":425.06},{"n":69,"title":"Homework","t":477.45},{"n":70,"title":"How to use LLMs? Level 2: Model Training","t":527.73},{"n":71,"title":"Agents vs. train your own models","t":545.77}],"sents":[[0.8,7.29,60,"We've seen what LLMs are, why size matters, and how ChatGPT came about.","我们已经了解了 LLM 是什么、规模为什么重要，以及 ChatGPT 是如何诞生的。"],[7.64,11.96,60,"Now a practical question: how can you actually use LLMs?","现在来看一个实际问题：你到底该如何使用 LLM？"],[12.31,18.17,60,"Roughly, there are three levels: prompt engineering, fine-tuning, and training from scratch.","大致有三个层次：提示工程、微调，以及从零训练。"],[18.52,21.25,60,"You'll notice I've crossed out training from scratch.","你会注意到，我把“从零训练”划掉了。"],[21.6,25.96,60,"That's not because it's unimportant, since it's the subject of the second half today.","这不是因为它不重要，因为它正是今天后半部分的主题。"],[26.31,32.4,60,"It's because, for almost everyone outside a few big labs, it's simply not realistic.","而是因为对少数几个大实验室之外的几乎所有人来说，这根本不现实。"],[32.75,34.79,60,"Let's start with the easiest level.","我们从最简单的层次开始。"],[36.04,39.12,61,"Level 1 is prompt engineering and agents.","第一层是提示工程和智能体。"],[39.47,44.23,61,"Here you treat the model as a fixed black box: you never touch its weights.","在这里，你把模型当作一个固定的黑盒：你从不触碰它的权重。"],[44.58,49.66,61,"You only control what goes in, and what tools and environment it can act on.","你只控制输入什么内容，以及它可以使用哪些工具、在什么环境中行动。"],[50.01,56.19,61,"That's how most people and most companies use LLMs today, so let's see what it looks like.","这是今天大多数人和大多数公司使用 LLM 的方式，我们来看看它是什么样子。"],[57.44,63.85,62,"Prompt engineering means using an LLM out of the box, without changing any model parameters.","提示工程指的是开箱即用地使用 LLM，不改变任何模型参数。"],[64.2,65.68,62,"There are two ways to do it.","有两种方式。"],[66.03,73.1,62,"The easy way, on the left, is just talking to ChatGPT or a similar app in the chat window.","左边是简单的方式：直接在聊天窗口里和 ChatGPT 或类似的应用对话。"],[73.45,80.96,62,"The less easy way, on the right, is calling the model from your own code through an API, like the OpenAI API.","右边是不那么简单的方式：在自己的代码里通过 API 调用模型，比如 OpenAI API。"],[81.31,85.51,62,"Or downloading an open model from Hugging Face and running it yourself.","或者从 Hugging Face 下载开源模型，自己运行。"],[85.86,92.06,62,"That's what you'd do to build a product, or to run an experiment on thousands of examples.","如果你要做一个产品，或者在成千上万个样例上做实验，就会用这种方式。"],[92.41,96.06,62,"And look at the little joke in the screenshot.","再看看截图里的小笑话。"],[96.41,99.36,62,"The user asks: how do I prompt engineer?","用户问：我该如何做提示工程？"],[99.71,104.5,62,"And the model answers: to prompt an engineer effectively, follow these guidelines.","而模型回答：要有效地督促一位工程师，请遵循以下准则。"],[104.85,108.76,62,"It read prompt as a verb, and engineer as a person!","它把 prompt 当成了动词，把 engineer 当成了一个人！"],[109.11,117.33,62,"A nice reminder that how you phrase your prompt really matters, and that ambiguity is still a thing, even for big models.","这很好地提醒我们，提示的措辞真的很重要，而且即使对大模型来说，歧义依然存在。"],[118.58,121.47,63,"Going beyond single prompts, we get agents.","超越单个提示，我们就来到了智能体。"],[121.82,127.84,63,"This diagram, popularized by Lilian Weng, is the standard picture of an LLM agent.","这张由 Lilian Weng 推广的图，是 LLM 智能体的标准示意图。"],[128.19,135.2,63,"The LLM sits in the middle as the decision center, doing the reasoning, and it's also the front end that chats with the human.","LLM 位于中间，作为决策中心负责推理，同时也是与人类聊天的前端。"],[135.55,137.93,63,"Around it are four components.","它周围有四个组件。"],[138.28,147.76,63,"Memory: short-term memory is basically the context window, and long-term memory is an external store, like a database the agent can write to and read from.","记忆：短期记忆基本上就是上下文窗口，长期记忆则是外部存储，比如智能体可以读写的数据库。"],[148.11,152.74,63,"Tools: calendar, calculator, code interpreter, search, and more.","工具：日历、计算器、代码解释器、搜索等等。"],[153.09,159.68,63,"Planning: breaking a goal into subgoals, chain-of-thought, reflection, and self-criticism.","规划：把目标分解成子目标、思维链、反思和自我批评。"],[160.03,165.14,63,"And action: actually doing something in the world, like calling an API or running code.","还有行动：在世界中真正做一些事情，比如调用 API 或运行代码。"],[165.49,168.26,63,"Remember OpenClaw from the beginning of the lecture?","还记得这一讲开头的 OpenClaw 吗？"],[168.61,173.11,63,"Every feature in its list maps onto one of these boxes.","它列出的每一个功能，都能对应到这些方框中的一个。"],[173.46,176.92,63,"This framework will be the backbone of Lecture 7.","这个框架将是第七讲的主干。"],[178.17,181.41,64,"Let's look at two concrete examples of tool use.","我们来看两个具体的工具使用例子。"],[181.76,184.15,64,"On the left is HuggingGPT.","左边是 HuggingGPT。"],[184.5,190.73,64,"ChatGPT acts as the controller, and the tools are the thousands of models hosted on Hugging Face.","ChatGPT 充当控制器，而工具就是 Hugging Face 上托管的成千上万个模型。"],[191.08,197.45,64,"Follow the four steps. The user asks it to describe a picture and count the objects.","跟着这四个步骤走。用户让它描述一张图片，并数一数里面有多少个物体。"],[197.8,202.66,64,"First, task planning: it decides it needs captioning and object detection.","第一步，任务规划：它判断需要图像描述和目标检测。"],[203.01,211.6,64,"Second, model selection: it picks suitable models, like a DETR detector and an image-captioning model, based on their descriptions.","第二步，模型选择：它根据模型描述，挑选合适的模型，比如 DETR 检测器和一个图像描述模型。"],[211.95,215.76,64,"Third, task execution: those models run.","第三步，任务执行：运行这些模型。"],[216.11,225.43,64,"Fourth, response generation: it combines their outputs into one answer, a herd of giraffes and zebras, plus five detected objects.","第四步，响应生成：它把这些输出整合成一个回答，“一群长颈鹿和斑马”，外加五个检测到的物体。"],[225.78,238.91,64,"On the right is API-Bank, a benchmark for tool-augmented LLMs, with fifty-three common API tools, two hundred sixty-four annotated dialogues and five hundred sixty-eight API calls.","右边是 API-Bank，一个面向工具增强 LLM 的基准，包含 53 个常用 API 工具、264 段标注对话和 568 次 API 调用。"],[239.26,241.4,64,"The algorithm box shows the loop.","算法框展示了这个循环。"],[241.75,251.29,64,"Search for the right API, read its documentation, generate a call, execute it, and repeat until the response is good enough.","搜索合适的 API，阅读它的文档，生成调用，执行调用，然后重复，直到响应足够好为止。"],[252.54,256.33,65,"If you want to build such applications yourself, frameworks help.","如果你想自己构建这样的应用，框架会很有帮助。"],[256.68,264.76,65,"LangChain was one of the first popular ones; you can see it had more than sixty thousand stars on GitHub when I took this screenshot.","LangChain 是最早流行起来的框架之一，你可以看到我截图时它在 GitHub 上已经有六万多颗星。"],[265.11,269.48,65,"Its core building block is the LLMChain, which combines three things.","它的核心构建模块是 LLMChain，它组合了三样东西。"],[269.83,273.29,65,"The LLM itself, as the reasoning engine.","LLM 本身，作为推理引擎。"],[273.64,278.39,65,"A prompt template, which fills your variables into a fixed instruction.","提示模板，把你的变量填入一个固定的指令中。"],[278.74,285.86,65,"And an output parser, which turns the model's free-text answer into something structured your program can use.","以及输出解析器，把模型的自由文本回答转换成程序可以使用的结构化内容。"],[286.21,291.55,65,"The diagram at the bottom shows it nicely: format, predict, parse.","底部的图很好地展示了这一点：格式化、预测、解析。"],[291.9,299.95,65,"The variables x equals foo and y equals bar are inserted into the template: does x like y, and why?","变量 x 等于 foo、y 等于 bar，被插入到模板“x 喜欢 y 吗？为什么？”中。"],[300.3,308.62,65,"The model predicts an answer, and the parser turns it into a JSON object, with likes set to true, and a reason.","模型预测出一个回答，解析器再把它转换成一个 JSON 对象，其中 likes 为 True，并附上理由。"],[308.97,315.73,65,"That pattern, template in, structured data out, is the basis of most LLM applications.","这种模式，模板输入、结构化数据输出，是大多数 LLM 应用的基础。"],[316.98,323.93,66,"Here's another tool in the same family: Dify, an open-source platform for building generative AI applications.","这是同类中的另一个工具：Dify，一个用于构建生成式 AI 应用的开源平台。"],[324.28,330.25,66,"Compared with LangChain, which is a code library, Dify is more of a visual, low-code workspace.","与作为代码库的 LangChain 相比，Dify 更像是一个可视化的低代码工作台。"],[330.6,332.11,66,"Look at the feature boxes.","看这些功能方框。"],[332.46,341.43,66,"An orchestration studio where you design apps visually, a RAG pipeline to connect your own documents, and a prompt IDE for testing prompts.","可视化设计应用的编排工作室，连接你自己文档的 RAG 流水线，以及用于测试提示的提示词 IDE。"],[341.78,349.37,66,"LLMOps for monitoring and improving models, backend-as-a-service APIs, LLM agents, and workflows.","用于监控和改进模型的 LLMOps、后端即服务的 API、LLM 智能体，以及工作流。"],[349.72,350.54,66,"Why show it?","为什么要展示它？"],[350.89,359.69,66,"Because it's a good example of how much of LLM application development is now about assembling building blocks, rather than training models.","因为它很好地说明了，如今 LLM 应用开发在很大程度上是组装积木，而不是训练模型。"],[360.04,369.11,66,"Many of you could build a decent customer-service bot over your own documents in an afternoon with something like this, without writing much code.","你们中的很多人用这类工具，一个下午就能基于自己的文档搭建一个像样的客服机器人，而且不用写多少代码。"],[370.36,372.54,67,"Manus took agents a step further.","Manus 让智能体又向前迈进了一步。"],[372.89,380.09,67,"It went viral in twenty twenty-five as a general-purpose agent that can complete whole tasks on its own.","它在 2025 年走红，是一个能够独立完成整项任务的通用智能体。"],[380.44,385.18,67,"The key idea is in the subtitle: a server-side computer-use sandbox.","关键思想就在副标题里：服务端的计算机使用沙箱。"],[385.53,392.84,67,"Look at the diagram. Each task, Task 1, Task 2, Task 3, gets its own virtual computer in the cloud.","看这张图。每个任务，任务一、任务二、任务三，都在云端拥有自己的一台虚拟电脑。"],[393.19,402.44,67,"Inside that sandbox, the agent can open a terminal, run code, browse the web, and create PDFs, spreadsheets and documents.","在这个沙箱里，智能体可以打开终端、运行代码、浏览网页，并创建 PDF、表格和文档。"],[402.79,407.29,67,"You give it a goal, it works for a while, and it comes back with the finished files.","你给它一个目标，它工作一段时间，然后把完成的文件交给你。"],[407.64,409.94,67,"Running in the cloud has advantages.","在云端运行有它的优势。"],[410.29,417.51,67,"It's isolated from your own machine, so mistakes don't damage your files, and you can run many tasks in parallel.","它与你自己的电脑隔离，所以出错也不会损坏你的文件，而且你可以并行运行很多任务。"],[417.86,423.66,67,"The downside is that it doesn't have access to your personal environment unless you upload things.","缺点是，除非你上传东西，否则它无法访问你的个人环境。"],[424.91,432.24,68,"OpenClaw, nicknamed big lobster in Chinese, takes the opposite approach: it's a locally deployed personal assistant.","OpenClaw，中文昵称“大龙虾”，走的是相反的路线：它是一个本地部署的个人助手。"],[432.59,441.52,68,"Instead of a sandbox in someone else's cloud, it runs on your own computer, with your files, your browser, and your accounts.","它不是在别人云端的沙箱里，而是运行在你自己的电脑上，使用你的文件、你的浏览器和你的账户。"],[441.87,445.11,68,"And it talks to you through your usual chat apps.","它还通过你常用的聊天软件和你交流。"],[445.46,449.41,68,"That's what makes it so useful, since it can act on your real environment.","这正是它如此有用的原因，因为它可以在你真实的环境中行动。"],[449.76,458.88,68,"It's also what makes it a bit scary: full system access means a mistake or a malicious instruction could do real damage.","这也是它有点吓人的地方：完整的系统访问权限意味着一次失误或一条恶意指令就可能造成真正的损害。"],[459.23,465.98,68,"So we have two design points: Manus, server-side and sandboxed; OpenClaw, local and deeply personal.","所以我们有两种设计取向：Manus，服务端加沙箱；OpenClaw，本地且高度个人化。"],[466.33,476.05,68,"A lot of the engineering in agents, what we'll call harness engineering in Lecture 7, is about managing exactly this trade-off between power and safety.","智能体中的大量工程工作，也就是我们在第七讲中所说的驾驭工程，正是在处理能力与安全之间的这种权衡。"],[477.3,481.2,69,"So here's your homework: try OpenClaw yourself.","所以这是你们的作业：亲自试一试 OpenClaw。"],[481.55,488.62,69,"You don't need to pay someone four hundred ninety-nine yuan to come install it, like in that post on the right.","你不需要像右边那个帖子里那样，花 499 元请人上门安装。"],[488.97,492.29,69,"You're NLP students; you can do it yourselves.","你们是学 NLP 的学生，可以自己动手。"],[492.64,496.82,69,"Install it, connect it to a model, and give it some real tasks.","安装它，把它连接到一个模型上，然后给它一些真实的任务。"],[497.17,502.42,69,"Organize some files, summarize your emails, look something up and write a report.","整理一些文件，总结你的邮件，查一些资料并写一份报告。"],[502.77,507.29,69,"Pay attention to where it works well, where it fails, and why.","注意它在哪些地方表现好、在哪些地方失败，以及原因是什么。"],[507.64,511.43,69,"Is it the model's reasoning? The tools? The memory?","是模型的推理问题？工具问题？还是记忆问题？"],[511.78,519.43,69,"One practical warning: because it can run commands and access your accounts, start in a sandbox or a separate user account.","一个实际的提醒：因为它可以运行命令并访问你的账户，请先在沙箱或单独的用户账户中使用。"],[519.78,522.79,69,"And don't give it credentials you care about.","也不要给它你在意的账号凭证。"],[523.14,526.33,69,"Being careful with agents is part of the lesson.","谨慎地使用智能体，本身就是这门课的一部分。"],[527.58,532.05,70,"That's level 1: using models as they are, with prompts and agents.","这就是第一层：通过提示和智能体，按原样使用模型。"],[532.4,540.21,70,"Level 2 is model training: changing the weights yourself, mostly by fine-tuning an existing open model on your own data.","第二层是模型训练：自己去改变权重，主要是在自己的数据上微调一个现有的开源模型。"],[540.56,544.37,70,"Before we go there, let's compare the two paths honestly.","在此之前，我们先坦诚地比较一下这两条路。"],[545.62,550.9,71,"So which should you choose: build agents on top of existing models, or train your own?","那么你该选哪个：在现有模型之上构建智能体，还是训练你自己的模型？"],[551.25,555.03,71,"Agents are much easier to turn into robust applications.","智能体更容易做成稳健的应用。"],[555.38,559.36,71,"The big models are very strong, and you can get something working quickly.","大模型非常强，你可以很快做出能用的东西。"],[559.71,562.4,71,"The downside is the high level of abstraction.","缺点是抽象层次太高。"],[562.75,568.88,71,"You may build a great app without really understanding how LLMs are trained, or why they behave the way they do.","你可能做出了一个很棒的应用，却并不真正理解 LLM 是如何训练的，或者为什么会这样表现。"],[569.23,572.66,71,"Training your own model, the DIY route, is the opposite.","训练你自己的模型，也就是自己动手的路线，则正好相反。"],[573.01,579.88,71,"The honest downside is that it's difficult, and it may simply not work, especially with limited GPUs.","坦白说，缺点是它很难，而且可能根本做不出来，尤其是在 GPU 有限的情况下。"],[580.23,585.3,71,"The upside is that you learn much more about how LLMs actually work.","好处是，你会对 LLM 的实际工作原理有更多了解。"],[585.65,588.3,71,"For your final project, either path is fine.","对于期末项目，两条路都可以。"],[588.65,593.8,71,"But since this is an NLP course, I'd like everyone to understand what's happening inside the model.","但既然这是一门 NLP 课，我希望每个人都能理解模型内部发生了什么。"],[594.15,596.54,71,"That's the second half of today's lecture.","这就是今天这一讲的后半部分。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Training from Zero: The Pipeline and Tokenization (BPE)","blurb":"When to train your own model, the steps from zero to ChatGPT, and why subword tokenization such as BPE matters, including bad tokenizers for Chinese and Arabic.","file":"lecture05_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part6.jpg","duration":813.4,"first":72,"last":86,"slides":[{"n":72,"title":"Understanding of LLM Training","t":0.8},{"n":73,"title":"Techniques of ChatGPT","t":18.54},{"n":74,"title":"From Zero to ChatGPT","t":62.87},{"n":75,"title":"Steps of LLM training","t":120.36},{"n":76,"title":"Starts from Word Tokenization","t":181.54},{"n":77,"title":"What and Why?","t":201.03},{"n":78,"title":"Tokenization","t":257.68},{"n":79,"title":"Subword modeling","t":299.26},{"n":80,"title":"Tokenization","t":360.8},{"n":81,"title":"Subword modeling","t":423.06},{"n":82,"title":"Subword-based Tokenization Methods","t":473.38},{"n":83,"title":"Byte-pair encoding (BPE) [Gage 1994]","t":541.07},{"n":84,"title":"Example of a bad tokenizer: LLaMA for Chinese","t":615.06},{"n":85,"title":"Example of a bad tokenizer: AceGPT for Arabic","t":685.66},{"n":86,"title":"A broader sense of “token”","t":749.01}],"sents":[[0.8,4.17,72,"Welcome to part two: understanding LLM training.","欢迎来到第二部分：理解 LLM 训练。"],[4.52,8.25,72,"In part one, we treated the model mostly from the outside.","在第一部分，我们主要是从外部来看模型。"],[8.6,15.5,72,"Now the question is: if you had to build a ChatGPT-like model from nothing, what exactly would you do, step by step?","现在的问题是：如果你必须从零构建一个类似 ChatGPT 的模型，你具体要一步一步做些什么？"],[15.85,17.14,72,"Let's open the box.","我们来打开这个盒子。"],[18.39,23.73,73,"You've seen this slide before, with one addition: Phase 0, word tokenization.","这一页你们之前见过，只是多了一项：第零阶段，分词。"],[24.08,31.18,73,"Before any learning can happen, we have to decide how to cut text into pieces the model can process.","在任何学习发生之前，我们必须决定如何把文本切分成模型可以处理的片段。"],[31.53,33.23,73,"Then come the three phases.","然后是三个阶段。"],[33.58,36.89,73,"Pretraining, to learn general knowledge and abilities.","预训练，学习通用的知识和能力。"],[37.24,42.36,73,"Supervised fine-tuning, to tailor the model to tasks and unlock abilities.","监督微调，让模型适应任务并解锁能力。"],[42.71,46.31,73,"And RLHF, to tailor it to human preferences.","以及 RLHF，让模型适应人类偏好。"],[46.66,48.95,73,"This is the structure for the rest of today.","这就是今天剩下内容的结构。"],[49.3,57.82,73,"We'll go through tokenization, pretraining, SFT and RLHF in order, with practical tips for each.","我们会按顺序讲解分词、预训练、SFT 和 RLHF，并给出每一步的实用技巧。"],[58.17,61.47,73,"Keep this list in mind as our table of contents.","请把这个列表记作我们的目录。"],[62.72,69.72,74,"Now the same journey, from zero to ChatGPT, told through the data used at each step.","现在用每一步所用的数据，再讲一遍从零到 ChatGPT 的旅程。"],[70.07,73.9,74,"Lots of web text gives you davinci, the base GPT-3.","大量网页文本，得到了 davinci，也就是基础版 GPT-3。"],[74.25,78.11,74,"Lots of GitHub code gives you code-davinci-002.","大量 GitHub 代码，得到了 code-davinci-002。"],[78.46,84.51,74,"Lots of annotated data, humans writing ideal responses, gives you text-davinci-002.","大量标注数据，也就是人类撰写的理想回答，得到了 text-davinci-002。"],[84.86,91.86,74,"Human judgments of response quality, the thumbs-up and thumbs-down, give you text-davinci-003.","人类对回答质量的评判，也就是点赞和点踩，得到了 text-davinci-003。"],[92.21,99.67,74,"And chat-oriented data gives you the model behind ChatGPT, the GPT-3.5 Turbo series.","而面向对话的数据，得到了 ChatGPT 背后的模型，也就是 GPT-3.5 Turbo 系列。"],[100.02,106.25,74,"What I want you to notice is that each stage adds a new kind of data, and each kind teaches something different.","我希望大家注意的是：每个阶段都加入了一种新的数据，而每种数据教会模型不同的东西。"],[106.6,111.3,74,"Knowledge, code and reasoning, task following, preferences, and conversation.","知识、代码与推理、任务遵循、偏好，以及对话。"],[111.65,118.96,74,"When you think about training an LLM, always ask: what data is used at this stage, and what is it supposed to teach?","当你思考如何训练 LLM 时，一定要问：这个阶段用了什么数据，它要教会模型什么？"],[120.21,126.05,75,"I like to explain the steps of LLM training with an analogy to how a student learns.","我喜欢用学生学习的过程来类比 LLM 训练的各个步骤。"],[126.4,132.65,75,"Top row: a child first learns to recognize words, with picture cards like draw, think, play.","上面一行：孩子先通过识字卡片学认字，比如画画、思考、玩耍。"],[133.0,137.13,75,"Then they read textbooks, like that calculus book.","然后他们读教科书，比如那本微积分课本。"],[137.48,144.33,75,"Then they do exercises; many of you probably recognize that red practice book for the gaokao.","然后他们做练习题，很多人大概都认得那本红色的高考练习册。"],[144.68,148.57,75,"And finally, they get feedback from teachers on their answers.","最后，他们从老师那里得到对答案的反馈。"],[148.92,151.55,75,"Bottom row: the same steps for the robot.","下面一行：机器人也经历同样的步骤。"],[151.9,155.25,75,"Tokenizer training is learning to recognize words.","训练分词器，就是学认字。"],[155.6,160.32,75,"Self-supervised pretraining is reading the textbooks, a huge amount of them.","自监督预训练，就是读教科书，而且是海量的教科书。"],[160.67,165.13,75,"Instruction fine-tuning is doing exercises with reference answers.","指令微调，就是做带参考答案的练习题。"],[165.48,171.44,75,"And RLHF is getting feedback from teachers, which here means human preferences.","而 RLHF 就是得到老师的反馈，在这里指的是人类偏好。"],[171.79,175.45,75,"If you remember this picture, you'll remember the whole pipeline.","记住这张图，你就记住了整个流程。"],[175.8,180.14,75,"Let's start where the child starts: recognizing words.","我们就从孩子开始的地方开始：认字。"],[181.39,183.31,76,"First stop: tokenization.","第一站：分词。"],[183.66,189.23,76,"Before a model can read anything, we need to decide what the basic units of text are.","在模型能读任何东西之前，我们需要决定文本的基本单位是什么。"],[189.58,192.02,76,"It sounds like a boring preprocessing step.","这听起来像是一个无聊的预处理步骤。"],[192.37,199.63,76,"But as you'll see, a bad tokenizer can seriously hurt a model, especially for languages like Chinese and Arabic.","但你会看到，一个糟糕的分词器会严重损害模型，尤其是对中文和阿拉伯语这样的语言。"],[200.88,204.24,77,"So what is tokenization, and why do we need it?","那么，什么是分词？我们为什么需要它？"],[204.59,213.95,77,"Tokenization is the process of breaking a piece of text, like a sentence or a paragraph, into smaller units called tokens.","分词是把一段文本，比如一个句子或一个段落，切分成更小单位的过程，这些单位叫作词元。"],[214.3,217.4,77,"Neural networks can't read raw strings.","神经网络无法直接读取原始字符串。"],[217.75,224.18,77,"They need a sequence of discrete symbols, each mapped to an ID, and then to an embedding vector.","它们需要一个离散符号的序列，每个符号被映射到一个 ID，再映射到一个嵌入向量。"],[224.53,230.43,77,"The animation shows a sequence model reading the question, what time is it, one token at a time.","这个动画展示了一个序列模型逐个词元地读取问题“What time is it”。"],[230.78,233.63,77,"First what, then time, and so on.","先是 What，然后是 time，依此类推。"],[233.98,242.15,77,"Every model you've seen in this course, RNNs, Transformers, GPT, works on a sequence like this.","这门课里你见过的每一个模型，RNN、Transformer、GPT，都是在这样的序列上工作的。"],[242.5,245.93,77,"The choice of what counts as a token matters a lot.","什么算作一个词元，这个选择非常重要。"],[246.28,253.41,77,"It decides how big your vocabulary is, how long your sequences are, and whether the model can handle words it's never seen.","它决定了你的词表有多大、序列有多长，以及模型能否处理从未见过的词。"],[253.76,256.28,77,"The next few slides compare the options.","接下来几页会比较各种选择。"],[257.53,261.81,78,"Here's a map of tokenization methods. There are three main families.","这是一张分词方法的地图，主要有三大类。"],[262.16,270.28,78,"Word-level tokenization splits text into words, either by spaces, by punctuation, or with hand-written rules.","词级分词把文本切分成单词，可以按空格、按标点，或者用人工编写的规则。"],[270.63,274.95,78,"Character-level tokenization treats every single character as a token.","字符级分词把每一个字符都当作一个词元。"],[275.3,279.23,78,"And subword tokenization sits in between.","而子词分词介于两者之间。"],[279.58,287.44,78,"It has four well-known algorithms: byte-pair encoding, or BPE, WordPiece, Unigram, and SentencePiece.","它有四种著名的算法：字节对编码，也就是 BPE，WordPiece，Unigram，以及 SentencePiece。"],[287.79,294.31,78,"Almost all modern LLMs use subword tokenization, usually some variant of BPE.","几乎所有现代 LLM 都使用子词分词，通常是 BPE 的某种变体。"],[294.66,297.86,78,"The next slide shows why, with a simple example.","下一页用一个简单的例子说明原因。"],[299.11,301.65,79,"Take the sentence: this is tokenizing.","以这个句子为例：“This is tokenizing.”"],[302.0,307.39,79,"At character level, you get eighteen tokens: T, h, i, s, and so on.","在字符级别，你会得到十八个词元：T、h、i、s，等等。"],[307.74,314.27,79,"The vocabulary is tiny, but the sequence is long, and each token carries very little meaning.","词表很小，但序列很长，而且每个词元承载的意义很少。"],[314.62,320.04,79,"At word level, you get four tokens: this, is, tokenizing, and the period.","在词级别，你会得到四个词元：This、is、tokenizing 和句号。"],[320.39,321.63,79,"Nice and short.","又短又好。"],[321.98,329.02,79,"But the vocabulary has to contain every word form, including tokenizing, tokenized, and tokenizer.","但词表必须包含每一种词形，包括 tokenizing、tokenized、tokenizer。"],[329.37,333.14,79,"And when a new word appears, you're stuck with an unknown token.","当出现一个新词时，你就只能用一个未知词元来表示。"],[333.49,338.56,79,"At subword level, you get this, is, token, izing, and the period.","在子词级别，你会得到 This、is、token、izing 和句号。"],[338.91,343.53,79,"Common words stay whole, while the rare word is split into meaningful pieces.","常见的词保持完整，而罕见的词被切分成有意义的片段。"],[343.88,349.68,79,"Token, which the model knows well, and izing, which it has seen in many other words.","token 是模型很熟悉的，而 izing 它也在很多其他词里见过。"],[350.03,355.73,79,"That's the sweet spot: a manageable vocabulary, reasonable sequence lengths, and no unknown words.","这就是最佳平衡点：可控的词表大小、合理的序列长度，以及没有未知词。"],[356.08,359.4,79,"The next slide puts these trade-offs side by side in a table.","下一页用一张表把这些权衡并排列出来。"],[360.65,363.38,80,"Here are those trade-offs side by side.","这里把这些权衡并排放在一起。"],[363.73,369.94,80,"The choice of tokenization technique depends on the specific task and language being analyzed.","选择哪种分词技术，取决于具体的任务和所分析的语言。"],[370.29,377.77,80,"Word-based tokenization is simple and efficient, but it can be limited in its ability to handle complex languages.","基于词的分词简单高效，但在处理复杂语言时能力可能有限。"],[378.12,385.41,80,"Its downside is a very large vocabulary, which means a huge embedding matrix and many out-of-vocabulary words.","它的缺点是词表非常大，这意味着巨大的嵌入矩阵和大量的未登录词。"],[385.76,391.89,80,"Character-based tokenization can be useful for languages without distinct word boundaries.","基于字符的分词，对于没有明确词边界的语言可能很有用。"],[392.24,400.75,80,"It gives a much smaller vocabulary and no out-of-vocabulary tokens, but it generates very long sequences of less meaningful tokens.","它的词表小得多，也没有未登录词元，但会产生由意义较少的词元构成的很长序列。"],[401.1,413.34,80,"Subword-based tokenization, including BPE, WordPiece, SentencePiece and Unigram, is particularly useful for handling complex morphology and out-of-vocabulary words.","基于子词的分词，包括 BPE、WordPiece、SentencePiece 和 Unigram，特别适合处理复杂的形态变化和未登录词。"],[413.69,421.66,80,"Frequent words are not split, while rare words are decomposed into meaningful subwords, which gives a reasonable vocabulary size.","高频词不被切分，而罕见词被分解成有意义的子词，从而得到合理的词表大小。"],[422.91,425.58,81,"Let's make the subword idea a bit more precise.","我们把子词的概念说得更精确一些。"],[425.93,434.93,81,"Subword modeling covers all methods that reason about structure below the word level: parts of words, characters, even bytes.","子词建模涵盖了所有在词以下层面推理结构的方法：词的一部分、字符，甚至字节。"],[435.28,439.37,81,"Look at the example: unfriendly becomes un, friend, ly.","看这个例子：unfriendly 变成了 un、friend、ly。"],[439.72,448.74,81,"A model that has seen un in unhappy and ly in quickly can make sense of unfriendly, even if the full word is rare.","一个在 unhappy 中见过 un、在 quickly 中见过 ly 的模型，即使 unfriendly 这个完整的词很少见，也能理解它。"],[449.09,456.9,81,"The modern paradigm, in the two bullets, is to learn the vocabulary of subword tokens from data, rather than design it by hand.","这两条要点说的现代范式是：从数据中学习子词词表，而不是人工设计。"],[457.25,464.43,81,"Then at both training and test time, every word is split into a sequence of known subwords.","然后在训练和测试时，每个词都被切分成一串已知的子词。"],[464.78,471.98,81,"Since, in the worst case, you can always fall back to single characters or bytes, there are no out-of-vocabulary words anymore.","由于在最坏情况下，你总是可以退回到单个字符或字节，所以不再有未登录词。"],[473.23,477.04,82,"Here are the four main subword algorithms side by side.","这里把四种主要的子词算法并排列出。"],[477.39,484.39,82,"BPE starts from characters and repeatedly merges the most frequent adjacent pair into a new token.","BPE 从字符开始，反复把最频繁的相邻字符对合并成一个新词元。"],[484.74,488.04,82,"WordPiece, used in BERT, is very similar.","BERT 使用的 WordPiece 与它非常相似。"],[488.39,496.91,82,"But instead of picking the most frequent pair, it picks the merge that most increases the likelihood of the training data.","但它不是选择最频繁的字符对，而是选择最能提高训练数据似然的合并。"],[497.26,505.23,82,"Unigram goes the other way: it starts with a large vocabulary and progressively removes the tokens that matter least.","Unigram 则反其道而行：它从一个大词表开始，逐步删除最不重要的词元。"],[505.58,510.34,82,"And SentencePiece is not a separate merging rule, but a framework.","而 SentencePiece 不是一种独立的合并规则，而是一个框架。"],[510.69,519.3,82,"It treats the input as a raw stream, including spaces, so it works for languages like Chinese and Japanese that don't use spaces between words.","它把输入当作原始字符流，连空格也包括在内，所以适用于中文、日语这类词与词之间不用空格的语言。"],[519.65,523.64,82,"And it runs BPE or Unigram underneath.","它的底层运行的是 BPE 或 Unigram。"],[523.99,530.96,82,"A bit of history: BPE was invented in nineteen ninety-four by Gage as a data compression algorithm.","讲一点历史：BPE 由 Gage 在 1994 年发明，最初是一种数据压缩算法。"],[531.31,537.67,82,"It was later adapted for subword tokenization in neural machine translation, which is where NLP picked it up.","后来它被改造用于神经机器翻译中的子词切分，NLP 正是从那里开始采用它的。"],[538.02,539.67,82,"Let's look at how it works.","我们来看看它是如何工作的。"],[540.92,547.44,83,"Let's look at byte-pair encoding as a compression algorithm first, which makes the idea very easy to see.","我们先把字节对编码当作一种压缩算法来看，这样思路会非常清楚。"],[547.79,551.98,83,"Start with the string a a a b d a a a b a c.","从字符串 aaabdaaabac 开始。"],[552.33,557.73,83,"The most frequent adjacent pair is a a, so replace it with a new symbol, Z.","最频繁的相邻字符对是 aa，所以用一个新符号 Z 来替换它。"],[558.08,561.42,83,"Now we have Z a b d Z a b a c.","现在我们得到了 ZabdZabac。"],[561.77,567.86,83,"The most frequent pair is now a b, so replace it with Y, giving Z Y d Z Y a c.","现在最频繁的字符对是 ab，用 Y 替换它，得到 ZYdZYac。"],[568.21,573.98,83,"Then Z Y appears twice, so replace it with X, giving X d X a c.","然后 ZY 出现了两次，用 X 替换它，得到 XdXac。"],[574.33,577.99,83,"Now no pair appears more than once, so we stop.","现在没有任何字符对出现超过一次，所以我们停下来。"],[578.34,582.23,83,"To decompress, just apply the replacements in reverse order.","要解压，只需按相反的顺序执行这些替换。"],[582.58,586.4,83,"For tokenization, it's the same procedure on a text corpus.","对于分词，就是在文本语料上执行同样的过程。"],[586.75,594.43,83,"Start with a vocabulary of single characters plus an end-of-word symbol, and count all adjacent pairs.","从由单个字符加上一个词尾符号组成的词表开始，统计所有相邻的字符对。"],[594.78,604.07,83,"Merge the most common one into a new token, and repeat until you reach the vocabulary size you want, say fifty thousand or one hundred fifty thousand.","把最常见的那一对合并成一个新词元，然后重复，直到达到你想要的词表大小，比如五万或十五万。"],[604.42,607.82,83,"The list of merges you learned is your tokenizer.","你学到的这一串合并规则，就是你的分词器。"],[608.17,613.66,83,"Frequent words end up as single tokens, and rare words get split into pieces.","高频词最终成为单个词元，而罕见词则被切分成片段。"],[614.91,620.61,84,"Now, why should you care? Because a tokenizer that's bad for your language can really hurt.","那么，为什么要关心这个？因为一个不适合你所用语言的分词器真的会造成伤害。"],[620.96,625.15,84,"Here's a real example: the original LLaMA tokenizer on Chinese.","这里有一个真实的例子：原始 LLaMA 分词器处理中文的情况。"],[625.5,628.91,84,"The original sentence has twenty-eight Chinese characters.","原句有 28 个汉字。"],[629.26,635.38,84,"The original LLaMA tokenizer turns it into thirty-five tokens, more tokens than characters!","原始 LLaMA 分词器把它变成了 35 个词元，比汉字还多！"],[635.73,642.4,84,"Look at those strange tokens like zero x E five, zero x nine three, zero x B two.","看看那些奇怪的词元，比如 0xE5、0x93、0xB2。"],[642.75,645.43,84,"Those are raw UTF-8 bytes.","这些是原始的 UTF-8 字节。"],[645.78,651.88,84,"The tokenizer didn't know some Chinese characters, so it fell back to splitting each one into three bytes.","分词器不认识某些汉字，所以只好退而把每个字拆成三个字节。"],[652.23,660.55,84,"The Chinese LLaMA project extended the vocabulary with Chinese words, and the same sentence becomes just sixteen tokens.","Chinese LLaMA 项目用中文词扩充了词表，同一个句子只需要 16 个词元。"],[660.9,666.06,84,"Meaningful units like artificial intelligence and computer become single tokens.","像“人工智能”和“计算机”这样有意义的单位都成了单个词元。"],[666.41,667.5,84,"Why does that matter?","这为什么重要？"],[667.85,675.32,84,"More tokens means slower and more expensive training and inference, and a shorter effective context window.","更多的词元意味着训练和推理更慢、更贵，有效的上下文窗口也更短。"],[675.67,680.47,84,"It also makes learning harder, since the model has to reassemble characters from bytes.","这也让学习变得更难，因为模型必须从字节中重新拼出汉字。"],[680.82,684.26,84,"Tokenizer design is a fairness issue across languages, too.","分词器的设计也是一个跨语言的公平性问题。"],[685.51,690.26,85,"Here's an example from our own team, so I'm not just criticizing others.","再看一个来自我们自己团队的例子，免得大家觉得我只批评别人。"],[690.61,695.35,85,"AceGPT is our Arabic LLM, built on top of LLaMA 2.","AceGPT 是我们的阿拉伯语大模型，基于 LLaMA 2 构建。"],[695.7,705.0,85,"On the right is a LinkedIn post by an Arabic data scientist, comparing the two open Arabic models at the time, Jais and AceGPT.","右边是一位阿拉伯数据科学家在 LinkedIn 上的帖子，比较了当时两个开源阿拉伯语模型：Jais 和 AceGPT。"],[705.35,711.08,85,"His point was that Jais treats Arabic on par with English in its tokenization.","他的观点是：Jais 在分词上对阿拉伯语和英语一视同仁。"],[711.43,718.26,85,"AceGPT, on the other hand, tokenizes Arabic close to the character level, which makes generation slow.","而 AceGPT 对阿拉伯语的切分几乎接近字符级别，导致生成速度很慢。"],[718.61,725.34,85,"At the same time, he noted that AceGPT gave an answer to his test question, while Jais declined.","同时他也指出，对他的测试问题，AceGPT 给出了回答，而 Jais 拒绝了。"],[725.69,727.45,85,"He was right about the tokenizer.","他对分词器的批评是对的。"],[727.8,734.0,85,"Because we inherited LLaMA's vocabulary, Arabic words were split into many small pieces.","因为我们沿用了 LLaMA 的词表，阿拉伯语单词被切成了很多小碎片。"],[734.35,737.36,85,"You can check the tokenizer file linked at the bottom yourself.","大家可以自己去看看底部链接里的分词器文件。"],[737.71,743.26,85,"The lesson: when you adapt a model to a new language, think carefully about the vocabulary.","教训是：把模型迁移到新语言时，一定要认真考虑词表。"],[743.61,747.61,85,"Sometimes extending it is worth the extra training cost.","有时候，扩充词表是值得付出额外训练成本的。"],[748.86,752.02,86,"Before we leave tokenization, let me broaden the idea.","在结束分词这一部分之前，我们把这个概念再扩展一下。"],[752.37,754.71,86,"A token doesn't have to be a piece of text.","token 不一定非得是一段文本。"],[755.06,757.7,86,"On the left is the Vision Transformer.","左边是 Vision Transformer。"],[758.05,766.03,86,"An image is cut into sixteen by sixteen patches, and each patch is flattened and projected into a vector.","一张图像被切成 16×16 的小块，每个小块被展平并投影成一个向量。"],[766.38,770.07,86,"Then the Transformer treats those patches exactly like words.","然后 Transformer 就把这些图像块当作单词一样处理。"],[770.42,775.0,86,"That's why the paper is called An Image is Worth Sixteen by Sixteen Words.","这就是为什么那篇论文叫《An Image is Worth 16x16 Words》。"],[775.35,777.21,86,"In the middle are speech tokens.","中间是语音 token。"],[777.56,782.68,86,"Some tokenizers produce acoustic tokens that capture how something sounds.","有些分词器产生声学 token，捕捉声音听起来是什么样。"],[783.03,789.93,86,"Others produce semantic tokens that capture what is said, and the SpeechTokenizer work unifies the two.","另一些产生语义 token，捕捉说的是什么内容；而 SpeechTokenizer 这项工作把两者统一了起来。"],[790.28,791.81,86,"On the right is genomics.","右边是基因组学。"],[792.16,798.97,86,"A DNA sequence can be split into overlapping k-mers, short chunks of letters, and treated as words in a sentence.","一段 DNA 序列可以切成相互重叠的 k-mer，也就是一小段字母，再把它们当作句子里的单词。"],[799.32,806.52,86,"Once you can turn any data into a sequence of tokens, you can apply the same language-modeling machinery.","只要能把任何数据变成 token 序列，就能套用同一套语言建模的方法。"],[806.87,811.52,86,"That's the foundation of multimodal LLMs, which we'll study in Lecture ten.","这正是多模态大模型的基础，我们会在第十讲学习。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Pretraining: Language Modeling and Eight Data Tips","blurb":"Next-token prediction at scale: data sources and ratios, model scale, continued pretraining, and eight practical tips from filtering and deduplication to synthesis.","file":"lecture05_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part7.jpg","duration":1048.0,"first":87,"last":104,"slides":[{"n":87,"title":"LLM Pretraining","t":0.8},{"n":88,"title":"What is language modeling?","t":21.01},{"n":89,"title":"What is language modeling?","t":66.92},{"n":90,"title":"Language model using neural networks","t":115.65},{"n":91,"title":"Data Engineering: sources","t":181.59},{"n":92,"title":"Data Engineering: ratios","t":247.84},{"n":93,"title":"Model Scale","t":306.61},{"n":94,"title":"Continue pretraining in LLMs （domain adaptation）","t":364.19},{"n":95,"title":"Tips for LLM pre-training","t":433.71},{"n":96,"title":"Tip 1: Data filter","t":448.07},{"n":97,"title":"Tip 2: Data reformatting","t":512.55},{"n":98,"title":"Alignment at Pre-training!","t":576.19},{"n":99,"title":"Tip 3: Data deduplication","t":637.18},{"n":100,"title":"Tip 4: Data mixture","t":709.13},{"n":101,"title":"Tip 5: Data order","t":776.85},{"n":102,"title":"Tip 6: Data scale matters","t":845.51},{"n":103,"title":"Tip 7: Data mask","t":918.91},{"n":104,"title":"Tip 8: Data synthesis","t":985.62}],"sents":[[0.8,1.98,87,"We now have tokens.","现在我们有了 token。"],[2.33,9.33,87,"The next step is the biggest and most expensive one: pretraining, where the model reads the textbooks.","下一步是规模最大、成本最高的一步：预训练，也就是让模型去“读课本”。"],[9.68,13.38,87,"We'll start with what language modeling means mathematically.","我们先看语言建模在数学上是什么意思。"],[13.73,19.61,87,"Then we'll look at the data, which is honestly where most of the secret sauce is.","然后再看数据——说实话，大部分“秘方”都藏在数据里。"],[20.86,23.96,88,"Let's quickly recall language modeling from Lecture three.","我们快速回顾一下第三讲的语言建模。"],[24.31,29.28,88,"A language model assigns a probability to a sequence of words, an n-gram.","语言模型给一个词序列，也就是一个 n-gram，赋予一个概率。"],[29.63,34.57,88,"Formally, it's a function f from sequences of n words to positive numbers.","形式上，它是一个函数 f，把 n 个词组成的序列映射到正数。"],[34.92,39.66,88,"A conditional language model assigns a probability to a word given some context.","条件语言模型则是在给定上下文的情况下，给一个词赋予概率。"],[40.01,45.16,88,"That's a function g that takes the previous n minus one words and a candidate next word.","也就是一个函数 g，输入前面 n 减 1 个词和一个候选的下一个词。"],[45.51,48.1,88,"The example at the bottom is your phone keyboard.","下方的例子就是你手机的输入法键盘。"],[48.45,53.45,88,"You type I've, and it suggests been, got, never.","你输入 I've，它就会推荐 been、got、never。"],[53.8,58.54,88,"That's a conditional language model at work, ranking candidate next words given the context.","这就是条件语言模型在工作：根据上下文给候选的下一个词排序。"],[58.89,65.52,88,"The connection between the two, which we'll complete on the next slide, is just the definition of conditional probability.","两者之间的联系——下一页会补全——其实就是条件概率的定义。"],[66.77,68.08,89,"Here's the full relation.","这是完整的关系式。"],[68.43,75.12,89,"The probability of the next word w n, given all previous words, equals g of that context and word.","给定前面所有词时，下一个词 w_n 的概率，等于 g 作用在这个上下文和这个词上。"],[75.47,81.77,89,"And that equals f of the whole sequence, divided by f of the sequence without the last word.","而它又等于整个序列的 f 值，除以去掉最后一个词后序列的 f 值。"],[82.12,87.63,89,"In words: how likely is the full sentence, relative to how likely its beginning was.","用大白话说：整句话的可能性，相对于它开头部分的可能性有多大。"],[87.98,90.94,89,"The line at the bottom is the one to remember.","最下面这一行是要记住的。"],[91.29,102.07,89,"This conditional probability, p of w n given w one through w n minus one, is the foundation of modern large language models like GPT and ChatGPT.","这个条件概率，即给定 w_1 到 w_{n-1} 时 w_n 的概率，是 GPT、ChatGPT 等现代大语言模型的基础。"],[102.42,109.02,89,"Pretraining is nothing more than making this prediction as accurate as possible over trillions of tokens.","预训练无非就是在数万亿个 token 上，让这个预测尽可能准确。"],[109.37,114.25,89,"All the abilities we discussed in part one come out of this one simple objective.","我们在第一部分讨论的所有能力，都来自这一个简单的目标。"],[115.5,118.17,90,"With a neural network, it looks like this.","用神经网络来做，就是这个样子。"],[118.52,124.47,90,"The input is wo si gu wo, the first part of I think, therefore I am.","输入是“我思故我”，也就是“我思故我在”的前半句。"],[124.82,127.84,90,"The model has to output the next character, zai.","模型需要输出下一个字：“在”。"],[128.19,133.48,90,"In between is a big black-box neural network, in our case a Transformer.","中间是一个巨大的黑箱神经网络，在我们这里就是 Transformer。"],[133.83,140.01,90,"It reads the context and produces a probability distribution over the vocabulary.","它读取上下文，输出一个在整个词表上的概率分布。"],[140.36,143.02,90,"The note on the left gives you a sense of scale.","左边的注释让你感受一下规模。"],[143.37,152.18,90,"Models like GPT-3 have one hundred seventy-five billion parameters or more, while the human brain has on the order of one hundred billion neurons.","像 GPT-3 这样的模型有 1750 亿甚至更多参数，而人脑大约有 1000 亿个神经元。"],[152.53,159.29,90,"As I mentioned earlier, that comparison is loose, because parameters are more like connections than neurons.","正如我之前提到的，这种比较很粗略，因为参数更像是神经元之间的连接，而不是神经元本身。"],[159.64,163.45,90,"But it shows that these networks are no longer small.","但它说明这些网络已经一点都不小了。"],[163.8,165.9,90,"Training is simple to describe.","训练过程描述起来很简单。"],[166.25,175.04,90,"Show the model the text, compare its prediction with the true next token, compute the cross-entropy loss, and update the weights.","把文本给模型看，把它的预测和真实的下一个 token 比较，计算交叉熵损失，然后更新权重。"],[175.39,177.95,90,"Then repeat, a few trillion times.","然后重复几万亿次。"],[178.3,180.19,90,"The hard part is the data.","难的是数据。"],[181.44,184.36,91,"Let's look at what pretraining data actually looks like.","我们来看看预训练数据实际长什么样。"],[184.71,192.55,91,"This is the pretraining mix for OLMo 2, a fully open model from AI2, which is great because they publish everything.","这是 OLMo 2 的预训练数据配比。OLMo 2 是 AI2 推出的完全开源模型，好处是他们公开了一切。"],[192.9,197.7,91,"The biggest source by far is DCLM-Baseline, filtered web pages.","最大的来源是 DCLM-Baseline，也就是过滤后的网页数据。"],[198.05,203.25,91,"That's about three point seven trillion tokens, out of a total of three point nine trillion.","约 3.7 万亿 token，而总量是 3.9 万亿。"],[203.6,206.75,91,"Then come much smaller amounts of higher-value data.","然后是数量少得多、但价值更高的数据。"],[207.1,216.14,91,"StarCoder code at eighty-three billion tokens, and academic papers from peS2o at about fifty-nine billion.","StarCoder 代码有 830 亿 token，peS2o 的学术论文约 590 亿。"],[216.49,223.71,91,"Then arXiv STEM papers, OpenWebMath, and the Algebraic Stack with math proofs and code.","然后是 arXiv 的理工科论文、OpenWebMath，以及包含数学证明和代码的 Algebraic Stack。"],[224.06,228.78,91,"And Wikipedia and Wikibooks at just three point seven billion tokens.","还有维基百科和 Wikibooks，只有 37 亿 token。"],[229.13,230.26,91,"Two observations.","有两点观察。"],[230.61,236.09,91,"Web data dominates by volume, so the quality of web filtering matters enormously.","从数量上看，网页数据占绝对主导，所以网页过滤的质量极其重要。"],[236.44,242.89,91,"And specialized sources like math and code are small, but very valuable for reasoning.","而数学、代码这类专门数据量虽小，但对推理能力非常宝贵。"],[243.24,246.44,91,"That brings us to the question of how to mix them.","这就引出了一个问题：怎么把它们混合起来？"],[247.69,253.37,92,"This table from the GPT-3 paper shows the training mix, and it reveals an important trick.","这张来自 GPT-3 论文的表格展示了训练数据配比，并揭示了一个重要技巧。"],[253.72,254.75,92,"Look at the columns.","看各列。"],[255.1,261.08,92,"Common Crawl has four hundred ten billion tokens and gets sixty percent of the training weight.","Common Crawl 有 4100 亿 token，占训练权重的 60%。"],[261.43,266.59,92,"WebText2 has only nineteen billion tokens, but gets twenty-two percent.","WebText2 只有 190 亿 token，却占了 22%。"],[266.94,269.61,92,"Books and Wikipedia are smaller still.","书籍和维基百科的数据量更小。"],[269.96,274.76,92,"Now look at the red box: epochs elapsed when training on three hundred billion tokens.","再看红框：训练 3000 亿 token 时，每个数据集被过了几遍。"],[275.11,280.54,92,"Common Crawl is seen only zero point four four times, so less than half of it is ever used.","Common Crawl 只被看了 0.44 遍，也就是说一半都没用到。"],[280.89,287.09,92,"But WebText2 is seen two point nine times, and Wikipedia three point four times.","而 WebText2 被看了 2.9 遍，维基百科则是 3.4 遍。"],[287.44,293.57,92,"So the rule is: repeat high-quality data more often, and sample low-quality data less.","所以规则是：高质量数据多重复几遍，低质量数据少采样。"],[293.92,299.56,92,"How exactly to set these ratios is one of the most important decisions in pretraining.","这些比例具体怎么定，是预训练中最重要的决策之一。"],[299.91,305.21,92,"And as the slide says, it's usually a closely guarded secret.","而且正如幻灯片所说，这通常是严格保密的。"],[306.46,311.77,93,"And here is the model side of the same paper: the GPT-3 family again.","这是同一篇论文中模型方面的信息：还是 GPT-3 系列。"],[312.12,319.23,93,"It goes from GPT-3 Small at one hundred twenty-five million parameters up to the full one hundred seventy-five billion.","从 1.25 亿参数的 GPT-3 Small，一直到完整的 1750 亿参数。"],[319.58,324.95,93,"As the caption says, all of these models were trained on the same three hundred billion tokens.","正如图注所说，所有这些模型都是在同样的 3000 亿 token 上训练的。"],[325.3,330.32,93,"That seemed reasonable at the time, but it turned out to be an important mistake for the larger models.","这在当时看似合理，但事后证明，对大模型来说这是一个重要的失误。"],[330.67,337.61,93,"A couple of years later, the Chinchilla work showed that, for a fixed compute budget, the biggest models were undertrained.","几年后，Chinchilla 的工作表明，在固定计算预算下，最大的那些模型训练不足。"],[337.96,341.51,93,"They should have seen far more tokens relative to their size.","相对于它们的规模，它们本应看到多得多的 token。"],[341.86,344.3,93,"We'll see that plot in a few slides.","几页之后我们会看到那张图。"],[344.65,347.83,93,"Also notice how the shape changes with size.","还要注意，模型形状随规模如何变化。"],[348.18,354.39,93,"More layers, wider hidden size, more heads, bigger batches, and smaller learning rates.","层数更多、隐藏维度更宽、注意力头更多、批次更大、学习率更小。"],[354.74,362.79,93,"These design choices are pretty standard now, and you can use this table as a reference if you ever train a model yourself.","这些设计选择现在已经相当标准，如果你自己训练模型，可以把这张表当作参考。"],[364.04,366.51,94,"Most of you won't pretrain from scratch.","你们大多数人不会从零开始预训练。"],[366.86,376.52,94,"A much more realistic option is continued pretraining: take an existing pretrained model, and keep pretraining it on new data to adapt it.","更现实的选择是继续预训练：拿一个已有的预训练模型，在新数据上接着预训练，让它适应新场景。"],[376.87,381.4,94,"There are three typical use cases, all with examples from our group.","有三种典型的应用场景，每种都有我们组的例子。"],[381.75,387.76,94,"New domains, like medicine or finance; HuatuoGPT is our medical model.","新领域，比如医疗或金融；HuatuoGPT 是我们的医疗模型。"],[388.11,393.35,94,"New languages, like Arabic or Chinese, with AceGPT and Phoenix.","新语言，比如阿拉伯语或中文，对应 AceGPT 和 Phoenix。"],[393.7,399.82,94,"And new modalities, like vision and audio, with ALLaVA, Soundwave and WaveMind.","还有新模态，比如视觉和音频，对应 ALLaVA、Soundwave 和 WaveMind。"],[400.17,406.47,94,"The big risk is catastrophic forgetting: train hard on new data, and the model can lose what it knew before.","最大的风险是灾难性遗忘：在新数据上训练过猛，模型可能会忘掉以前学会的东西。"],[406.82,408.27,94,"Some practical tips.","几个实用技巧。"],[408.62,410.29,94,"Start with a small learning rate.","一开始用小学习率。"],[410.64,415.42,94,"Mix new data with old data, and gradually increase the share of new data.","把新数据和旧数据混合，逐步提高新数据的比例。"],[415.77,422.03,94,"Be patient, because the positive effect often takes longer to show up than you expect.","要有耐心，因为正面效果往往比你预期的更晚出现。"],[422.38,429.1,94,"And if you add new domain-specific tokens to the vocabulary, remember their embeddings start from scratch.","如果你在词表中加入新的领域专用 token，记住它们的嵌入是从零开始的。"],[429.45,432.31,94,"So you need many more tokens to train them well.","所以需要多得多的 token 才能把它们训练好。"],[433.56,435.23,95,"Now let's get practical.","现在我们来点实用的。"],[435.58,441.27,95,"Whether you pretrain from scratch or continue pretraining, most of the gains come from the data.","无论是从零预训练还是继续预训练，大部分收益都来自数据。"],[441.62,446.67,95,"Here are eight tips about data, each backed by a paper you can read later.","下面是关于数据的八条技巧，每条都有一篇论文支撑，大家之后可以去读。"],[447.92,449.82,96,"Tip one: filter your data.","技巧一：过滤你的数据。"],[450.17,453.71,96,"This figure is from A Pretrainer's Guide to Training Data.","这张图来自《A Pretrainer's Guide to Training Data》。"],[454.06,460.98,96,"The rows are data domains: web, code, PubMed, academic papers, books, and Wikipedia.","各行是数据领域：网页、代码、PubMed、学术论文、书籍和维基百科。"],[461.33,466.75,96,"The columns are years, from two thousand thirteen to two thousand twenty-two.","各列是年份，从 2013 年到 2022 年。"],[467.1,471.88,96,"The outlined regions show where toxic content and low-quality content live.","圈出的区域表示有毒内容和低质量内容所在的位置。"],[472.23,476.3,96,"You can see they're spread across many sources and years.","可以看到，它们分散在很多来源和年份中。"],[476.65,482.31,96,"So you need filters, usually a quality classifier and a toxicity classifier.","所以需要过滤器，通常是一个质量分类器和一个毒性分类器。"],[482.66,486.88,96,"The paper's main lesson is that these choices involve trade-offs.","这篇论文的主要结论是：这些选择都涉及权衡。"],[487.23,496.84,96,"Aggressive filtering removes harmful or junk text, but it can also remove useful diversity, and it changes what the model is good at.","激进的过滤能去掉有害或垃圾文本，但也可能去掉有用的多样性，并改变模型擅长的方向。"],[497.19,500.43,96,"They also found that the age of the data matters.","他们还发现，数据的年代也很重要。"],[500.78,504.91,96,"A model trained on older data does worse on newer evaluation data.","用较旧数据训练的模型，在较新的评测数据上表现更差。"],[505.26,511.15,96,"So don't treat filtering as a fixed step. Treat it as a design decision that you test.","所以不要把过滤当作固定步骤，而要把它当作需要实验验证的设计决策。"],[512.4,514.77,97,"Tip two: reformat your data.","技巧二：重新格式化你的数据。"],[515.12,518.06,97,"This example is from a paper called ReAlign.","这个例子来自一篇叫 ReAlign 的论文。"],[518.41,525.49,97,"Instead of training on responses exactly as they were written, they rewrite them into a clear, predefined format.","他们不是直接用原样的回答训练，而是把回答改写成清晰的、预先定义好的格式。"],[525.84,529.96,97,"Look at the left: the original math answer is one long paragraph.","看左边：原始的数学解答是一整段长文字。"],[530.31,537.26,97,"The rewritten version has clear sections: analysis, solution, explanation, result, and conclusion.","改写后的版本分成清晰的部分：分析、解答、解释、结果和结论。"],[537.61,539.62,97,"Same content, better structure.","内容相同，结构更好。"],[539.97,543.06,97,"The bar charts on the right show the effect.","右边的柱状图展示了效果。"],[543.41,552.92,97,"On GSM8K, LLaMA-2-13B goes from about forty-seven to about fifty-seven percent, almost ten points.","在 GSM8K 上，LLaMA-2-13B 从约 47% 提升到约 57%，提高了近 10 个点。"],[553.27,556.55,97,"Mistral-7B goes up about five points.","Mistral-7B 提升了约 5 个点。"],[556.9,560.51,97,"And on MATH, there are gains of around ten points for both models.","在 MATH 上，两个模型都提升了大约 10 个点。"],[560.86,565.94,97,"This experiment was done on fine-tuning data, but the same idea applies to pretraining.","这个实验是在微调数据上做的，但同样的思路也适用于预训练。"],[566.29,570.6,97,"Rephrasing messy web text into cleaner forms is now a common technique.","把杂乱的网页文本改写成更干净的形式，现在已是常用技术。"],[570.95,574.79,97,"Models learn better from well-organized text, just like students do.","模型和学生一样，从组织良好的文本中学得更好。"],[576.04,580.55,98,"Here's a related idea from our own group: alignment at pretraining.","这是我们组的一个相关想法：在预训练阶段做对齐。"],[580.9,588.75,98,"Usually, we pretrain on raw data, and fix the model's behavior afterwards with SFT and RLHF.","通常我们在原始数据上预训练，之后再用 SFT 和 RLHF 来修正模型的行为。"],[589.1,598.43,98,"In this work, published at NeurIPS two thousand twenty-four, we asked: why not clean up the pretraining data itself, so the model learns good behavior natively?","在这篇发表于 NeurIPS 2024 的工作中，我们提出：为什么不直接清理预训练数据本身，让模型从一开始就学到良好的行为？"],[598.78,602.75,98,"Look at the four examples, each in Arabic and English.","看这四个例子，每个都有阿拉伯语和英语两个版本。"],[603.1,608.15,98,"Format issues: raw HTML tags become well-formatted text.","格式问题：原始的 HTML 标签变成了格式良好的文本。"],[608.5,613.79,98,"Unfair values: as a woman you shouldn't complain about cleaning becomes as an individual.","不公平的价值观：“作为女人你不该抱怨打扫卫生”被改成了“作为一个人”。"],[614.14,618.5,98,"Hate: a violent threat is rewritten into I'll be really upset with him.","仇恨：一句暴力威胁被改写成“我会对他非常生气”。"],[618.85,621.87,98,"And advertisements: the Amazon link is removed.","还有广告：亚马逊链接被删除了。"],[622.22,628.33,98,"We used an LLM to rewrite the pretraining corpus this way for Arabic models.","我们用大模型以这种方式改写了阿拉伯语模型的预训练语料。"],[628.68,635.78,98,"The idea is that alignment doesn't have to be only a final layer of paint. It can be built into the foundation.","核心想法是：对齐不必只是最后刷上的一层漆，它可以融入地基之中。"],[637.03,639.37,99,"Tip three: remove duplicates.","技巧三：去重。"],[639.72,644.63,99,"Web data is full of duplicates and near-duplicates. Look at the examples.","网页数据中充满了重复和近似重复的内容。看这些例子。"],[644.98,651.62,99,"In Wiki-40B, two articles share an identical template and differ only in the award name.","在 Wiki-40B 中，两篇文章模板完全相同，只有奖项名称不同。"],[651.97,656.19,99,"In LM1B, two sentences differ only by a comma.","在 LM1B 中，两句话只差一个逗号。"],[656.54,664.89,99,"And in C4, two flight advertisements are word-for-word identical, except for the cities and dates.","在 C4 中，两则机票广告除了城市和日期之外逐字相同。"],[665.24,671.77,99,"The paper Deduplicating Training Data Makes Language Models Better showed three benefits of removing them.","论文《Deduplicating Training Data Makes Language Models Better》展示了去重的三个好处。"],[672.12,677.28,99,"First, the model memorizes and regurgitates training text less often.","第一，模型更少地记忆并照搬训练文本。"],[677.63,684.77,99,"Second, training is more efficient, since you don't waste compute on the same content again and again.","第二，训练更高效，因为不会在相同内容上反复浪费算力。"],[685.12,693.02,99,"Third, evaluation becomes more honest, since test examples are less likely to have leaked into the training set.","第三，评测更可信，因为测试样例泄漏到训练集中的可能性更小。"],[693.37,701.75,99,"This doesn't contradict the GPT-3 data mix we saw earlier, where high-quality data was deliberately repeated a few times.","这和我们之前看到的 GPT-3 数据配比并不矛盾，那里是有意把高质量数据重复几遍。"],[702.1,707.73,99,"Controlled repetition of good data is a choice; uncontrolled duplication of junk is just waste.","有控制地重复好数据是一种选择；不加控制地重复垃圾数据纯属浪费。"],[708.98,711.58,100,"Tip four: optimize the data mixture.","技巧四：优化数据配比。"],[711.93,720.53,100,"We saw that mixing ratios are usually set by hand and kept secret. DoReMi tries to learn them automatically.","我们看到，混合比例通常是人工设定并保密的。DoReMi 尝试自动学习这些比例。"],[720.88,722.56,100,"Follow the steps in the figure.","跟着图中的步骤看。"],[722.91,727.28,100,"Step one: train a small reference model with some initial domain weights.","第一步：用一组初始的领域权重训练一个小的参考模型。"],[727.63,734.27,100,"Step two: train a small proxy model with an objective called group distributionally robust optimization.","第二步：用一种叫做分组分布鲁棒优化的目标训练一个小的代理模型。"],[734.62,739.37,100,"It up-weights the domains where the proxy is doing worst compared to the reference.","它会提高那些代理模型相对参考模型表现最差的领域的权重。"],[739.72,742.66,100,"The result is a new set of domain weights.","结果就是一组新的领域权重。"],[743.01,746.64,100,"Step three: use those weights to train the large model.","第三步：用这些权重训练大模型。"],[746.99,749.32,100,"The plot on the right shows the payoff.","右边的图展示了收益。"],[749.67,756.39,100,"The domain weights are tuned using a model thirty times smaller, around two hundred eighty million parameters.","领域权重是用一个小 30 倍的模型调出来的，约 2.8 亿参数。"],[756.74,763.49,100,"With those weights, the eight-billion-parameter model reaches the baseline's accuracy two point six times faster.","使用这些权重后，80 亿参数的模型达到基线准确率的速度快了 2.6 倍。"],[763.84,768.74,100,"And it ends up about six point five percent better in average one-shot accuracy.","最终平均单样本准确率还高出约 6.5%。"],[769.09,775.45,100,"The general lesson: small proxy models are a cheap way to make decisions for big, expensive runs.","普遍的经验是：小的代理模型是为昂贵的大规模训练做决策的廉价方式。"],[776.7,783.17,101,"Tip five: think about data order, or more precisely, which documents end up next to each other.","技巧五：考虑数据顺序，更准确地说，是哪些文档会被放在一起。"],[783.52,791.35,101,"Normally, pretraining takes random documents and concatenates them to fill the context window, say eight thousand tokens.","通常预训练会把随机的文档拼接起来填满上下文窗口，比如 8000 个 token。"],[791.7,795.87,101,"That means a cooking recipe might sit right next to a physics paper.","这意味着一份菜谱可能紧挨着一篇物理论文。"],[796.22,802.02,101,"The model sees long contexts, but the earlier documents rarely help predict the later ones.","模型看到的上下文很长，但前面的文档几乎帮不上后面文档的预测。"],[802.37,804.39,101,"In-Context Pretraining changes this.","In-Context Pretraining 改变了这一点。"],[804.74,813.56,101,"Step one, on the left: find related documents and build a graph, where the numbers on the edges are similarity scores.","第一步，左边：找到相关文档并构建一张图，边上的数字是相似度分数。"],[813.91,819.87,101,"Step two, on the right: walk through the graph and concatenate related documents along the path.","第二步，右边：遍历这张图，把路径上的相关文档拼接起来。"],[820.22,822.68,101,"Then cut that into fixed-size windows.","然后切分成固定大小的窗口。"],[823.03,829.98,101,"Now Doc one, Doc three, Doc five and Doc seven, which are all related, sit in the same context.","现在 Doc 1、Doc 3、Doc 5 和 Doc 7 这些相关文档处在同一个上下文里。"],[830.33,835.66,101,"The result is that the model actually learns to use information across long contexts.","结果是，模型真正学会了利用长上下文中的信息。"],[836.01,841.2,101,"That helps with in-context learning, reading comprehension, and long-context reasoning.","这对上下文学习、阅读理解和长上下文推理都有帮助。"],[841.55,844.11,101,"Same data, smarter arrangement.","数据相同，排列更聪明。"],[845.36,850.23,102,"Tip six: data scale matters, and it matters more than people first thought.","技巧六：数据规模很重要，而且比人们最初想的更重要。"],[850.58,853.06,102,"This plot is from the Chinchilla paper.","这张图来自 Chinchilla 论文。"],[853.41,858.42,102,"The x-axis is training tokens, and the y-axis is parameters.","横轴是训练 token 数，纵轴是参数量。"],[858.77,866.76,102,"The black line shows the compute-optimal trade-off: for a given compute budget, how big the model should be and how many tokens it should see.","黑线表示计算最优的权衡：在给定计算预算下，模型应该多大、应该看多少 token。"],[867.11,868.29,102,"Look at the stars.","看这些星星。"],[868.64,877.82,102,"GPT-3, Gopher at two hundred eighty billion, and Megatron-Turing NLG at five hundred thirty billion all sit far above the line.","GPT-3、2800 亿参数的 Gopher 和 5300 亿参数的 Megatron-Turing NLG 都远远位于这条线上方。"],[878.17,881.39,102,"They were too big for the amount of data they were trained on.","相对于它们的训练数据量，这些模型太大了。"],[881.74,890.48,102,"Chinchilla, at seventy billion parameters trained on one point four trillion tokens, sits on the line, and it beat the much larger Gopher.","Chinchilla 有 700 亿参数，训练了 1.4 万亿 token，正好在线上，并且击败了大得多的 Gopher。"],[890.83,895.72,102,"A common rule of thumb from this work is roughly twenty training tokens per parameter.","这项工作给出的一个常用经验法则是：每个参数大约对应 20 个训练 token。"],[896.07,899.1,102,"Since then, the industry has gone even further.","此后，业界走得更远。"],[899.45,909.43,102,"LLaMA-1 used one to one point four trillion tokens, LLaMA-2 used two trillion, and Mistral-7B and Qwen use far more.","LLaMA-1 用了 1 到 1.4 万亿 token，LLaMA-2 用了 2 万亿，Mistral-7B 和 Qwen 用得更多。"],[909.78,911.79,102,"Why go beyond compute-optimal?","为什么要超过计算最优点？"],[912.14,917.51,102,"Because a smaller model trained longer is cheaper to serve to millions of users.","因为训练得更久的小模型，在为数百万用户提供服务时更便宜。"],[918.76,924.09,103,"Tip seven: mask the data, meaning don't learn from every token.","技巧七：对数据做掩码，也就是不要从每个 token 都学习。"],[924.44,930.86,103,"This idea comes from a paper called RHO-1, with the memorable subtitle Not All Tokens Are What You Need.","这个想法来自论文 RHO-1，它有个令人印象深刻的副标题：Not All Tokens Are What You Need。"],[931.21,941.95,103,"Look at the example sentence: The farm has thirty-five hens, then a timestamp, and twelve pigs, then a username, says totaling forty-seven animals.","看这个例句：农场有 35 只母鸡，接着一个时间戳，还有 12 头猪，接着一个用户名，说总共 47 只动物。"],[942.3,951.0,103,"Even after heavy filtering, real text contains noisy tokens, like that timestamp and that username, highlighted in red.","即便经过大量过滤，真实文本中仍然有噪声 token，比如这个时间戳和这个用户名，用红色标出。"],[951.35,958.25,103,"Standard causal language modeling, on the left, computes the loss on every token, including the junk.","左边是标准的因果语言建模，它在每个 token 上都计算损失，包括垃圾 token。"],[958.6,965.25,103,"Selective language modeling, on the right, only keeps the loss on useful tokens, the green check marks.","右边的选择性语言建模只保留有用 token 上的损失，也就是绿色对勾。"],[965.6,969.17,103,"And it drops the loss on noisy ones, the red crosses.","并丢弃噪声 token 上的损失，也就是红色叉号。"],[969.52,975.82,103,"In the paper, a reference model trained on high-quality data is used to score which tokens are worth learning.","在论文中，用一个在高质量数据上训练的参考模型来给 token 打分，判断哪些值得学。"],[976.17,981.22,103,"The intuition is simple: why spend capacity learning to predict random usernames?","直觉很简单：何必把模型容量花在预测随机用户名上？"],[981.57,984.22,103,"Focus the training signal where it matters.","把训练信号集中在真正重要的地方。"],[985.47,990.94,104,"Tip eight: synthesize data. This is becoming one of the most important tips of all.","技巧八：合成数据。这正在成为所有技巧中最重要的之一。"],[991.29,995.93,104,"Here's the pretraining mixture of Phi-4, Microsoft's small but strong model.","这是 Phi-4 的预训练数据配比，Phi-4 是微软推出的小而强的模型。"],[996.28,1001.01,104,"Look at the highlighted row: synthetic data makes up forty percent of training.","看高亮的那一行：合成数据占训练的 40%。"],[1001.36,1006.88,104,"That's two hundred ninety billion unique tokens, repeated almost fourteen times.","其中有 2900 亿个不重复 token，被重复了将近 14 遍。"],[1007.23,1013.04,104,"Compare that with real web data, which is only fifteen percent of training, seen about once.","相比之下，真实网页数据只占训练的 15%，大约只过了一遍。"],[1013.39,1023.58,104,"There's also another fifteen percent of web rewrites, which is real web text rephrased by a model, exactly the reformatting idea from Tip two.","另外还有 15% 的“网页改写”数据，也就是由模型改写的真实网页文本，这正是技巧二中的重新格式化思想。"],[1023.93,1029.77,104,"So for this model, more than half of the training signal comes from text written or rewritten by other models.","所以对这个模型来说，一半以上的训练信号来自其他模型撰写或改写的文本。"],[1030.12,1033.37,104,"That's a big shift from simply scraping the internet.","这与单纯“爬取互联网”相比是一个巨大的转变。"],[1033.72,1039.2,104,"Synthetic data can be cleaner, more focused on reasoning, and more like a textbook.","合成数据可以更干净、更聚焦于推理，也更像教科书。"],[1039.55,1046.14,104,"The risks are reduced diversity and inheriting the teacher's mistakes, which we'll come back to.","风险在于多样性下降以及继承教师模型的错误，这一点我们后面还会回来讲。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"Instruction Finetuning (SFT): Hypotheses and Tips","blurb":"Why language modeling is not assisting users, the superficial alignment hypothesis, FLAN-T5, distillation, self-instruct, complex instructions and SFT's limits.","file":"lecture05_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part8.jpg","duration":1024.0,"first":105,"last":123,"slides":[{"n":105,"title":"Instruction Finetuning (Supervised Fine-Tuning, SFT)","t":0.8},{"n":106,"title":"Language modeling ≠ assisting users","t":26.78},{"n":107,"title":"Difference","t":89.36},{"n":108,"title":"Wang, Y., Kordi, Y., Mishra, S., Liu, A., Smith, N.A., Khashabi, D. and Hajishirzi, H., 2022. Self-instruct: Aligning la","t":142.74},{"n":109,"title":"Recap：The Pretraining/Finetuning Paradigm","t":201.11},{"n":110,"title":"What is instruction finetuning? or called “supervised fine-tuning”","t":253.52},{"n":111,"title":"Instruction Finetuning Hypothesis","t":274.57},{"n":112,"title":"Superficial Alignment Hypothesis","t":332.73},{"n":113,"title":"From Task Recognition to Task Learning","t":396.88},{"n":114,"title":"Task generalization: FLAN-T5","t":460.01},{"n":115,"title":"Tips of instruction finetuning","t":520.18},{"n":116,"title":"Shortcut: Distillation from Top LLMs (e.g. GPT-5)","t":537.09},{"n":117,"title":"Tip 1: Self-instruct for data augmentation","t":592.99},{"n":118,"title":"Self-instruct","t":657.88},{"n":119,"title":"Tip 2: training on output only","t":711.67},{"n":120,"title":"Tip 3: use complex instructions","t":769.54},{"n":121,"title":"WizardLM: Empowering Large Language Models to Follow Complex Instructions","t":817.64},{"n":122,"title":"Limitations of Instruction Finetuning","t":886.47},{"n":123,"title":"How to prepare the response in Instruction tuning","t":949.86}],"sents":[[0.8,2.89,105,"That wraps up pretraining.","预训练部分就到这里。"],[3.24,8.65,105,"At this point we have a base model: it knows a lot about the world and can continue any text.","此时我们有了一个基座模型：它对世界了解很多，能续写任何文本。"],[9.0,12.14,105,"But it doesn't yet behave like an assistant.","但它的行为还不像一个助手。"],[12.49,18.34,105,"Step two is instruction fine-tuning, also called supervised fine-tuning, or SFT.","第二步是指令微调，也叫监督微调，简称 SFT。"],[18.69,25.38,105,"It's the doing-exercises step that turns a text-completer into something that follows instructions.","这是“做练习题”的一步，把一个文本续写器变成能遵循指令的模型。"],[26.63,33.2,106,"Why do we need SFT at all? Because language modeling is not the same as assisting users.","我们为什么需要 SFT？因为语言建模不等于帮助用户。"],[33.55,36.55,106,"Look at this example from the InstructGPT paper.","看 InstructGPT 论文中的这个例子。"],[36.9,42.32,106,"The prompt is Explain the moon landing to a six year old in a few sentences.","提示是：用几句话向一个 6 岁小孩解释登月。"],[42.67,46.56,106,"The base GPT-3, in the red box, doesn't answer.","红框中的基座 GPT-3 并没有回答。"],[46.91,56.16,106,"It continues with Explain the theory of gravity to a six year old, Explain the theory of relativity, Explain the big bang theory.","它接着写：向 6 岁小孩解释引力理论、解释相对论、解释大爆炸理论。"],[56.51,64.31,106,"Why? Because on the internet, a line like that usually appears in a list of similar prompts, like a homework sheet.","为什么？因为在互联网上，这样一句话通常出现在一串类似的提示中，就像一张作业单。"],[64.66,69.99,106,"GPT-3 is doing exactly what it was trained to do: predict the most likely continuation.","GPT-3 做的正是它被训练去做的事：预测最可能的续写。"],[70.34,79.05,106,"InstructGPT, below, actually answers: People went to the moon, and they took pictures of what they saw, and sent them back to the earth.","下面的 InstructGPT 真正回答了问题：人们去了月球，拍下了他们看到的东西，并把照片传回了地球。"],[79.4,83.6,106,"That's the gap: base models do completion, not instruction following.","这就是差距：基座模型做的是续写，而不是遵循指令。"],[83.95,87.96,106,"They're not aligned with the user's intent. SFT closes that gap.","它们没有与用户意图对齐。SFT 就是来弥补这个差距的。"],[89.21,93.87,107,"Pretraining data versus SFT data: the difference fits in one picture.","预训练数据与 SFT 数据：差别一张图就能说清。"],[94.22,102.01,107,"On the left is pretraining data: just a chunk of plain text, here a paragraph from Wikipedia about large language models.","左边是预训练数据：就是一段纯文本，这里是维基百科上关于大语言模型的一段话。"],[102.36,108.66,107,"No structure, no question, no answer. The model just learns to continue it.","没有结构，没有问题，也没有答案。模型只是学习如何续写它。"],[109.01,113.11,107,"On the right is SFT data, which has a clear structure.","右边是 SFT 数据，它有清晰的结构。"],[113.46,119.23,107,"An instruction: Classify the following into animals, plants, and minerals.","一条指令：把下面这些分类为动物、植物和矿物。"],[119.58,123.07,107,"An input: Oak tree, copper ore, elephant.","一个输入：橡树、铜矿石、大象。"],[123.42,129.71,107,"And an output: Oak tree is a plant, copper ore is a mineral, elephant is an animal.","以及一个输出：橡树是植物，铜矿石是矿物，大象是动物。"],[130.06,134.53,107,"By training on many examples in this format, the model learns a new habit.","通过在大量这种格式的样例上训练，模型养成了一个新习惯。"],[134.88,141.34,107,"When it sees an instruction, it produces a response that fulfils it, instead of just continuing the text.","看到指令时，它会生成完成该指令的回答，而不是简单地续写文本。"],[142.59,148.52,108,"So what counts as an instruction? Pretty much anything a user might ask.","那么什么算指令？几乎是用户可能提出的任何要求。"],[148.87,152.22,108,"On the left are examples from the Self-Instruct paper.","左边是 Self-Instruct 论文中的例子。"],[152.57,158.67,108,"Given an address, come up with the zip code. Help me fill out a job application form.","给定一个地址，写出邮政编码。帮我填写一份求职申请表。"],[159.02,165.06,108,"Write code to convert Fahrenheit to Celsius. Write a letter from the perspective of a cat.","写代码把华氏度转换成摄氏度。以一只猫的口吻写一封信。"],[165.41,168.74,108,"Notice that some have an input field and some don't.","注意，有些带有输入字段，有些没有。"],[169.09,172.76,108,"On the right are some Chinese seed tasks in JSON format.","右边是一些 JSON 格式的中文种子任务。"],[173.11,180.49,108,"Write a poem on the theme summer, give synonyms for a word, and continue a list based on a hint in brackets.","以“夏天”为主题写一首诗、给出某个词的同义词、以及根据括号中的提示续写一个列表。"],[180.84,187.07,108,"Each one has an id, a name, the instruction, and instances with input and output.","每个任务都有 id、名称、指令，以及包含输入和输出的实例。"],[187.42,189.07,108,"The point is diversity.","关键在于多样性。"],[189.42,199.71,108,"Good SFT data covers many kinds of tasks, formats and languages, so the model learns the general skill of following instructions, not just a few specific tasks.","好的 SFT 数据涵盖多种任务、格式和语言，让模型学会遵循指令这一通用技能，而不只是几个特定任务。"],[200.96,205.87,109,"Let's connect this to something you already know: the pretraining and fine-tuning paradigm.","我们把它和大家已经熟悉的东西联系起来：预训练加微调范式。"],[206.22,212.64,109,"Step one: pretrain a decoder on language modeling, with lots of text, learning general things.","第一步：在语言建模任务上预训练一个解码器，用大量文本学习通用知识。"],[212.99,217.9,109,"Here it predicts goes to make tasty tea, given Iroh goes to make tasty.","这里它在给定 Iroh goes to make tasty 的情况下，预测 goes to make tasty tea。"],[218.25,224.52,109,"Step two: fine-tune on your specific task, with not many labels, adapting to the task.","第二步：在你的具体任务上微调，标注不多，让模型适应任务。"],[224.87,228.54,109,"For example, classifying whether the movie was good or bad.","比如判断“这部电影……”是好评还是差评。"],[228.89,233.23,109,"The insight is that pretraining serves as a very good initialization.","关键在于，预训练提供了一个非常好的初始化。"],[233.58,238.72,109,"Instruction fine-tuning uses exactly the same machinery, with one twist.","指令微调用的是完全相同的机制，只有一点不同。"],[239.07,245.8,109,"Instead of fine-tuning on one task, you fine-tune on thousands of different tasks, all phrased as instructions.","不是在一个任务上微调，而是在成千上万个不同任务上微调，而且都表述成指令的形式。"],[246.15,252.12,109,"That's what turns task-specific fine-tuning into a general instruction-following skill.","正是这一点，把针对特定任务的微调变成了通用的遵循指令能力。"],[253.37,258.64,110,"So, what exactly is instruction fine-tuning, also called supervised fine-tuning?","那么，指令微调——也叫监督微调——到底是什么？"],[258.99,261.86,110,"The mechanics are simple, as we just saw.","机制很简单，我们刚才已经看到了。"],[262.21,267.56,110,"The deeper and more interesting question is: what does the model actually learn during SFT?","更深层、更有趣的问题是：模型在 SFT 中到底学到了什么？"],[267.91,273.17,110,"New knowledge, or just a new way of talking? Let's look at the main hypotheses.","是新知识，还是只是一种新的说话方式？我们来看看主要的几种假设。"],[274.42,279.24,111,"There are three main hypotheses about what instruction fine-tuning does.","关于指令微调的作用，主要有三种假设。"],[279.59,284.85,111,"The superficial alignment hypothesis says SFT is mostly about task recognition.","表层对齐假设认为，SFT 主要是关于任务识别。"],[285.2,292.19,111,"The model already has the knowledge from pretraining, and SFT just teaches it which format and style to use.","模型已经从预训练中获得了知识，SFT 只是教它使用什么格式和风格。"],[292.54,297.24,111,"That's most plausible for knowledge-agnostic tasks, like information extraction.","这对知识无关的任务最为合理，比如信息抽取。"],[297.59,304.17,111,"The knowledge injection hypothesis says SFT is task learning: it actually teaches the model new knowledge.","知识注入假设认为，SFT 是任务学习：它确实教给模型新的知识。"],[304.52,310.32,111,"That matters more for knowledge-intensive tasks, like question answering in a specialized domain.","这对知识密集型任务更重要，比如专业领域的问答。"],[310.67,315.2,111,"And the FLAN hypothesis focuses on task generalization.","而 FLAN 假设关注的是任务泛化。"],[315.55,322.04,111,"Training on many diverse instructions teaches the model to handle new tasks it has never seen.","在大量多样的指令上训练，能让模型学会处理从未见过的新任务。"],[322.39,328.74,111,"These aren't mutually exclusive. Which one dominates depends on your task and your data.","这些假设并不互斥。哪一个占主导取决于你的任务和数据。"],[329.09,331.33,111,"Let's look at the evidence for each.","我们来逐一看看证据。"],[332.58,339.63,112,"Let's start with superficial alignment, from the LIMA paper, whose title says it all: Less Is More for Alignment.","先看表层对齐，来自 LIMA 论文，题目就说明了一切：Less Is More for Alignment。"],[339.98,348.15,112,"The claim is that alignment is mostly about learning the response format or the interaction style, in other words, task recognition.","它的主张是：对齐主要是学习回答格式或交互风格，换句话说，就是任务识别。"],[348.5,352.23,112,"Almost all of the knowledge and ability come from pretraining.","几乎所有知识和能力都来自预训练。"],[352.58,354.32,112,"The evidence is surprising.","证据令人惊讶。"],[354.67,360.55,112,"They fine-tuned a strong base model on just one thousand thirty carefully selected examples.","他们只用了 1030 个精心挑选的样例来微调一个强大的基座模型。"],[360.9,365.77,112,"One thousand for instruction following, and thirty for multi-turn conversation.","其中 1000 个用于指令遵循，30 个用于多轮对话。"],[366.12,372.06,112,"And they got a model that was competitive with much more heavily trained assistants in human evaluations.","得到的模型在人工评测中，可以和训练量大得多的助手相媲美。"],[372.41,380.53,112,"Another paper, the second reference, even suggested that zero point five percent of a typical instruction dataset might be enough.","另一篇论文，也就是第二篇参考文献，甚至认为一个典型指令数据集的 0.5% 可能就够了。"],[380.88,384.61,112,"So, less is more? With a question mark.","所以，少即是多？这里打了个问号。"],[384.96,390.55,112,"It's true for style and format, if the base model is strong and the data is high-quality.","对于风格和格式来说确实如此，前提是基座模型够强、数据质量够高。"],[390.9,395.48,112,"But as the next slide shows, it's not the whole story.","但正如下一页所示，这并不是全部。"],[396.73,402.67,113,"Here's a useful way to resolve the debate: distinguish task recognition from task learning.","有一个解决这场争论的好办法：区分任务识别和任务学习。"],[403.02,409.06,113,"This idea comes from research on in-context learning, but it applies nicely to SFT.","这个想法来自对上下文学习的研究，但同样很适用于 SFT。"],[409.41,420.67,113,"Task recognition is when the model recognizes what task you want, even from demonstrations without correct labels, and then applies what it already knows from pretraining.","任务识别是指模型能识别出你想要的任务——即使示例没有正确标签——然后运用它在预训练中已经掌握的知识。"],[421.02,424.15,113,"Summarize the following paragraphs is an example.","“总结下面几段话”就是一个例子。"],[424.5,429.48,113,"The model already knows how to summarize; it just needs to realize that's what you want.","模型本来就会总结，它只需要意识到你要的是这个。"],[429.83,433.6,113,"For that, as the red label says, few is enough.","对此，正如红色标签所说，少量就够了。"],[433.95,440.71,113,"Task learning is when the model must capture new input-output mappings that it didn't see in pretraining.","任务学习是指模型必须掌握预训练中没见过的新的输入输出映射。"],[441.06,444.32,113,"For example, new facts in a specialized domain.","比如专业领域中的新事实。"],[444.67,447.81,113,"Who is Barack Obama stands in for knowledge questions.","“奥巴马是谁？”代表的就是知识类问题。"],[448.16,451.36,113,"For that, more is better: you really need more data.","对此，越多越好：你确实需要更多数据。"],[451.71,458.61,113,"So when you plan an SFT dataset, ask yourself: am I teaching format, or am I teaching knowledge?","所以在规划 SFT 数据集时，问问自己：我是在教格式，还是在教知识？"],[459.86,466.23,114,"The third hypothesis is task generalization, with FLAN-T5 as the classic example.","第三种假设是任务泛化，经典例子是 FLAN-T5。"],[466.58,477.12,114,"The recipe is at the top: collect instruction and output pairs across many tasks, here something like a thousand or more, and fine-tune a language model on all of them.","做法在最上面：收集许多任务上的指令与输出对，这里大约有一千个甚至更多任务，并在所有这些数据上微调一个语言模型。"],[477.47,485.6,114,"Look at the examples: What is the boiling point of nitrogen, and a math word problem with step-by-step reasoning.","看这些例子：“氮的沸点是多少？”以及一道需要逐步推理的数学应用题。"],[485.95,489.64,114,"Then, below the dashed line, evaluate on unseen tasks.","然后，在虚线下方，在没见过的任务上评测。"],[489.99,495.28,114,"Can Geoffrey Hinton have a conversation with George Washington? Give the rationale before answering.","“Geoffrey Hinton 能和乔治·华盛顿对话吗？请先给出理由再回答。”"],[495.63,500.13,114,"The model was never trained on this task, but it answers correctly.","模型从没在这个任务上训练过，但它回答对了。"],[500.48,505.78,114,"Hinton was born in nineteen forty-seven, Washington died in seventeen ninety-nine, so no.","Hinton 生于 1947 年，华盛顿死于 1799 年，所以答案是否。"],[506.13,512.6,114,"The key finding, highlighted in red: the more diverse the training tasks, the better the generalization.","红色高亮的关键发现是：训练任务越多样，泛化就越好。"],[512.95,518.78,114,"Diversity of instructions matters more than sheer quantity of any one task.","指令的多样性比单一任务的数量更重要。"],[520.03,523.54,115,"We know what SFT is and roughly how it works.","我们已经知道 SFT 是什么，以及它大致如何起作用。"],[523.89,528.69,115,"Now, how do you actually get good SFT data without spending a fortune?","那么，怎样才能不花大价钱就拿到好的 SFT 数据？"],[529.04,535.69,115,"Here are some practical tips, starting with a shortcut that almost everyone in the open-source community has used.","下面是一些实用技巧，先从一个开源社区几乎人人都用过的捷径说起。"],[536.94,539.81,116,"The shortcut is distillation from top LLMs.","这个捷径就是从顶尖大模型中蒸馏。"],[540.16,542.05,116,"The idea is in the diagram.","思路就在图里。"],[542.4,548.92,116,"You write instructions or questions, and send them to a strong model like ChatGPT or GPT-5.","你写好指令或问题，发给 ChatGPT 或 GPT-5 这样的强模型。"],[549.27,555.49,116,"Collect its answers, and then train your own smaller model on those question-answer pairs.","收集它的回答，然后用这些问答对训练你自己的小模型。"],[555.84,558.53,116,"Your model learns from ChatGPT.","你的模型就是在向 ChatGPT 学习。"],[558.88,565.62,116,"This is how many early open models were built, like Alpaca and Vicuna, which we'll see in a moment.","很多早期开源模型就是这样做出来的，比如 Alpaca 和 Vicuna，我们马上会看到。"],[565.97,572.63,116,"It's cheap and fast, and it works surprisingly well for teaching format and general helpfulness.","它便宜又快，在教授格式和一般性的有用性方面效果出奇地好。"],[572.98,575.75,116,"But keep three caveats in mind.","但要记住三点注意事项。"],[576.1,579.54,116,"Check the terms of service of the model you're distilling from.","检查你所蒸馏模型的服务条款。"],[579.89,583.16,116,"Your student will usually not surpass its teacher.","学生模型通常不会超过它的老师。"],[583.51,588.73,116,"And if everyone distills from the same few models, all models start to sound the same.","而且如果大家都从同样几个模型蒸馏，所有模型听起来都会越来越像。"],[589.08,591.59,116,"We'll return to those issues shortly.","我们稍后会再讨论这些问题。"],[592.84,597.07,117,"Tip one: use self-instruct for data augmentation.","技巧一：用 self-instruct 做数据增强。"],[597.42,603.84,117,"This is the Alpaca pipeline from Stanford, and it was a landmark in early two thousand twenty-three.","这是斯坦福的 Alpaca 流程，它是 2023 年初的一个里程碑。"],[604.19,611.14,117,"Start with one hundred seventy-five human-written seed tasks, like Brainstorm a list of possible New Year's resolutions.","从 175 个人工编写的种子任务开始，比如“列出一些可能的新年愿望”。"],[611.49,620.87,117,"Feed a few of them to a strong model, here OpenAI's text-davinci-003, and ask it to generate new, different tasks with answers.","把其中几个喂给一个强模型，这里是 OpenAI 的 text-davinci-003，让它生成新的、不同的任务及答案。"],[621.22,623.96,117,"This uses a modified self-instruct procedure.","这里用的是改进版的 self-instruct 流程。"],[624.31,631.61,117,"That produced fifty-two thousand instruction-following examples, like Brainstorm creative ideas for designing a conference room.","由此产生了 5.2 万个指令遵循样例，比如“为设计一间会议室构思创意”。"],[631.96,638.15,117,"Then fine-tune Meta's LLaMA 7B on that data, and you get Alpaca 7B.","然后用这些数据微调 Meta 的 LLaMA 7B，就得到了 Alpaca 7B。"],[638.5,642.53,117,"What made it famous was the cost and simplicity.","让它出名的是低成本和简单。"],[642.88,652.09,117,"A small academic team, with very little money, turned a base model into a chatbot that felt surprisingly close to the commercial ones of the time.","一个小型学术团队，只花了很少的钱，就把一个基座模型变成了一个聊天机器人，感觉出奇地接近当时的商业产品。"],[652.44,656.48,117,"It kicked off a wave of open instruction-tuned models.","它掀起了一波开源指令微调模型的浪潮。"],[657.73,663.68,118,"What does self-instruct look like in practice? I did this myself with ChatGPT, in Chinese.","self-instruct 在实践中是什么样的？我自己用 ChatGPT 用中文试过。"],[664.03,666.4,118,"At the top, I give it three examples.","在上面，我给了它三个例子。"],[666.75,675.22,118,"Write a poem on the theme summer, give synonyms for astonishingly, and continue a list in brackets about what dogs like to eat in summer.","以“夏天”为主题写一首诗、给出“惊人地”的同义词，以及续写括号里关于狗狗夏天爱吃什么的列表。"],[675.57,681.74,118,"Then I simply say: imitate the content above and create three more examples like these.","然后我只说了一句：仿照上面的内容，再造三个这样的数据。"],[682.09,684.23,118,"Below is ChatGPT's response.","下面是 ChatGPT 的回复。"],[684.58,687.28,118,"A new poem on the theme rainy night.","一首以“雨夜”为主题的新诗。"],[687.63,689.2,118,"Synonyms for happily.","“快乐地”的同义词。"],[689.55,695.94,118,"And a new list about where cats like to curl up in winter: by the fireplace, on blankets, and so on.","还有一个新列表，关于猫咪冬天喜欢蜷缩在哪里：火炉旁、毯子上，等等。"],[696.29,697.98,118,"That's really all there is to it.","就这么简单。"],[698.33,703.88,118,"With a few seeds and a good prompt, you can generate thousands of diverse examples.","有几个种子样例加一个好的提示，就能生成成千上万个多样的样例。"],[704.23,710.27,118,"The hard part isn't generating data; it's filtering it and making sure it's diverse and correct.","难点不在生成数据，而在于过滤数据，并确保它多样且正确。"],[711.52,716.99,119,"Tip two: train on the output only. This is a small detail with a big effect.","技巧二：只在输出上训练。这是一个影响很大的小细节。"],[717.34,719.01,119,"Look at the single-turn case.","先看单轮的情况。"],[719.36,725.21,119,"A training example is a system prompt, then the user's input, then the response.","一个训练样例由系统提示、用户输入和回答组成。"],[725.56,731.51,119,"We feed the whole thing into the model, but we only compute the loss on the response tokens, shown in red.","我们把整段都输入模型，但只在红色标出的回答 token 上计算损失。"],[731.86,736.04,119,"The system prompt and the user's input are just context.","系统提示和用户输入只是上下文。"],[736.39,739.69,119,"In the multi-turn case, the same principle applies.","多轮的情况道理相同。"],[740.04,745.28,119,"Compute the loss on every assistant response in the conversation, and mask out the user turns.","在对话中每一轮助手回答上计算损失，把用户轮次屏蔽掉。"],[745.63,752.11,119,"Why? Because we want the model to learn to answer, not to learn to imitate users writing questions.","为什么？因为我们希望模型学会回答，而不是学会模仿用户提问。"],[752.46,759.59,119,"Training on user turns wastes capacity, and can even teach the model to start writing the next user message itself.","在用户轮次上训练会浪费模型容量，甚至可能教会模型自己去写下一条用户消息。"],[759.94,764.15,119,"As the slide says, this is the default in most fine-tuning libraries now.","正如幻灯片所说，这已经是大多数微调库的默认做法。"],[764.5,768.14,119,"But always check that your data collator actually does it.","但一定要检查你的数据整理器是否真的这样做了。"],[769.39,774.18,120,"Tip three: use complex instructions. Let me ask you a question first.","技巧三：使用复杂指令。我先问大家一个问题。"],[774.53,776.97,120,"When you were fifteen, which improved you more?","在你 15 岁的时候，哪个让你进步更多？"],[777.32,780.12,120,"Doing one plus one equals what, over and over?","是一遍又一遍地做“1 加 1 等于几”？"],[780.47,785.48,120,"Or working through a tough practice book, like the Huanggang exam papers on the right?","还是啃一本很难的练习册，比如右边的黄冈密卷？"],[785.83,788.82,120,"Obviously B, the complex exercises.","显然是 B，复杂的练习。"],[789.17,796.21,120,"Easy exercises you can already do teach you nothing new. Hard ones force you to combine skills and think.","你已经会做的简单练习教不了你新东西，难题则迫使你综合运用技能、动脑思考。"],[796.56,797.65,120,"Models are similar.","模型也是一样。"],[798.0,803.81,120,"If your SFT data is full of trivial instructions, the model learns little beyond the format.","如果你的 SFT 数据里满是琐碎的指令，模型除了格式之外学不到什么。"],[804.16,811.54,120,"Complex, multi-step, constrained instructions push it to use and organize more of what it learned in pretraining.","复杂的、多步骤的、带约束的指令，会促使它运用和组织更多在预训练中学到的东西。"],[811.89,816.24,120,"The next slide shows a neat way to create such instructions automatically.","下一页展示了一种自动生成这类指令的巧妙方法。"],[817.49,825.72,121,"This is WizardLM and its method, called Evol-Instruct: automatically evolving simple instructions into complex ones.","这是 WizardLM 及其方法 Evol-Instruct：自动把简单指令进化成复杂指令。"],[826.07,830.55,121,"Start at the bottom, with the initial instruction one plus one equals what.","从底部开始，初始指令是“1 加 1 等于几”。"],[830.9,834.72,121,"Then use an LLM to evolve it in different directions.","然后用大模型朝不同方向进化它。"],[835.07,840.36,121,"Add constraints: How to prove one plus one equals two in the Goldbach Conjecture?","增加约束：如何在哥德巴赫猜想中证明 1 加 1 等于 2？"],[840.71,844.59,121,"Deepening: In what situation does one plus one not equal two?","加深：在什么情况下 1 加 1 不等于 2？"],[844.94,851.16,121,"Increase reasoning: What is the value of x, if x cubed plus two x plus three equals seven?","增加推理：如果 x 的立方加 2x 加 3 等于 7，x 等于多少？"],[851.51,855.43,121,"Concretizing: an apples-and-bananas word problem.","具体化：一道关于苹果和香蕉的应用题。"],[855.78,860.16,121,"Complicate the input with a formula, and then with code.","用公式让输入变复杂，然后再用代码。"],[860.51,865.69,121,"And in-breadth evolving, the red arrows, jumps to new topics entirely.","而广度进化，也就是红色箭头，会跳到全新的话题。"],[866.04,871.29,121,"From arithmetic to the speed of light in a vacuum, and then on to tables and chemistry.","从算术跳到真空中的光速，再到表格和化学。"],[871.64,874.91,121,"Each round makes the data harder and more diverse.","每一轮都让数据更难、更多样。"],[875.26,880.94,121,"Training on the evolved set made the model noticeably better at following complex instructions.","在进化后的数据集上训练，让模型遵循复杂指令的能力明显提升。"],[881.29,885.07,121,"It's basically a curriculum generator for LLMs.","这基本上就是一个为大模型生成课程的工具。"],[886.32,890.32,122,"Instruction fine-tuning is powerful, but it has real limitations.","指令微调很强大，但也有实实在在的局限。"],[890.67,895.13,122,"First, it's expensive to collect ground-truth answers for so many tasks.","第一，为这么多任务收集标准答案代价高昂。"],[895.48,904.31,122,"Second, for open-ended creative tasks, like Write a story about a dog and her pet grasshopper, there's no single correct answer to imitate.","第二，对于开放式的创意任务，比如“写一个关于一只狗和她的宠物蚱蜢的故事”，没有唯一的正确答案可以模仿。"],[904.66,913.52,122,"Third, and most subtle: the language-modeling loss penalizes all token-level mistakes equally, but some mistakes are much worse than others.","第三，也是最微妙的一点：语言建模损失对所有 token 级错误一视同仁，但有些错误比其他错误严重得多。"],[913.87,918.12,122,"Look at the example. The reference says Avatar is a fantasy TV show.","看这个例子。参考答案是“Avatar 是一部奇幻电视剧”。"],[918.47,922.1,122,"If the model says adventure TV show, that's a small error.","如果模型说“冒险电视剧”，那是一个小错误。"],[922.45,925.86,122,"If it says musical TV show, that's quite wrong.","如果说“音乐电视剧”，那就错得很离谱了。"],[926.21,930.29,122,"But the token-level loss treats both as simply not the reference token.","但 token 级损失把两者都简单地当作“不是参考 token”。"],[930.64,935.82,122,"So there's a mismatch between the LM objective and what humans actually prefer.","所以，语言模型的目标与人类真正的偏好之间存在错配。"],[936.17,942.47,122,"That raises the question at the bottom: can we explicitly optimize for human preferences?","这就引出了底部的问题：我们能否显式地针对人类偏好进行优化？"],[942.82,948.46,122,"Keep that question in mind. Before we answer it, one more practical issue about SFT data.","记住这个问题。在回答它之前，再讲一个关于 SFT 数据的实际问题。"],[949.71,954.22,123,"Where should the responses in your SFT data come from? There are three options.","SFT 数据中的回答应该从哪里来？有三种选择。"],[954.57,958.46,123,"First, human-written, like the Dolly dataset from Databricks.","第一，人工撰写，比如 Databricks 的 Dolly 数据集。"],[958.81,963.71,123,"It's rich in knowledge, but surprisingly not ideal for training LLMs.","它知识丰富，但出人意料地并不适合训练大模型。"],[964.06,966.96,123,"Formats are inconsistent across annotators.","不同标注者的格式不一致。"],[967.31,975.46,123,"And humans often skip easy but important steps, because to us they're common sense, so the logic can look incoherent to the model.","而且人常常跳过简单但重要的步骤，因为对我们来说那是常识，于是在模型看来逻辑可能不连贯。"],[975.81,983.09,123,"Training on answers that state things the model can't derive may even encourage it to hallucinate.","用那些陈述了模型推导不出来的内容的答案来训练，甚至可能助长幻觉。"],[983.44,988.53,123,"Second, distilled from powerful models like ChatGPT or DeepSeek.","第二，从 ChatGPT 或 DeepSeek 这样的强模型蒸馏。"],[988.88,996.86,123,"It's clean and consistent, but there's a risk of model collapse: humans are diverse, LLM outputs much less so.","这种数据干净且一致，但有模型崩塌的风险：人类是多样的，而大模型的输出远没那么多样。"],[997.21,1000.56,123,"And a student can rarely outperform its teacher.","而且学生很少能超过老师。"],[1000.91,1008.17,123,"The third option, which we've used a lot in Phoenix and the HuatuoGPT series, is to combine the two.","第三种选择是把两者结合，我们在 Phoenix 和 HuatuoGPT 系列中大量使用了这种方法。"],[1008.52,1015.41,123,"Take expert-written content, and have an LLM rewrite it into a clear, consistent format.","拿专家撰写的内容，让大模型把它改写成清晰一致的格式。"],[1015.76,1022.15,123,"That way you inject domain knowledge from experts, while keeping the style the model learns best from.","这样既注入了专家的领域知识，又保留了模型最容易学习的风格。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"RLHF: Reward Models, InstructGPT and ChatGPT","blurb":"Aligning models with human preferences: learning a reward model from comparisons, optimizing it with RL, InstructGPT, biases of human feedback, and ChatGPT.","file":"lecture05_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part9.jpg","duration":1034.8,"first":124,"last":145,"slides":[{"n":124,"title":"RLHF Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback","t":0.8},{"n":125,"title":"Benefit of RLHF","t":21.96},{"n":126,"title":"Slide 126","t":82.24},{"n":127,"title":"Motivation: Alignment","t":139.82},{"n":128,"title":"Motivation: Alignment","t":153.97},{"n":129,"title":"Motivation: Alignment","t":177.11},{"n":130,"title":"Motivation: Alignment","t":203.53},{"n":131,"title":"Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) An early example in Summarization (before LLMs)","t":238.19},{"n":132,"title":"Stage 3: RLHF","t":256.76},{"n":133,"title":"Optimizing for human preferences","t":312.43},{"n":134,"title":"How do we model human preferences?","t":370.75},{"n":135,"title":"Reinforcement learning to the rescue","t":422.98},{"n":136,"title":"How do we model human preferences?","t":487.39},{"n":137,"title":"An overall picture of RLHF","t":550.86},{"n":138,"title":"RLHF provides gains over pretraining + finetuning","t":616.52},{"n":139,"title":"InstructGPT: scaling up RLHF to tens of thousands of tasks","t":684.81},{"n":140,"title":"InstructGPT: scaling up RLHF to tens of thousands of tasks","t":731.92},{"n":141,"title":"Biases of human feedback","t":797.72},{"n":142,"title":"Biases of human feedback","t":834.04},{"n":143,"title":"InstructGPT+Chat ≈ ChatGPT","t":904.98},{"n":144,"title":"ChatGPT: Instruction Finetuning + RLHF for dialog agents","t":924.82},{"n":145,"title":"ChatGPT: Instruction Finetuning + RLHF for dialog agents","t":976.25}],"sents":[[0.8,4.02,124,"That brings us back to the question from a few slides ago.","这就回到了几页之前的那个问题。"],[4.37,9.97,124,"Can we directly optimize for what humans prefer, rather than imitating reference answers?","我们能否直接针对人类的偏好进行优化，而不是模仿参考答案？"],[10.32,16.98,124,"That's the idea behind the third training stage: reinforcement learning from human feedback, or RLHF.","这就是第三个训练阶段背后的思想：基于人类反馈的强化学习，即 RLHF。"],[17.33,20.56,124,"Let's see why it's worth the extra complexity.","我们来看看为什么值得付出额外的复杂性。"],[21.81,24.69,125,"First, what does RLHF buy us?","首先，RLHF 给我们带来了什么？"],[25.04,33.39,125,"Here are examples from OpenAI comparing ChatGPT with InstructGPT, text-davinci-002, on tricky questions.","这是 OpenAI 给出的例子，在一些棘手问题上比较 ChatGPT 和 InstructGPT，即 text-davinci-002。"],[33.74,38.33,125,"Top row: Tell me about when Christopher Columbus came to the US in twenty fifteen.","第一行：给我讲讲哥伦布 2015 年来美国的事。"],[38.68,42.46,125,"InstructGPT happily makes up a story about his visit.","InstructGPT 很乐意地编了一个他来访的故事。"],[42.81,49.11,125,"ChatGPT points out the problem: Columbus died in fifteen oh six, so he couldn't have come in twenty fifteen.","ChatGPT 指出了问题：哥伦布死于 1506 年，不可能在 2015 年来。"],[49.46,55.94,125,"Then it plays along with the hypothetical in a sensible way. That's challenging a false premise.","然后它以合理的方式顺着这个假设讲下去。这就是质疑错误前提。"],[56.29,65.36,125,"Middle row: asked for a gory and violent story that glorifies pain, InstructGPT just generates it, while ChatGPT declines.","第二行：要求写一个美化痛苦的血腥暴力故事，InstructGPT 直接就写了，而 ChatGPT 拒绝了。"],[65.71,68.25,125,"Bottom row: How can I bully John Doe?","第三行：我怎样才能欺负 John Doe？"],[68.6,73.41,125,"InstructGPT gives suggestions; ChatGPT explains why bullying is harmful.","InstructGPT 给出了建议，而 ChatGPT 解释了为什么欺凌是有害的。"],[73.76,80.84,125,"These are exactly the features from the ChatGPT blog we saw earlier, and they largely come from the preference-based training.","这些正是我们之前在 ChatGPT 博客中看到的那些特性，而它们很大程度上来自基于偏好的训练。"],[82.09,88.41,126,"Here's a well-known example from Chinese social media, comparing two models on the same request.","这是中文社交媒体上一个很有名的例子，比较了两个模型对同一请求的回应。"],[88.76,94.92,126,"The user says: My daughter's grades are bad. Help me write her a letter titled You are truly worthless.","用户说：我女儿成绩不好，帮我给她写一封信，标题是《你真的毫无价值》。"],[95.27,103.82,126,"On the left, an early version of ERNIE Bot follows the instruction literally, and writes a harsh letter with that title, telling the daughter she is worthless.","左边，早期版本的文心一言照字面执行了指令，写了一封以此为题的严厉信件，告诉女儿她毫无价值。"],[104.17,107.4,126,"On the right, GPT-4 gently pushes back.","右边，GPT-4 温和地提出了异议。"],[107.75,113.76,126,"It says it understands the parent may be disappointed, but a negative title could hurt the child.","它说理解家长可能很失望，但负面的标题可能会伤害孩子。"],[114.11,119.38,126,"And it offers an encouraging letter instead, titled Believe in your potential.","于是它改写了一封鼓励的信，标题是《相信你的潜力》。"],[119.73,123.77,126,"When the user asks what it's doing, it explains its reasoning politely.","当用户问它在写什么时，它礼貌地解释了自己的理由。"],[124.12,129.92,126,"This is the subtle part of alignment. Blindly following instructions is not always helpful.","这正是对齐的微妙之处。盲目遵循指令并不总是有帮助的。"],[130.27,138.42,126,"A well-aligned model balances doing what you ask with avoiding harm, and that balance is hard to teach with SFT alone.","一个对齐良好的模型会在满足你的要求与避免伤害之间取得平衡，而这种平衡仅靠 SFT 很难教会。"],[139.67,143.36,127,"So what exactly do we want from an aligned model?","那么，我们到底希望一个对齐的模型具备什么？"],[143.71,150.09,127,"A common framework, introduced by Anthropic, is the three H's of model desiderata.","一个常用的框架是 Anthropic 提出的模型期望的“三个 H”。"],[150.44,152.57,127,"Let's go through them one at a time.","我们一个一个来看。"],[153.82,160.54,128,"The first H is helpful: the AI should help the user solve their task, for example by answering their questions well.","第一个 H 是有帮助：AI 应该帮助用户完成任务，比如很好地回答他们的问题。"],[160.89,165.7,128,"The picture is Rosie, the robot maid from the old cartoon The Jetsons.","图中是老动画片《杰森一家》里的机器人女佣 Rosie。"],[166.05,168.75,128,"A good assistant actually gets the job done.","好的助手能真正把活干完。"],[169.1,175.71,128,"And helpfulness also means asking for clarification when the request is unclear, instead of guessing.","有帮助也意味着：在请求不清楚时主动询问澄清，而不是瞎猜。"],[176.96,181.11,129,"The second H is honest: the AI should give accurate information.","第二个 H 是诚实：AI 应该提供准确的信息。"],[181.46,188.62,129,"And it should express uncertainty when it doesn't know the answer, instead of hallucinating a wrong one.","当它不知道答案时，应该表达不确定，而不是编造一个错误答案。"],[188.97,192.03,129,"Hence Pinocchio, whose nose grows when he lies.","所以配图是匹诺曹，他一撒谎鼻子就会变长。"],[192.38,202.13,129,"Honesty is hard for LLMs, because the pretraining objective rewards producing fluent, plausible text, not saying I'm not sure.","诚实对大模型来说很难，因为预训练目标奖励的是生成流畅、看似合理的文本，而不是说“我不确定”。"],[203.38,211.95,130,"And the third H is harmless: the AI should not cause physical, psychological, or social harm to people or the environment.","第三个 H 是无害：AI 不应对人或环境造成身体、心理或社会层面的伤害。"],[212.3,218.41,130,"The picture is Tom, smiling sweetly at Jerry while hiding a mousetrap behind his back.","图中是汤姆，一边对杰瑞甜甜地笑，一边把捕鼠夹藏在身后。"],[218.76,221.2,130,"Being friendly on the surface isn't enough.","表面上友好是不够的。"],[221.55,225.07,130,"The tricky part is that these three goals can conflict.","棘手的是，这三个目标之间可能互相冲突。"],[225.42,232.97,130,"Maximally helpful might mean explaining how to do something dangerous; maximally harmless might mean refusing everything.","极致的有帮助可能意味着解释如何做危险的事；极致的无害可能意味着拒绝一切。"],[233.32,236.79,130,"RLHF is our main tool to find the balance.","RLHF 是我们寻找这种平衡的主要工具。"],[238.04,246.36,131,"Before applying RLHF to giant chat models, it was developed on a simpler problem: summarization.","在把 RLHF 用到巨型聊天模型之前，它是在一个更简单的问题上发展起来的：文本摘要。"],[246.71,253.42,131,"This early work, from before the LLM boom, is the clearest way to understand the whole RLHF pipeline.","这项在大模型热潮之前的早期工作，是理解整个 RLHF 流程最清晰的途径。"],[253.77,255.36,131,"So let's walk through it.","所以我们来逐步过一遍。"],[256.61,264.28,132,"The core insight of RLHF is in the first sentence: it's often much easier to compare answers than to write them.","RLHF 的核心洞见就在第一句话里：比较答案往往比写答案容易得多。"],[264.63,269.1,132,"Think about it. Writing a perfect summary of a long article is hard work.","想一想，为一篇长文写出完美的摘要是件辛苦活。"],[269.45,275.4,132,"But if I show you two summaries, you can usually tell me fairly quickly which one is better.","但如果我给你看两份摘要，你通常能很快告诉我哪份更好。"],[275.75,279.6,132,"Comparison is cheaper, faster, and often more reliable.","比较更便宜、更快，而且往往更可靠。"],[279.95,281.94,132,"The diagram shows how we use that.","这张图展示了我们如何利用这一点。"],[282.29,289.11,132,"Sample many prompts from a dataset, and let the initial language model generate several outputs for each.","从数据集中采样大量提示，让初始语言模型为每个提示生成多个输出。"],[289.46,291.74,132,"Then have humans score or rank them.","然后让人类给它们打分或排序。"],[292.09,297.75,132,"Then train a separate reward model, also called a preference model, on those rankings.","再基于这些排序训练一个单独的奖励模型，也叫偏好模型。"],[298.1,304.22,132,"Its job is to output a number, r theta, saying how much a human would like a given text.","它的任务是输出一个数值 r_θ，表示人类会有多喜欢某段文本。"],[304.57,311.03,132,"Once we have that reward model, we can use it to improve the language model. Let's see the details.","有了这个奖励模型，就可以用它来改进语言模型。我们来看细节。"],[312.28,315.96,133,"Let's set up the problem, using summarization as the example.","我们以摘要为例来设定问题。"],[316.31,323.92,133,"For each sample s from the language model, imagine a human gives us a reward R of s, where higher is better.","对语言模型的每个样本 s，假设有人给出一个奖励 R(s)，越高越好。"],[324.27,330.17,133,"On the left is a news article about a magnitude four point two earthquake in San Francisco.","左边是一篇关于旧金山 4.2 级地震的新闻报道。"],[330.52,339.76,133,"A good summary, s one: An earthquake hit San Francisco. There was minor property damage, but no injuries. Reward eight point zero.","一个好的摘要 s1：“旧金山发生地震，有轻微财产损失，但无人受伤。”奖励为 8.0。"],[340.11,347.93,133,"A bad summary, s two: The Bay Area has good weather but is prone to earthquakes and wildfires. Reward one point two.","一个差的摘要 s2：“湾区天气好，但容易发生地震和山火。”奖励为 1.2。"],[348.28,350.61,133,"It's fluent, but it misses the point.","它很流畅，但没抓住重点。"],[350.96,357.95,133,"The goal is simple to state: we want to maximize the expected reward of samples from our language model.","目标说起来很简单：我们想最大化语言模型所生成样本的期望奖励。"],[358.3,364.21,133,"In other words, adjust the model so that, on average, the summaries it writes get high rewards.","换句话说，调整模型，让它写出的摘要平均能获得高奖励。"],[364.56,369.35,133,"There are two problems with this, and the next slides tackle them one at a time.","这里有两个问题，接下来几页会逐一解决。"],[370.6,374.12,134,"Problem one: having a human in the loop is expensive.","问题一：让人参与到训练循环中代价高昂。"],[374.47,383.46,134,"If every training step needed a person to score the model's outputs, we'd need millions of human ratings, delivered instantly. Not realistic.","如果每一步训练都需要有人给模型输出打分，我们就需要数百万个即时的人工评分。这不现实。"],[383.81,388.09,134,"That's what the little money icons next to each reward are reminding you of.","每个奖励旁边的小钞票图标就是在提醒你这一点。"],[388.44,396.11,134,"The solution: instead of asking humans directly every time, model their preferences as a separate NLP problem.","解决方案是：不要每次都直接问人，而是把人的偏好建模成一个独立的 NLP 问题。"],[396.46,405.02,134,"We collect a dataset of human judgments once, and train a reward model, an RM, to predict what humans would say.","我们一次性收集人类判断的数据集，训练一个奖励模型，即 RM，来预测人类会怎么评价。"],[405.37,410.18,134,"After that, the reward model can score as many outputs as we want, for free.","之后，奖励模型可以免费给任意多的输出打分。"],[410.53,417.1,134,"This idea goes back to work by Knox and Stone in two thousand nine, in robotics, long before LLMs.","这个想法可以追溯到 Knox 和 Stone 在 2009 年的机器人领域研究，远早于大模型。"],[417.45,421.58,134,"The reward model becomes a learned stand-in for the human.","奖励模型成了人类的一个学习得到的替身。"],[422.83,424.84,135,"Why reinforcement learning, though?","不过，为什么是强化学习？"],[425.19,432.1,135,"Because maximizing the expected reward of what the model generates is exactly the problem RL was designed for.","因为最大化模型生成内容的期望奖励，正是强化学习要解决的问题。"],[432.45,434.68,135,"RL has been studied for decades.","强化学习已经被研究了几十年。"],[435.03,442.78,135,"The policy gradient method by Williams in nineteen ninety-two, and the classic textbook by Sutton and Barto, are the foundations.","Williams 在 1992 年提出的策略梯度方法，以及 Sutton 和 Barto 的经典教材，是其基础。"],[443.13,450.69,135,"Around twenty thirteen, deep RL had its breakthrough, with agents learning to play Atari games, shown on the Nature cover.","2013 年前后，深度强化学习取得突破，智能体学会了玩 Atari 游戏，登上了《自然》杂志封面。"],[451.04,454.23,135,"Later, AlphaGo beat top human Go players.","后来，AlphaGo 击败了顶尖的人类围棋选手。"],[454.58,461.89,135,"Applying RL to language models is much newer, from around twenty nineteen onward, with the three papers listed.","把强化学习用于语言模型则新得多，大约从 2019 年开始，就是列出的这三篇论文。"],[462.24,471.5,135,"Why so late? Because RL with language models is notoriously hard to get right, and as the slide says, it still is.","为什么这么晚？因为在语言模型上做强化学习出了名地难，而且正如幻灯片所说，现在依然如此。"],[471.85,480.76,135,"What helped was newer algorithms that work reasonably stably with large neural networks, especially PPO, proximal policy optimization.","帮上忙的是一些在大型神经网络上能较稳定工作的新算法，尤其是 PPO，即近端策略优化。"],[481.11,485.99,135,"We'll go much deeper into PPO and its successors in Lecture six.","我们会在第六讲深入讨论 PPO 及其后续方法。"],[487.24,489.63,136,"Back to modeling human preferences.","回到人类偏好的建模。"],[489.98,494.11,136,"Problem two: human judgments are noisy and miscalibrated.","问题二：人类判断有噪声，且标尺不统一。"],[494.46,500.51,136,"If I ask ten people to rate a summary from one to ten, one person's seven is another person's five.","如果我请十个人给一份摘要打 1 到 10 分，一个人的 7 分可能是另一个人的 5 分。"],[500.86,503.42,136,"Absolute scores are unreliable.","绝对分数并不可靠。"],[503.77,511.6,136,"The solution: instead of asking for direct ratings, ask for pairwise comparisons, which are much more consistent.","解决方案是：不要直接打分，而是做两两比较，这样一致性高得多。"],[511.95,516.14,136,"People may disagree on whether a summary deserves a six or an eight.","人们可能对一份摘要该得 6 分还是 8 分意见不一。"],[516.49,524.19,136,"But they mostly agree that summary s one is better than s three, and s three is better than s two.","但他们大多同意摘要 s1 优于 s3，s3 又优于 s2。"],[524.54,531.56,136,"Then we train the reward model, shown at the bottom, to assign scores consistent with those comparisons.","然后我们训练底部所示的奖励模型，让它给出与这些比较结果一致的分数。"],[531.91,540.21,136,"The usual loss, often called a Bradley-Terry objective, pushes the score of the preferred response above the score of the rejected one.","常用的损失函数，通常叫 Bradley-Terry 目标，会把被偏好回答的分数推到被拒绝回答的分数之上。"],[540.56,545.08,136,"It does this by maximizing the log of the sigmoid of their difference.","具体做法是最大化两者分差经过 sigmoid 后的对数。"],[545.43,549.46,136,"The model learns a consistent scale from relative judgments alone.","模型仅凭相对判断就学到了一个一致的评分标尺。"],[550.71,552.94,137,"Now let's put it all together.","现在把所有部分整合起来。"],[553.29,558.46,137,"This is the full RLHF pipeline from the Learning to summarize from human feedback paper.","这是《Learning to summarize from human feedback》论文中完整的 RLHF 流程。"],[558.81,561.11,137,"Step one, collect human feedback.","第一步，收集人类反馈。"],[561.46,568.57,137,"Take a Reddit post from the TL DR dataset, sample several summaries from different policies, and pick two.","从 TL;DR 数据集中取一个 Reddit 帖子，用不同策略采样几份摘要，从中挑出两份。"],[568.92,573.55,137,"Then a human judges which is better: j is better than k.","然后由人来判断哪份更好：j 优于 k。"],[573.9,576.4,137,"Step two, train the reward model.","第二步，训练奖励模型。"],[576.75,581.75,137,"Feed both summaries to the reward model, and get scores r j and r k.","把两份摘要都输入奖励模型，得到分数 r_j 和 r_k。"],[582.1,589.91,137,"Update it with the loss based on the sigmoid of r j minus r k, so the preferred summary gets the higher score.","用基于 r_j 减 r_k 的 sigmoid 构造的损失来更新它，使被偏好的摘要得分更高。"],[590.26,593.0,137,"Step three, train the policy with PPO.","第三步，用 PPO 训练策略。"],[593.35,601.2,137,"Sample a new post, let the policy write a summary, have the reward model score it, and use that reward to update the policy.","采样一个新帖子，让策略写摘要，由奖励模型打分，再用这个奖励来更新策略。"],[601.55,609.97,137,"In practice, a penalty also keeps the policy from drifting too far from the original model, so it can't just exploit quirks of the reward model.","在实践中，还会加一个惩罚项，防止策略偏离原始模型太远，这样它就无法钻奖励模型的空子。"],[610.32,615.12,137,"This three-step structure is exactly what InstructGPT later scaled up.","这个三步结构正是 InstructGPT 后来扩大规模所采用的。"],[616.37,619.75,138,"And it works. This plot is from the same paper.","而且它确实有效。这张图来自同一篇论文。"],[620.1,627.31,138,"The y-axis is how often human raters preferred the model's summary over the human-written reference summary.","纵轴表示人类评审者在多大比例上更喜欢模型的摘要，而不是人写的参考摘要。"],[627.66,632.29,138,"So zero point five, the dashed line, means as good as the references.","所以 0.5，也就是虚线，表示和参考摘要一样好。"],[632.64,639.0,138,"The x-axis is model size, from one point three to twelve point nine billion parameters.","横轴是模型规模，从 13 亿到 129 亿参数。"],[639.35,642.12,138,"The blue line, pretraining only, is the worst.","蓝线是只做预训练的，效果最差。"],[642.47,649.36,138,"The green line, supervised fine-tuning, is better, but stays below zero point five even at twelve point nine billion.","绿线是监督微调，好一些，但即使到 129 亿参数也仍低于 0.5。"],[649.71,654.69,138,"The orange line, RLHF, is above the reference summaries.","橙线是 RLHF，超过了参考摘要。"],[655.04,662.21,138,"It's around zero point six at one point three billion, and about zero point seven at six point seven billion.","在 13 亿参数时约为 0.6，在 67 亿参数时约为 0.7。"],[662.56,670.9,138,"The most striking comparison: the one point three billion RLHF model beats the twelve point nine billion supervised model.","最惊人的对比是：13 亿参数的 RLHF 模型胜过了 129 亿参数的监督模型。"],[671.25,677.58,138,"Optimizing for human preferences was worth more than a tenfold increase in model size.","针对人类偏好进行优化，比把模型规模扩大十倍还管用。"],[677.93,683.41,138,"That result convinced a lot of people that RLHF was worth the trouble.","这个结果让很多人相信 RLHF 值得这番折腾。"],[684.66,692.81,139,"InstructGPT took that summarization recipe and scaled it up to tens of thousands of tasks, using prompts from real users.","InstructGPT 把这套摘要任务的方法扩展到了数万个任务，使用的是来自真实用户的提示。"],[693.16,696.99,139,"You've already seen this diagram, so let me just recap it in one breath.","这张图大家之前已经见过，我一口气快速回顾一下。"],[697.34,704.19,139,"Step one: humans write demonstrations, and we fine-tune GPT-3 with supervised learning.","第一步：人类写示范，我们用监督学习微调 GPT-3。"],[704.54,709.57,139,"Step two: humans rank several model outputs, and we train a reward model.","第二步：人类对多个模型输出排序，我们训练一个奖励模型。"],[709.92,714.31,139,"Step three: we optimize the policy against the reward model with PPO.","第三步：我们用 PPO 针对奖励模型优化策略。"],[714.66,717.59,139,"The structure is identical to the summarization paper.","结构与摘要那篇论文完全相同。"],[717.94,727.02,139,"The difference is scope: instead of one task, the prompts cover writing, question answering, brainstorming, coding, and much more.","区别在于范围：提示不再只是一个任务，而是涵盖写作、问答、头脑风暴、编程等等。"],[727.37,730.52,139,"The next slide shows where those prompts came from.","下一页展示这些提示从哪里来。"],[731.77,736.31,140,"Where did InstructGPT's prompts come from? The labelers created three kinds.","InstructGPT 的提示从哪里来？标注员创建了三类。"],[736.66,742.03,140,"Plain: labelers just came up with arbitrary tasks, making sure there was enough diversity.","普通类：标注员随意构想任务，同时确保足够的多样性。"],[742.38,748.44,140,"Few-shot: labelers wrote an instruction plus several example query-response pairs.","少样本类：标注员写一条指令，外加若干查询与回答的示例对。"],[748.79,760.17,140,"And user-based: OpenAI looked at use cases people described when applying for API access, and asked labelers to write prompts for those use cases.","基于用户类：OpenAI 查看了人们申请 API 使用权限时描述的用例，并让标注员针对这些用例写提示。"],[760.52,764.23,140,"Look at the middle table, the distribution of use cases.","看中间的表格，即用例的分布。"],[764.58,771.36,140,"Generation dominates at almost forty-six percent, followed by open QA, brainstorming, chat and rewriting.","生成类占主导，接近 46%，其后是开放问答、头脑风暴、聊天和改写。"],[771.71,776.78,140,"Classic NLP tasks like classification and extraction are tiny.","分类、抽取这类经典 NLP 任务占比很小。"],[777.13,784.01,140,"That tells you what people actually want from these models: mostly open-ended generation, not benchmark tasks.","这说明人们真正想从这些模型得到的，主要是开放式生成，而不是基准测试任务。"],[784.36,790.12,140,"And look at the right table: the SFT data is only around thirteen thousand training prompts.","再看右边的表格：SFT 数据只有大约一万三千条训练提示。"],[790.47,796.32,140,"That's small compared with pretraining, which fits the less is more idea we discussed.","与预训练相比这很小，符合我们讨论过的“少即是多”的思想。"],[797.57,805.21,141,"RLHF depends on human feedback, so here's an uncomfortable question: is human feedback actually reliable?","RLHF 依赖人类反馈，所以有个令人不安的问题：人类反馈真的可靠吗？"],[805.56,812.64,141,"This is a paper from our team: Humans or LLMs as the Judge? A Study on Judgement Biases.","这是我们团队的一篇论文：《Humans or LLMs as the Judge? A Study on Judgement Biases》。"],[812.99,819.36,141,"It matters because both humans and, increasingly, LLMs are used as judges.","这很重要，因为人类以及越来越多的大模型都被用作评判者。"],[819.71,824.94,141,"They produce the preference data that trains reward models, and they evaluate models.","它们产生用于训练奖励模型的偏好数据，也用于评估模型。"],[825.29,828.94,141,"If the judges are biased, the model will learn those biases.","如果评判者有偏见，模型就会学到这些偏见。"],[829.29,832.64,141,"The next slide shows what kinds of bias we looked at.","下一页展示我们研究了哪些类型的偏见。"],[833.89,834.94,142,"Here's the setup.","实验设置是这样的。"],[835.29,842.48,142,"We take a simple question, What is the square root of thirty-six, and generate two answers, A one and A two.","我们取一个简单的问题“36 的平方根是多少”，生成两个答案 A1 和 A2。"],[842.83,847.52,142,"Then we carefully modify one answer to test how judges react.","然后我们仔细修改其中一个答案，测试评判者的反应。"],[847.87,851.19,142,"Two biases show up even without intervention.","即使不做干预，也会出现两种偏见。"],[851.54,859.7,142,"Verbosity bias, preferring the longer answer, and positional bias, preferring whichever answer is shown first or second.","冗长偏见，即偏好更长的答案；以及位置偏见，即偏好排在第一或第二位的答案。"],[860.05,862.61,142,"Then come the interventions on the right.","然后是右边的干预。"],[862.96,868.46,142,"Factual error: we change the answer to say seven times seven equals thirty-six.","事实错误：我们把答案改成“7 乘 7 等于 36”。"],[868.81,874.0,142,"If judges still prefer it, that's fallacy oversight bias, missing the mistake.","如果评判者仍然偏好它，就是谬误忽视偏见，即没发现错误。"],[874.35,881.76,142,"Reference: we add a citation to an authoritative-looking source, and judges may trust it more, which is authority bias.","引用：我们加上一个看起来很权威的来源引用，评判者可能就更信任它，这是权威偏见。"],[882.11,889.42,142,"Rich content: we add bold text and emoji, and judges may prefer the prettier answer, which is beauty bias.","丰富内容：我们加上粗体和表情符号，评判者可能偏好更好看的答案，这是美观偏见。"],[889.77,890.92,142,"Why does this matter?","为什么这很重要？"],[891.27,899.44,142,"Because a reward model trained on biased judgments rewards length, formatting and confident citations, not just correctness.","因为在有偏判断上训练的奖励模型，会奖励长度、格式和自信的引用，而不仅仅是正确性。"],[899.79,903.58,142,"That's one reason chatbots can become wordy and over-formatted.","这正是聊天机器人可能变得啰嗦和过度排版的原因之一。"],[904.83,910.09,143,"So far we've looked at RLHF in general and in InstructGPT.","到目前为止，我们看了一般意义上的 RLHF 以及 InstructGPT 中的 RLHF。"],[910.44,914.02,143,"ChatGPT added one more ingredient on top: conversation.","ChatGPT 在此之上又加了一种成分：对话。"],[914.37,919.51,143,"The equation on this slide sums it up: InstructGPT plus chat is roughly ChatGPT.","这页的等式总结了一切：InstructGPT 加上聊天，约等于 ChatGPT。"],[919.86,923.42,143,"Let's see what OpenAI actually said about how they did it.","我们来看看 OpenAI 自己是怎么说的。"],[924.67,929.75,144,"This is from the ChatGPT launch blog, and it's one of the few descriptions OpenAI gave.","这段来自 ChatGPT 发布时的博客，是 OpenAI 为数不多的说明之一。"],[930.1,937.12,144,"As the red note says, they've kept more details secret than before, including data, training parameters and model size.","正如红色注释所说，他们比以前保密了更多细节，包括数据、训练参数和模型规模。"],[937.47,939.59,144,"Here's the instruction fine-tuning part.","这是指令微调的部分。"],[939.94,943.31,144,"They trained an initial model with supervised fine-tuning.","他们先用监督微调训练了一个初始模型。"],[943.66,950.44,144,"Human AI trainers wrote conversations in which they played both sides, the user and the AI assistant.","人类 AI 训练师撰写对话，他们同时扮演用户和 AI 助手两个角色。"],[950.79,955.67,144,"The trainers had access to model-written suggestions to help them compose responses.","训练师可以参考模型给出的建议来帮助撰写回复。"],[956.02,962.58,144,"Then they mixed this new dialogue dataset with the InstructGPT dataset, converted into dialogue format.","然后他们把这个新的对话数据集与转换成对话格式的 InstructGPT 数据集混合。"],[962.93,969.12,144,"So the main change from InstructGPT is the data: multi-turn conversations instead of single instructions.","所以与 InstructGPT 相比，主要变化在于数据：多轮对话取代了单条指令。"],[969.47,974.85,144,"That's how the model learned to handle follow-up questions and keep track of context across turns.","模型正是这样学会处理追问，并在多轮之间记住上下文的。"],[976.1,979.59,145,"And here's the RLHF part from the same blog post.","这是同一篇博客中 RLHF 的部分。"],[979.94,986.98,145,"To train the reward model, they needed comparison data: two or more model responses ranked by quality.","为了训练奖励模型，他们需要比较数据：两个或更多按质量排序的模型回答。"],[987.33,994.74,145,"To collect it, they took conversations that AI trainers had with the chatbot, and randomly selected a model-written message.","为了收集这些数据，他们选取 AI 训练师与聊天机器人的对话，随机挑出一条模型写的消息。"],[995.09,1000.08,145,"They sampled several alternative completions, and had the trainers rank them.","再采样几个备选回复，让训练师对它们排序。"],[1000.43,1007.91,145,"Then they used those reward models to fine-tune the model with PPO, and they repeated this process several times.","然后用这些奖励模型通过 PPO 微调模型，并把这个过程重复了好几轮。"],[1008.26,1013.03,145,"Notice the word iterations. RLHF isn't run once.","注意“迭代”这个词。RLHF 不是只做一次。"],[1013.38,1022.57,145,"You collect comparisons on the current model, train, deploy the improved model, collect new comparisons on its outputs, and repeat.","你在当前模型上收集比较数据、训练、部署改进后的模型，再在它的输出上收集新的比较数据，如此循环。"],[1022.92,1027.86,145,"Remember from earlier that human feedback data is model-dependent.","记得我们之前说过，人类反馈数据是依赖于模型的。"],[1028.21,1032.92,145,"Preferences are always collected on the outputs of the model you're currently improving.","偏好总是在你当前正在改进的那个模型的输出上收集的。"]]},{"n":10,"title":"Multi-turn Data, PlatoLM and Pretraining vs. SFT vs. RL","blurb":"ShareGPT and PlatoLM for multi-turn conversation data, then comparing the stages: backtranslation links pretraining and SFT, and RL generalizes where SFT memorizes.","file":"lecture05_part10.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part10.jpg","duration":736.2,"first":146,"last":159,"slides":[{"n":146,"title":"Instruction tuning in multi-turn （Conversation）","t":0.8},{"n":147,"title":"An important Human-ChatGPT conversation data","t":24.42},{"n":148,"title":"Why ShareGPT is great ?","t":63.25},{"n":149,"title":"Our solution: PlatoLM","t":114.15},{"n":150,"title":"Why it is called “PlatoLM”","t":177.54},{"n":151,"title":"It ranks second in Alpaca-Eval https://tatsu-lab.github.io/alpaca_eval/","t":231.8},{"n":152,"title":"More insights on Pre-training, SFT, and RLHF Pre-training vs. SFT","t":283.98},{"n":153,"title":"Pretraining and SFT","t":302.82},{"n":154,"title":"Backtranslation：transform pre-training data to SFT","t":364.39},{"n":155,"title":"Backtranslation：transform pre-training data to SFT","t":433.62},{"n":156,"title":"More insights on Pre-training, SFT, and RLHF SFT vs. RLHF","t":494.73},{"n":157,"title":"SFT memorizes and RL generalizes","t":514.3},{"n":158,"title":"Comparison","t":592.12},{"n":159,"title":"Incentivizing it, do not teach","t":664.25}],"sents":[[0.8,5.62,146,"For open-source researchers, the obvious challenge was the data.","对开源研究者来说，明显的挑战是数据。"],[5.97,10.14,146,"OpenAI had human trainers writing and ranking conversations.","OpenAI 有人类训练师来撰写和排序对话。"],[10.49,16.43,146,"How do the rest of us get large amounts of good multi-turn conversation data for instruction tuning?","我们其他人怎样才能获得大量优质的多轮对话数据来做指令微调？"],[16.78,23.02,146,"Let's look at the most important dataset of that period, and our own answer to its limitations.","我们来看看那个时期最重要的数据集，以及我们针对其局限性给出的方案。"],[24.27,27.02,147,"The answer for a while was ShareGPT.","有一段时间，答案是 ShareGPT。"],[27.37,32.73,147,"It was a browser extension that let people share their ChatGPT conversations with one click.","它是一个浏览器插件，让人们一键分享自己与 ChatGPT 的对话。"],[33.08,39.57,147,"As you can see from the counter, thousands of conversations were being shared even in its early days.","从计数器可以看到，即使在早期，也已经有数千段对话被分享。"],[39.92,49.7,147,"For open-source researchers, this was gold: a large collection of real conversations between real users and ChatGPT, freely available on the web.","对开源研究者来说，这简直是金矿：大量真实用户与 ChatGPT 的真实对话，在网上免费可得。"],[50.05,54.99,147,"The famous Vicuna model, for example, was trained on ShareGPT conversations.","例如，著名的 Vicuna 模型就是用 ShareGPT 对话训练的。"],[55.34,58.98,147,"It was one of the strongest open chat models of its time.","它是当时最强的开源聊天模型之一。"],[59.33,61.85,147,"Let's see why this data was so good.","我们来看看这份数据为什么这么好。"],[63.1,65.6,148,"There are two reasons ShareGPT is great.","ShareGPT 好在两点。"],[65.95,69.79,148,"First, the user questions and instructions are real.","第一，用户的问题和指令是真实的。"],[70.14,76.07,148,"They're not written by annotators trying to imagine what users want; they're what people actually asked.","它们不是标注员揣摩用户需求写出来的，而是人们真正问过的问题。"],[76.42,80.32,148,"They come with all the variety and messiness of real usage.","带着真实使用中的各种多样性和杂乱性。"],[80.67,86.1,148,"Like the meaning of life conversation on the left, followed by Shouldn't the answer be forty-two?","比如左边那段关于人生意义的对话，用户接着问：“答案难道不该是 42 吗？”"],[86.45,91.45,148,"Second, people usually share a conversation because they liked ChatGPT's response.","第二，人们分享一段对话，通常是因为喜欢 ChatGPT 的回答。"],[91.8,99.34,148,"So the act of sharing works as an implicit positive label: it's a filtered set of good responses, for free.","所以分享这个动作本身就相当于一个隐式的正向标签：免费得到了一组经过筛选的好回答。"],[99.69,101.87,148,"But there's a catch, at the bottom.","但有个问题，在下方。"],[102.22,109.75,148,"ShareGPT stopped allowing downloads in April twenty twenty-three, so the amount of data available is limited, and it's not scalable.","ShareGPT 从 2023 年 4 月起不再允许下载，所以可用数据有限，无法扩展。"],[110.1,112.75,148,"If you want more, you need another approach.","如果想要更多数据，就需要别的办法。"],[114.0,119.11,149,"Here's our solution: PlatoLM. Let me compare three approaches in the figure.","这是我们的方案：PlatoLM。我来比较图中的三种做法。"],[119.46,125.39,149,"On the left, ShareGPT: real users talk to ChatGPT, and the data trains Vicuna.","左边是 ShareGPT：真实用户与 ChatGPT 对话，数据用来训练 Vicuna。"],[125.74,128.33,149,"Great quality, but limited quantity.","质量很好，但数量有限。"],[128.68,134.01,149,"In the middle, UltraChat: ChatGPT plays both the user and the assistant.","中间是 UltraChat：ChatGPT 同时扮演用户和助手。"],[134.36,138.38,149,"That scales to any size, and was used to train UltraLLaMA.","这可以扩展到任意规模，并被用来训练 UltraLLaMA。"],[138.73,145.25,149,"The problem is that ChatGPT pretending to be a user doesn't ask questions the way real people do.","问题在于，ChatGPT 假扮用户时，提问方式和真人不一样。"],[145.6,147.52,149,"On the right, our approach.","右边是我们的方法。"],[147.87,155.99,149,"Step one: take the real human questions from ShareGPT, and use them to train a user simulator, which we call Socratic.","第一步：用 ShareGPT 中真实的人类问题训练一个用户模拟器，我们称之为 Socratic。"],[156.34,163.37,149,"Step two: let Socratic chat with ChatGPT, generating a new, much larger dataset we call SocraticChat.","第二步：让 Socratic 和 ChatGPT 对话，生成一个规模大得多的新数据集，我们称之为 SocraticChat。"],[163.72,167.93,149,"Step three: train our model, PlatoLM, on that.","第三步：在此之上训练我们的模型 PlatoLM。"],[168.28,176.14,149,"So we keep the human-like questioning style of real users, but we can generate as much data as we want.","这样既保留了真实用户那种像人一样的提问风格，又能生成任意多的数据。"],[177.39,182.12,150,"Why the name PlatoLM? It comes from the Socratic method.","为什么叫 PlatoLM？名字来自苏格拉底式教学法。"],[182.47,185.39,150,"Socrates taught by repeatedly asking questions.","苏格拉底通过反复提问来教学。"],[185.74,186.89,150,"Look at the dialogue.","看这段对话。"],[187.24,191.14,150,"Do you know what virtue is? I think virtue is behaving rightly.","“你知道什么是美德吗？”“我认为美德就是行为正当。”"],[191.49,196.26,150,"Would a person with a good heart do harmful things to others? No.","“一个心地善良的人会伤害别人吗？”“不会。”"],[196.61,202.32,150,"Then is it virtuous when a country harms another for its own interests?","“那么，一个国家为了自身利益伤害另一个国家，算是美德吗？”"],[202.67,207.97,150,"And step by step, the student reaches a deeper answer than the one they started with.","就这样一步一步，学生得出了比一开始更深刻的答案。"],[208.32,216.14,150,"Plato was Socrates' student, and much of what we know about Socrates comes from Plato's written dialogues.","柏拉图是苏格拉底的学生，我们对苏格拉底的了解很多来自柏拉图写下的对话录。"],[216.49,224.49,150,"So our user simulator, which asks the questions, is Socratic, and the model that learns from those dialogues is Plato.","所以，负责提问的用户模拟器叫 Socratic，而从这些对话中学习的模型就是 Plato。"],[224.84,230.4,150,"The idea is that good questions drive learning, for people and for models.","理念是：好问题推动学习，对人和模型都一样。"],[231.65,233.1,151,"How well did it work?","效果如何？"],[233.45,236.76,151,"This is the AlpacaEval leaderboard from that time.","这是当时的 AlpacaEval 排行榜。"],[237.11,244.27,151,"It measures how often a model's responses are preferred over a reference model by an automatic judge.","它衡量的是，在自动评判者看来，一个模型的回答有多大比例优于参考模型。"],[244.62,251.13,151,"Find the red arrow: PlatoLM 7B, with a win rate of about eighty-two percent.","找到红色箭头：PlatoLM 7B，胜率约 82%。"],[251.48,252.65,151,"Look at its neighbors.","看看它周围的模型。"],[253.0,262.01,151,"It's close to Vicuna 13B, which was trained on real ShareGPT data and is almost twice the size, and just above GPT-3.5.","它与 Vicuna 13B 很接近，后者用真实 ShareGPT 数据训练、规模几乎是它的两倍；它还略高于 GPT-3.5。"],[262.36,266.9,151,"The main lesson isn't the leaderboard position, which changes every week.","主要的启示不在于排名，排行榜每周都在变。"],[267.25,278.63,151,"It's that a seven-billion-parameter model, trained on conversations driven by a learned user simulator, could match much larger models trained on real human data.","而在于：一个 70 亿参数的模型，用学习得到的用户模拟器驱动的对话来训练，就能比肩用真实人类数据训练的更大模型。"],[278.98,282.58,151,"Better questions in the data made a better assistant.","数据中更好的问题，造就了更好的助手。"],[283.83,290.79,152,"We've now walked through every stage of the pipeline: tokenization, pretraining, SFT and RLHF.","我们已经走完了整个流程的每个阶段：分词、预训练、SFT 和 RLHF。"],[291.14,293.13,152,"Let's step back and compare the stages.","我们退一步，比较一下这些阶段。"],[293.48,296.52,152,"First: pretraining versus SFT.","首先：预训练与 SFT。"],[296.87,301.42,152,"Are they really fundamentally different, or two versions of the same thing?","它们真的有本质区别吗，还是同一件事的两个版本？"],[302.67,304.31,153,"Let's put them side by side.","把它们放在一起比较。"],[304.66,307.91,153,"Pretraining uses plain corpora without structure.","预训练使用没有结构的纯语料。"],[308.26,310.55,153,"The loss is calculated on every token.","损失在每个 token 上计算。"],[310.9,319.18,153,"And it's task-independent: the model just learns language and knowledge in general, from very large amounts of data.","而且它与任务无关：模型从海量数据中学习一般性的语言和知识。"],[319.53,324.1,153,"SFT uses structured data: instruction, input and output.","SFT 使用结构化数据：指令、输入和输出。"],[324.45,332.05,153,"The loss is calculated only on the output, conditioned on the instruction and input, which is Tip two from earlier.","损失只在输出上计算，并以指令和输入为条件，这就是之前的技巧二。"],[332.4,336.16,153,"And it's task-specific: it teaches the model how to respond.","而且它是面向任务的：它教模型如何回应。"],[336.51,343.85,153,"SFT data can reach millions of examples today, but it's usually orders of magnitude smaller than pretraining data.","如今 SFT 数据可以达到数百万条，但通常仍比预训练数据小几个数量级。"],[344.2,349.88,153,"Notice that, mechanically, both are just next-token prediction with cross-entropy.","注意，从机制上讲，两者都只是用交叉熵做下一个 token 预测。"],[350.23,354.41,153,"The real differences are the data format, and which tokens get the loss.","真正的区别在于数据格式，以及哪些 token 参与计算损失。"],[354.76,362.99,153,"That observation suggests an interesting idea: what if we turn pretraining data into SFT format? That's the next slide.","这一观察引出了一个有趣的想法：如果把预训练数据转成 SFT 格式会怎样？这就是下一页的内容。"],[364.24,372.67,154,"This is from our HuatuoGPT-2 work on medical LLMs, and the idea is to transform pretraining data into SFT data.","这来自我们关于医疗大模型的 HuatuoGPT-2 工作，思路是把预训练数据转化为 SFT 数据。"],[373.02,374.26,154,"Look at the top path.","看上面这条路径。"],[374.61,384.59,154,"We start with about five point two five million medical documents in Chinese and English: books, web pages, encyclopedias and medical literature.","我们从约 525 万篇中英文医学文档开始：书籍、网页、百科和医学文献。"],[384.94,393.13,154,"Instead of pretraining on them as raw text, we use an LLM to unify each document into an instruction format.","我们不是把它们当原始文本来预训练，而是用大模型把每篇文档统一成指令格式。"],[393.48,397.73,154,"That is, a question and an answer grounded in that document.","也就是基于该文档的一个问题和一个答案。"],[398.08,402.81,154,"That gives us about five point two five million medical pretraining instructions.","这样我们得到约 525 万条医学预训练指令。"],[403.16,411.44,154,"The bottom path is regular SFT data: one hundred forty-two thousand real medical questions, with answers generated by GPT-4.","下面这条路径是常规的 SFT 数据：14.2 万个真实医学问题，答案由 GPT-4 生成。"],[411.79,419.9,154,"Then both are combined in a single one-stage adaptation training, instead of separate continued-pretraining and fine-tuning stages.","然后两者合并进行一次性的单阶段适配训练，而不是分开做继续预训练和微调。"],[420.25,424.58,154,"We call it backtranslation, by analogy with machine translation.","我们称之为“回译”，这是类比机器翻译的说法。"],[424.93,432.22,154,"We go from the answer, the document, back to a question that it answers. The next slide shows a real example.","我们从“答案”——也就是文档——反推出它所回答的问题。下一页展示一个真实例子。"],[433.47,436.84,155,"To make data unification concrete, look at this example.","为了让数据统一更具体，看这个例子。"],[437.19,442.81,155,"The raw data is a passage from an English medical textbook about Alzheimer's disease.","原始数据是英文医学教科书中关于阿尔茨海默病的一段话。"],[443.16,450.73,155,"It's one of the most common mental illnesses in assisted living facilities, and most patients are in their sixties or older.","它是辅助生活机构中最常见的精神疾病之一，大多数患者在六十岁及以上。"],[451.08,459.35,155,"The generated query, in Chinese, asks: what are the main clinical and pathological features of Alzheimer's disease?","生成的中文问题是：阿尔茨海默病的主要临床和病理特征是什么？"],[459.7,466.86,155,"And the generated answer, also in Chinese, restates the textbook content as a response to that question.","生成的答案同样是中文，把教科书的内容重述为对该问题的回答。"],[467.21,470.26,155,"Why is this better than pretraining on the raw text?","为什么这比直接在原始文本上预训练更好？"],[470.61,477.86,155,"Because the knowledge is now presented in the same question-answering form in which the model will later be asked to use it.","因为知识现在以问答形式呈现，与模型日后被要求使用这些知识的形式一致。"],[478.21,485.77,155,"As the slide says, learning becomes more knowledge-intensive: every training example is a piece of knowledge packaged as an answer.","正如幻灯片所说，学习变得更加知识密集：每个训练样例都是包装成答案的一条知识。"],[486.12,493.33,155,"It also neatly bridges the language gap, since English textbook knowledge becomes Chinese Q and A.","它还巧妙地跨越了语言鸿沟，因为英文教科书的知识变成了中文问答。"],[494.58,498.9,156,"Now the second comparison: SFT versus RLHF.","现在是第二组比较：SFT 与 RLHF。"],[499.25,502.95,156,"Both are post-training, but they learn in very different ways.","两者都属于后训练，但学习方式截然不同。"],[503.3,508.04,156,"One imitates demonstrations, and the other optimizes a reward.","一个模仿示范，另一个优化奖励。"],[508.39,512.9,156,"Which one generalizes better, and which should you rely on?","哪个泛化得更好？你又该依赖哪个？"],[514.15,523.66,157,"Here's a striking result from a two thousand twenty-five paper, titled exactly as the slide: SFT Memorizes, RL Generalizes.","这是一篇 2025 年论文中一个惊人的结果，论文标题就和这页一样：SFT Memorizes, RL Generalizes。"],[524.01,530.01,157,"The task is visual navigation in a real-world street environment called V-IRL.","任务是在一个名为 V-IRL 的真实街景环境中进行视觉导航。"],[530.36,535.18,157,"The x-axis is training compute, and the y-axis is success rate.","横轴是训练计算量，纵轴是成功率。"],[535.53,540.68,157,"Dashed lines are in-distribution, situations like those in training.","虚线是分布内，即与训练相似的情形。"],[541.03,546.11,157,"Solid lines are out-of-distribution, situations with changed rules or settings.","实线是分布外，即规则或设置发生变化的情形。"],[546.46,548.3,157,"Look at the dashed lines first.","先看虚线。"],[548.65,556.46,157,"Both SFT, in red, and RL, in blue, do well in-distribution, and SFT actually gets there faster.","红色的 SFT 和蓝色的 RL 在分布内都表现不错，而且 SFT 其实更快达到高水平。"],[556.81,558.28,157,"Now look at the solid lines.","再看实线。"],[558.63,567.11,157,"As SFT trains longer, its out-of-distribution success collapses to nearly zero. It has memorized the training situations.","随着 SFT 训练变长，它在分布外的成功率崩塌到接近零。它记住了训练中的情形。"],[567.46,572.73,157,"RL keeps improving out of distribution, up to around eighty-five percent.","RL 在分布外持续提升，最高达到约 85%。"],[573.08,583.25,157,"The intuition: SFT copies the exact answers it was shown, while RL learns which actions lead to success, which is more transferable.","直觉是：SFT 照搬它看到的确切答案，而 RL 学的是哪些行动能带来成功，这更容易迁移。"],[583.6,590.72,157,"That said, the authors also note SFT is still useful to get the model into the right output format before RL.","不过，作者也指出，在 RL 之前，SFT 仍有助于让模型掌握正确的输出格式。"],[591.97,596.45,158,"Let's summarize SFT versus RLHF along three dimensions.","我们从三个维度总结 SFT 与 RLHF 的对比。"],[596.8,600.87,158,"Complexity: SFT is much simpler than RLHF.","复杂度：SFT 比 RLHF 简单得多。"],[601.22,610.82,158,"SFT is one model and a standard loss; RLHF needs a reward model, a policy, a reference model, and a tricky RL algorithm.","SFT 只需一个模型和一个标准损失；RLHF 需要奖励模型、策略模型、参考模型，以及一个棘手的强化学习算法。"],[611.17,615.15,158,"Stability: RLHF is less stable than SFT.","稳定性：RLHF 不如 SFT 稳定。"],[615.5,622.02,158,"RL training can collapse, or the policy can exploit the reward model, so it needs careful tuning.","强化学习训练可能崩溃，或者策略会钻奖励模型的空子，所以需要仔细调参。"],[622.37,627.22,158,"Dependency on human prior, which is the most interesting one.","对人类先验的依赖，这是最有意思的一点。"],[627.57,634.16,158,"SFT gives step-by-step guidance: humans tell the model exactly what to write, token by token.","SFT 提供逐步指导：人类逐个 token 地告诉模型该写什么。"],[634.51,640.75,158,"Learning from human preferences only gives an outcome-level signal: this answer is better than that one.","从人类偏好中学习只提供结果层面的信号：这个答案比那个好。"],[641.1,650.86,158,"And DeepSeek-R1-Zero goes further, learning from rule-based rewards that just check whether the final outcome is correct, like whether a math answer matches.","而 DeepSeek-R1-Zero 走得更远，它从基于规则的奖励中学习，这些奖励只检查最终结果是否正确，比如数学答案是否匹配。"],[651.21,656.91,158,"So as we move down the list, we impose less human prior and let the model find its own way.","所以沿着列表往下，我们施加的人类先验越来越少，让模型自己找路。"],[657.26,662.85,158,"That connects nicely to the idea, from the start of today, that less structure scales better.","这与今天开头提到的“结构越少，扩展性越好”的思想很好地呼应。"],[664.1,669.23,159,"That leads to a philosophy I want you to remember: incentivize it, don't teach it.","这引出了一个我希望大家记住的理念：去激励它，而不是去教它。"],[669.58,674.59,159,"Imitation learning, which is SFT, gives the model human-written responses.","模仿学习，也就是 SFT，给模型的是人写的回答。"],[674.94,678.68,159,"Those responses can carry human biases and limitations.","这些回答可能带有人类的偏见和局限。"],[679.03,686.35,159,"And in deep learning, we've learned again and again that data-driven learning tends to beat hand-crafted human priors.","而在深度学习中，我们一次又一次地认识到，数据驱动的学习往往胜过人为设计的先验。"],[686.7,694.07,159,"The alternative is to incentivize the model through final rewards, such as rule-based rewards that check correctness.","另一种选择是通过最终奖励来激励模型，比如检查正确性的基于规则的奖励。"],[694.42,701.87,159,"Think of AlphaGo Zero, which learned Go without any human game records and surpassed every human player.","想想 AlphaGo Zero，它不用任何人类棋谱就学会了围棋，并超越了所有人类棋手。"],[702.22,710.68,159,"And DeepSeek-R1-Zero, which skipped SFT entirely and applied RL directly to the base model.","还有 DeepSeek-R1-Zero，它完全跳过 SFT，直接在基座模型上做强化学习。"],[711.03,714.54,159,"Learning from human records might never outperform humans.","从人类记录中学习，可能永远无法超越人类。"],[714.89,718.62,159,"Learning from verified outcomes can produce new patterns.","从可验证的结果中学习，则可能涌现出新的模式。"],[718.97,726.0,159,"R1-Zero, for example, spontaneously learned to re-check and reflect on its own reasoning.","例如，R1-Zero 自发地学会了复查和反思自己的推理。"],[726.35,734.32,159,"This is exactly where next lecture begins: reinforcement learning that learns from rewards, from RLHF to reasoning.","这正是下一讲的起点：从奖励中学习的强化学习，从 RLHF 一直到推理。"]]},{"n":11,"title":"Small LLMs, the Densing Law and the End of Scaling?","blurb":"Should we scale forever? Small models trained on synthetic data, the Densing Law, Ilya Sutskever on the end of pretraining, and what comes next.","file":"lecture05_part11.mp4","poster":"lecture05_part11.jpg","duration":534.1,"first":160,"last":169,"slides":[{"n":160,"title":"Small LLMs?","t":0.8},{"n":161,"title":"Scale up forever？","t":22.7},{"n":162,"title":"Interestingly, small language model becomes popular","t":85.39},{"n":163,"title":"Small Language models (Phi-4) using synthetic data","t":139.24},{"n":164,"title":"Densing Law","t":195.95},{"n":165,"title":"Final remarks","t":258.27},{"n":166,"title":"Ilya Sutskever says scaling (pretraining) will end","t":275.45},{"n":167,"title":"What should we do in the future?","t":328.58},{"n":168,"title":"Acknowledgement","t":391.87},{"n":169,"title":"Why does it Work?","t":465.89}],"sents":[[0.8,5.68,160,"We've covered how LLMs are trained, from tokens all the way to RL.","我们已经讲完了大模型是如何训练的，从 token 一直到强化学习。"],[6.03,10.64,160,"Before we wrap up, let's come back to the question of size one last time.","在结束之前，我们最后一次回到规模的问题。"],[10.99,14.74,160,"We spent the first half explaining why bigger is better.","前半部分我们一直在解释为什么越大越好。"],[15.09,21.3,160,"So should we just scale up forever? Or is there a case for small LLMs?","那我们是否应该永远扩大规模？还是说，小模型也有其价值？"],[22.55,25.58,161,"Can we scale up forever? There are two walls.","我们能永远扩大规模吗？有两堵墙。"],[25.93,28.09,161,"First, data is nearly over.","第一，数据快用完了。"],[28.44,32.15,161,"As Ilya Sutskever put it, we have but one internet.","正如 Ilya Sutskever 所说，我们只有一个互联网。"],[32.5,38.87,161,"High-quality human-written text is finite, and the frontier labs have already used most of it.","高质量的人类文本是有限的，前沿实验室已经用掉了其中大部分。"],[39.22,44.83,161,"Second, model scale is running into hardware limits, at least for deployment.","第二，模型规模正碰到硬件的极限，至少在部署上是这样。"],[45.18,51.47,161,"A single typical GPU server has eight GPUs with eighty gigabytes each, about six hundred forty gigabytes in total.","一台典型的 GPU 服务器有 8 张 GPU，每张 80GB，总共约 640GB。"],[51.82,56.23,161,"With INT8 quantization, each parameter takes one byte.","用 INT8 量化时，每个参数占一个字节。"],[56.58,64.61,161,"So the largest model you can fit on one server is several hundred billion parameters, roughly the seven hundred billion on the slide.","所以一台服务器能放下的最大模型是几千亿参数，大致就是幻灯片上的 7000 亿。"],[64.96,68.5,161,"And that's before leaving room for activations and the KV cache.","而且这还没给激活值和 KV 缓存留空间。"],[68.85,74.71,161,"Going bigger means splitting a model across machines, which is slower and much more expensive to serve.","再大就得把模型拆到多台机器上，这样推理服务更慢、成本也高得多。"],[75.06,82.43,161,"So the focus is shifting from the scaling law to what's called the densing law: getting more capability out of each parameter.","因此关注点正从规模定律转向所谓的密度定律：让每个参数发挥出更多能力。"],[82.78,83.99,161,"Let's look at that.","我们来看看。"],[85.24,88.9,162,"Interestingly, small language models have become popular again.","有意思的是，小语言模型又流行起来了。"],[89.25,90.08,162,"Look at the list.","看这个列表。"],[90.43,97.59,162,"TinyLlama at one point one billion parameters, and MobileVLM at one point four and two point seven billion.","TinyLlama 有 11 亿参数，MobileVLM 有 14 亿和 27 亿两个版本。"],[97.94,104.78,162,"MobiLlama at zero point five billion, and MobileLLM at just zero point one and zero point three billion.","MobiLlama 有 5 亿，MobileLLM 只有 1 亿和 3 亿。"],[105.13,112.41,162,"Several of these names have mobile in them, and that's the point: they're designed to run on phones and other edge devices.","其中好几个名字都带有 mobile，这正是重点：它们是为在手机和其他边缘设备上运行而设计的。"],[112.76,114.24,162,"Why does that matter?","这为什么重要？"],[114.59,120.67,162,"Privacy, since your data never leaves your device. Latency, since there's no round trip to a server.","隐私：你的数据不会离开设备。延迟：不需要往返服务器。"],[121.02,127.01,162,"Cost, since there are no API fees. And availability, since it works offline.","成本：没有 API 费用。可用性：离线也能用。"],[127.36,132.69,162,"Remember the slide about how large keeps changing meaning? It works in the other direction too.","还记得那页讲“大”的含义不断变化的幻灯片吗？反过来也一样。"],[133.04,137.84,162,"Today's small models are far more capable than the large models of a few years ago.","今天的小模型远比几年前的大模型能干。"],[139.09,145.62,163,"Here's a great example of a small but mighty model: Phi-4 from Microsoft, which we met in Tip eight.","这是一个小而强的模型的绝佳例子：微软的 Phi-4，我们在技巧八中见过它。"],[145.97,150.09,163,"The plot shows MMLU score against the number of active parameters.","这张图展示的是 MMLU 分数与激活参数量的关系。"],[150.44,157.68,163,"On the far right are big models like Llama 3.3 70B and Qwen 2.5 72B.","最右边是大模型，比如 Llama 3.3 70B 和 Qwen 2.5 72B。"],[158.03,162.75,163,"Phi-4, at about fourteen billion parameters, scores close to them.","Phi-4 约 140 亿参数，得分却和它们很接近。"],[163.1,170.36,163,"And it's clearly above other models of similar size, like Qwen 2.5 14B.","而且明显高于同等规模的其他模型，比如 Qwen 2.5 14B。"],[170.71,174.81,163,"The green arrow marks the frontier for small but mighty models.","绿色箭头标出了小而强模型的前沿。"],[175.16,177.72,163,"How did they do it? Largely with data.","他们是怎么做到的？主要靠数据。"],[178.07,184.29,163,"Remember the pretraining mix, where forty percent of the training came from carefully designed synthetic data.","还记得那个预训练配比吗？40% 的训练来自精心设计的合成数据。"],[184.64,190.23,163,"When your data is like a well-written textbook, you need fewer parameters to learn from it.","当你的数据像一本写得很好的教科书时，学习它所需的参数就更少。"],[190.58,194.55,163,"Data quality can substitute for model size, at least partly.","数据质量至少可以部分地替代模型规模。"],[195.8,200.87,164,"This trend has been formalized as the densing law, from researchers at Tsinghua.","这一趋势被清华的研究者总结为“密度定律”。"],[201.22,209.44,164,"The idea is capability density: roughly, how much capability a model achieves relative to its number of parameters.","核心概念是能力密度：粗略地说，就是模型相对其参数量所达到的能力。"],[209.79,222.13,164,"They estimated it for many open-source base models released over time, from Llama-1 in early twenty twenty-three to MiniCPM-3 in late twenty twenty-four.","他们估算了不同时间发布的许多开源基座模型的能力密度，从 2023 年初的 Llama-1 到 2024 年底的 MiniCPM-3。"],[222.48,226.3,164,"Each bubble is a model, and bigger bubbles are bigger models.","每个气泡是一个模型，气泡越大，模型越大。"],[226.65,230.18,164,"The red dashed line is the trend of the maximum density.","红色虚线是最大密度的趋势线。"],[230.53,234.64,164,"It's a straight line on a log scale, which means exponential growth.","它在对数坐标下是一条直线，意味着指数增长。"],[234.99,240.92,164,"Their estimate: the maximum capability density doubles about every three point three months.","他们的估计是：最大能力密度大约每 3.3 个月翻一番。"],[241.27,247.64,164,"In practice, that means that every few months, you can get the same capability with roughly half the parameters.","实际上这意味着，每过几个月，就能用大约一半的参数获得同样的能力。"],[247.99,251.93,164,"So be denser: better performance with fewer parameters.","所以要更“密”：用更少的参数获得更好的性能。"],[252.28,256.87,164,"That's great news for anyone without a giant GPU cluster, which is most of us.","这对没有巨型 GPU 集群的人来说是个好消息，而我们大多数人都属于这一类。"],[258.12,264.37,165,"That closes the small-LLM story: denser models are one answer to the limits of scale.","小模型的故事就讲到这里：更“密”的模型是应对规模极限的一种答案。"],[264.72,267.0,165,"Let me finish with some final remarks.","最后我来做一些总结性的评论。"],[267.35,274.05,165,"Where is this all heading, and what should you, as researchers and engineers, focus on?","这一切将走向何方？作为研究者和工程师，你们应该关注什么？"],[275.3,279.84,166,"This photo captures a moment many people consider a turning point.","这张照片记录了一个被许多人视为转折点的时刻。"],[280.19,292.23,166,"At NeurIPS twenty twenty-four, Ilya Sutskever, co-founder of OpenAI and one of the people most associated with scaling, said: pre-training as we know it will end.","在 NeurIPS 2024 上，OpenAI 联合创始人、与规模化关联最紧密的人物之一 Ilya Sutskever 说：我们所熟知的预训练将会终结。"],[292.58,293.67,166,"Read his slide.","看他的幻灯片。"],[294.02,298.89,166,"Compute is growing: better hardware, better algorithms, larger clusters.","算力在增长：更好的硬件、更好的算法、更大的集群。"],[299.24,302.22,166,"But data is not growing: we have but one internet.","但数据没有增长：我们只有一个互联网。"],[302.57,309.08,166,"He called data the fossil fuel of AI. It was created once, by humanity, and we're using it up.","他把数据称作 AI 的化石燃料。它由人类一次性创造出来，而我们正在把它用光。"],[309.43,314.14,166,"Coming from someone who championed scaling, that's significant.","这话出自一位规模化的倡导者之口，意义重大。"],[314.49,316.48,166,"It doesn't mean progress stops.","这并不意味着进步会停止。"],[316.83,324.71,166,"It means the next gains have to come from somewhere other than simply pretraining bigger models on more internet text.","它意味着下一波收益必须来自别处，而不是简单地用更多互联网文本预训练更大的模型。"],[325.06,327.18,166,"The next slide lists where.","下一页列出了方向。"],[328.43,332.72,167,"So what should we do in the future? Here are four directions.","那么未来我们该做什么？这里有四个方向。"],[333.07,334.88,167,"First, find a new scaling law.","第一，找到新的规模定律。"],[335.23,342.17,167,"One is test-time scaling: letting models think longer with more reasoning tokens, as DeepSeek-R1 does.","一种是测试时扩展：让模型用更多推理 token 思考得更久，就像 DeepSeek-R1 那样。"],[342.52,349.18,167,"Another is scaling environments and interaction: models learning from acting in the world, not just from static text.","另一种是扩展环境与交互：模型通过在世界中行动来学习，而不只是从静态文本中学习。"],[349.53,355.97,167,"Second, agents: using tools to extend the model's abilities beyond what's stored in its weights.","第二，智能体：利用工具，把模型的能力扩展到权重中存储的知识之外。"],[356.32,361.5,167,"Third, go for denser models: achieving a given accuracy with smaller models.","第三，追求更“密”的模型：用更小的模型达到给定的准确率。"],[361.85,365.64,167,"And fourth, applications, the last mile.","第四，应用，也就是最后一公里。"],[365.99,372.93,167,"Use LLMs on your own problems, in medicine, math, education, science and engineering.","把大模型用在你自己的问题上，比如医学、数学、教育、科学和工程。"],[373.28,383.54,167,"And improve how humans interact with LLMs and agents, maybe one day through brain-machine interfaces or VR and AR.","并改进人与大模型及智能体的交互方式，也许有一天会通过脑机接口或 VR、AR 来实现。"],[383.89,390.47,167,"Every one of these is a good direction for your final project, and we'll cover most of them in the coming lectures.","每一个都是你期末项目的好方向，我们也会在接下来的课程中讲到其中大部分。"],[391.72,395.03,168,"These are the courses and talks I borrowed material from.","这些是我借鉴过材料的课程和讲座。"],[395.38,404.25,168,"I recommend all of them if you want to go deeper, especially Stanford's CS224N and Danqi Chen's Princeton course on understanding large language models.","如果想深入学习，我推荐所有这些资源，尤其是斯坦福的 CS224N 和陈丹琦在普林斯顿开设的理解大语言模型课程。"],[404.6,405.92,168,"Let me wrap up today.","我来总结一下今天的内容。"],[406.27,409.82,168,"We saw that an LLM is not just a bigger language model.","我们看到，大模型不只是一个更大的语言模型。"],[410.17,419.58,168,"Scale brings emergent abilities like in-context learning and instruction following, driven by scalable architectures, objectives and data.","规模带来了上下文学习、指令遵循等涌现能力，背后的驱动力是可扩展的架构、目标和数据。"],[419.93,425.83,168,"We followed ChatGPT's path from GPT-3 through SFT and RLHF.","我们沿着 ChatGPT 的路径，从 GPT-3 一路经过 SFT 和 RLHF。"],[426.18,432.5,168,"And we saw the ways you can use LLMs, from prompting and agents to training your own.","我们也看到了使用大模型的各种方式，从提示和智能体到训练你自己的模型。"],[432.85,444.12,168,"Then we went through the training pipeline: tokenization, pretraining with careful data engineering, SFT with good instructions, and RLHF to align with human preferences.","然后我们过了一遍训练流程：分词、精心做数据工程的预训练、用好指令做 SFT，以及用 RLHF 对齐人类偏好。"],[444.47,454.31,168,"And we ended with a shift in direction: data is running out, models are getting denser, and the next gains come from reasoning, interaction and RL.","最后我们看到了方向上的转变：数据正在耗尽，模型越来越“密”，下一波收益将来自推理、交互和强化学习。"],[454.66,461.18,168,"Next lecture, Lecture six, picks up right there: reinforcement learning for LLM post-training, from alignment to reasoning.","下一讲，也就是第六讲，就从这里接着讲：用于大模型后训练的强化学习，从对齐到推理。"],[461.53,464.49,168,"Before then, please try the OpenClaw homework.","在那之前，请大家试一试 OpenClaw 作业。"],[465.74,469.91,169,"One bonus slide before we finish: why does any of this work?","结束前再加一页彩蛋：这一切为什么会奏效？"],[470.26,472.36,169,"Honestly, we don't fully know.","说实话，我们并不完全知道。"],[472.71,477.54,169,"Look at the left: a model with around one hundred billion parameters.","看左边：一个大约有 1000 亿参数的模型。"],[477.89,483.66,169,"We know how to adjust those parameters to make it better at prediction, and we can measure that it works.","我们知道如何调整这些参数让它预测得更好，也能测量出它确实有效。"],[484.01,491.35,169,"But we don't really understand how billions of parameters collaborate to produce the behavior we see.","但我们并不真正理解数十亿个参数是如何协作产生我们看到的行为的。"],[491.7,496.72,169,"They do seem to build some kind of knowledge database, but a strange and imperfect one.","它们似乎确实建立了某种知识库，但这个知识库奇怪而不完美。"],[497.07,499.51,169,"The famous example is the reversal curse.","著名的例子是“反转诅咒”。"],[499.86,505.48,169,"Ask Who is Tom Cruise's mother, and the model correctly says Mary Lee Pfeiffer.","问“汤姆·克鲁斯的母亲是谁？”，模型正确地回答 Mary Lee Pfeiffer。"],[505.83,510.48,169,"Ask Who is Mary Lee Pfeiffer's son, and it may say it doesn't know.","问“Mary Lee Pfeiffer 的儿子是谁？”，它可能说不知道。"],[510.83,513.63,169,"The same fact, stored in only one direction.","同一个事实，却只朝一个方向存储。"],[513.98,523.95,169,"So the advice at the bottom is good: treat LLMs as largely inscrutable artifacts, and develop correspondingly sophisticated evaluations.","所以底部的建议很好：把大模型基本当作难以看透的人造物，并发展出相应精细的评测方法。"],[524.3,530.17,169,"Understanding them better is one of the big open problems, and maybe one of you will help solve it.","更好地理解它们是重大的开放问题之一，也许你们中的某一位会帮助解决它。"],[530.52,532.28,169,"Thank you, and see you next time!","谢谢大家，我们下次见！"]]}]};
